Output~2025-04-24 16:31:52.799078: [RequestOutput(request_id=7, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Write a short story in third person narration about a protagonist who has to make an important career decision. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 9842, 264, 2875, 3446, 304, 4948, 1732, 86180, 922, 264, 46684, 889, 706, 311, 1304, 459, 3062, 7076, 5597, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='As she sat in her small apartment, staring blankly at the city skyline outside her window, Emily felt the weight of her decision bearing down on her. She had been working as a graphic designer at a small firm for five years, and while she loved the creative freedom and camaraderie with her colleagues, she couldn\'t shake the feeling that it was time for a change.\n\nThe problem was, Emily had no idea what that change should be. She had always been passionate about design, but as she approached her mid-twenties, she was starting to feel restless. Her friends were all making big moves - one had just landed a job at a prestigious advertising agency, another was starting her own business, and a third was pursuing a graduate degree. Emily, on the other hand, was stuck in a rut, feeling like she was just going through the motions.\n\nAs she pondered her future, Emily\'s mind wandered back to her childhood dreams. She had always loved art and music, and had even considered pursuing a career in fine art before deciding on design. But now, as she looked around her cluttered apartment, filled with design books and half-finished projects, she wondered if she had made a mistake.\n\nJust as Emily was starting to feel overwhelmed, her phone buzzed with a text from her best friend, Rachel. "Hey, girl, what\'s going on? You\'ve been MIA for weeks. Want to grab coffee and catch up?" Emily hesitated for a moment before responding. She really needed to talk to someone about this.\n\nOver coffee, Rachel listened intently as Emily poured out her frustrations and doubts. Rachel, who had recently started her own business, offered words of encouragement and advice. "You\'re not stuck, Emily. You\'re just at a crossroads. Sometimes you need to take a step back and re-evaluate what\'s important to you."\n\nEmily left the coffee shop feeling a sense of clarity wash over her. She realized that she didn\'t have to have all the answers right now. She could take her time, explore different options, and trust that the right path would reveal itself. With a newfound sense of purpose, Emily returned to her apartment and began to brainstorm. She started making lists of her strengths and weaknesses, her passions and interests. And as she did, a spark of excitement began to grow within her.\n\nOver the next few weeks, Emily started taking small steps towards her new direction. She began taking art classes, exploring different mediums and techniques. She started freelancing on the side,', token_ids=[2170, 1364, 7731, 304, 1077, 2678, 13455, 11, 37874, 10321, 398, 520, 279, 3363, 88839, 4994, 1077, 3321, 11, 35266, 6612, 279, 4785, 315, 1077, 5597, 18534, 1523, 389, 1077, 13, 3005, 1047, 1027, 3318, 439, 264, 21154, 15034, 520, 264, 2678, 7626, 369, 4330, 1667, 11, 323, 1418, 1364, 10456, 279, 11782, 11542, 323, 97686, 1013, 648, 449, 1077, 18105, 11, 1364, 7846, 956, 27116, 279, 8430, 430, 433, 574, 892, 369, 264, 2349, 382, 791, 3575, 574, 11, 35266, 1047, 912, 4623, 1148, 430, 2349, 1288, 387, 13, 3005, 1047, 2744, 1027, 25429, 922, 2955, 11, 719, 439, 1364, 2