Output~2025-04-24 16:32:13.111128: [RequestOutput(request_id=15, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Describe the function of a computer motherboard ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 61885, 279, 734, 315, 264, 6500, 65343, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="The computer motherboard is the main circuit board of a computer that connects all the hardware components together. It serves as the backbone of the system, allowing all the different parts to communicate with each other and function as a cohesive unit.\n\nThe motherboard performs several critical functions, including:\n\n1. **Connecting hardware components**: The motherboard provides connectors and sockets for installing and connecting various hardware components such as the central processing unit (CPU), memory (RAM), storage devices (hard drives or solid-state drives), graphics cards, sound cards, and network cards.\n2. **Routing data and power**: The motherboard acts as a communication highway, transmitting data and power signals between the various components. It routes data between the CPU, memory, and storage devices, and provides power to the components that require it.\n3. **Providing a platform for expansion**: The motherboard provides a platform for adding additional components, such as expansion cards, to enhance the computer's capabilities. This allows users to upgrade or customize their system to meet specific needs.\n4. **Managing power supply**: The motherboard regulates the power supply to the components, ensuring that each device receives the correct voltage and current.\n5. **Providing a BIOS or UEFI firmware**: The motherboard contains a basic input/output system (BIOS) or unified extensible firmware interface (UEFI) that allows users to configure the system settings, such as boot order, fan settings, and hardware settings.\n6. **Supporting peripherals**: The motherboard provides connectors and interfaces for connecting peripherals such as keyboards, mice, and monitors.\n\nIn summary, the motherboard is a critical component of a computer system, enabling the various hardware components to work together seamlessly and providing a platform for expansion and customization.", token_ids=[791, 6500, 65343, 374, 279, 1925, 16622, 4580, 315, 264, 6500, 430, 34161, 682, 279, 12035, 6956, 3871, 13, 1102, 17482, 439, 279, 56527, 315, 279, 1887, 11, 10923, 682, 279, 2204, 5596, 311, 19570, 449, 1855, 1023, 323, 734, 439, 264, 87516, 5089, 382, 791, 65343, 27772, 3892, 9200, 5865, 11, 2737, 1473, 16, 13, 3146, 64024, 12035, 6956, 96618, 578, 65343, 5825, 58170, 323, 48657, 369, 27730, 323, 21583, 5370, 12035, 6956, 1778, 439, 279, 8792, 8863, 5089, 320, 32715, 705, 5044, 320, 35005, 705, 5942, 7766, 320, 19221, 20722, 477, 6573, 21395, 20722, 705, 14515, 7563, 11, 5222, 7563, 11, 323, 4009, 7563, 627, 17, 13, 3146, 25730, 828, 323, 2410, 96618, 578, 65343, 14385, 439, 264, 10758, 27834, 11, 78768, 828, 323, 2410, 17738, 1990, 279, 5370, 6956, 13, 1102, 11543, 828, 1990, 279, 14266, 11, 5044, 11, 323, 5942, 7766, 11, 323, 5825, 2410, 311, 279, 6956, 430, 1397, 433, 627, 18, 13, 3146, 36919, 287, 264, 5452, 369, 14800, 96618, 578, 65343, 5825, 264, 5452, 369, 7999, 5217, 6956, 11, 1778, 439, 14800, 7563, 11, 311, 18885, 279, 6500, 596, 17357, 13, 1115, 6276, 3932, 311, 14234, 477, 32187, 872, 1887, 311, 3449, 3230, 3966, 627, 19, 13, 3146, 99729, 2410, 8312, 96618, 578, 65343, 80412, 279, 2410, 8312, 311, 279, 6956, 11, 23391, 430, 1855, 3756, 21879, 