ion**: The Cuban Missile Crisis was a crisis in the Caribbean, while the Vietnam War was fought in Southeast Asia.\n2. **Duration**: The Cuban Missile Crisis lasted for 13 days, while the Vietnam War lasted for nearly 20 years.\n3. **Military involvement**: The United States was directly involved in the Vietnam War, with over 2.5 million troops deployed, while in the Cuban Missile Crisis, the United States did not deploy troops, instead, it imposed a naval quarantine on Cuba.\n4. **Objectives**: The primary objective of the Cuban Missile Crisis was to prevent the Soviet Union from establishing a nuclear-armed missile base in Cuba, while the primary objective of the Vietnam War was to prevent the spread of communism in Southeast Asia.\n5. **International response**: The Cuban Missile Crisis brought the world to the brink of nuclear war, with the United Nations playing a key role in mediating the crisis. In contrast, the Vietnam War was not a global conflict, and the United Nations did not play a significant role in resolving the conflict.\n6. **Domestic impact**: The Cuban Missile Crisis had a significant impact on domestic politics in the United States, with President John F. Kennedy's handling of the crisis contributing to his popularity. The Vietnam War, on the other hand, was highly divisive, with many Americans opposing the war and protesting against it.\n\nIn conclusion, while both the Cuban Missile Crisis and the Vietnam War were", token_ids=[791, 44810, 68870, 46250, 323, 279, 23315, 5111, 1051, 1403, 5199, 26885, 304, 6617, 3925, 430, 4430, 1063, 43874, 11, 719, 1101, 617, 12742, 12062, 13, 5810, 596, 264, 12593, 315, 279, 1403, 1473, 334, 35502, 1385, 25, 57277, 16, 13, 3146, 77518, 5111, 2317, 96618, 11995, 26885, 10222, 2391, 279, 24062, 5111, 11639, 11, 264, 892, 315, 19428, 61022, 1990, 279, 3723, 4273, 323, 279, 19953, 9323, 13, 578, 44810, 68870, 46250, 320, 5162, 17, 8, 323, 279, 23315, 5111, 320, 6280, 20, 12, 4468, 20, 8, 1051, 2225, 28160, 555, 27