Output~2025-04-24 16:33:43.671207: [RequestOutput(request_id=53, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Calculate the total surface area of a cube with a side length of 5 cm. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 21157, 279, 2860, 7479, 3158, 315, 264, 24671, 449, 264, 3185, 3160, 315, 220, 20, 10166, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='To calculate the total surface area of a cube with a side length of 5 cm, we need to find the area of each face and then add them up.\n\nThe formula to find the area of a square (which is the face of a cube) is:\n\nArea = side × side\n\nSince all sides of a cube are equal, we can use the side length of 5 cm for all sides.\n\nThe cube has 6 faces: top, bottom, left, right, front, and back. Each face is a square with a side length of 5 cm.\n\nSo, the area of each face is:\n\nArea = 5 cm × 5 cm = 25 square cm\n\nSince there are 6 faces, the total surface area is:\n\nTotal Surface Area = 6 × 25 square cm = 150 square cm\n\nTherefore, the total surface area of the cube with a side length of 5 cm is 150 square cm.', token_ids=[1271, 11294, 279, 2860, 7479, 3158, 315, 264, 24671, 449, 264, 3185, 3160, 315, 220, 20, 10166, 11, 584, 1205, 311, 1505, 279, 3158, 315, 1855, 3663, 323, 1243, 923, 1124, 709, 382, 791, 15150, 311, 1505, 279, 3158, 315, 264, 9518, 320, 8370, 374, 279, 3663, 315, 264, 24671, 8, 374, 1473, 8900, 284, 3185, 25800, 3185, 271, 12834, 682, 11314, 315, 264, 24671, 527, 6273, 11, 584, 649, 1005, 279, 3185, 3160