Output~2025-04-24 16:34:32.788252: [RequestOutput(request_id=82, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Generate a list of methods to reduce food waste. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 20400, 264, 1160, 315, 5528, 311, 8108, 3691, 12571, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here is a list of methods to reduce food waste:\n\n1. **Meal planning**: Plan your meals for the week, and make a grocery list accordingly. This will help you avoid buying too much food that may go to waste.\n\n2. **Shop your fridge and pantry first**: Before going grocery shopping, take stock of what you already have at home and plan your meals around those ingredients.\n\n3. **Use up leftovers**: Plan to use leftovers in creative ways, such as turning last night\'s dinner into tomorrow\'s lunch or using leftover vegetables in a soup or stir-fry.\n\n4. **Store food properly**: Make sure to store food in airtight containers and keep your fridge and pantry organized to help you keep track of what you have and what\'s about to expire.\n\n5. **Freeze it**: Freeze food that\'s approaching its expiration date, such as meat, bread, and vegetables, to use later.\n\n6. **Compost**: Compost food scraps, such as fruit and vegetable peels, to reduce the amount of waste that ends up in landfills.\n\n7. **Shop in bulk**: Buying in bulk can help reduce packaging waste and save you money, but make sure you have a plan to use the food before it expires.\n\n8. **Use up food before it expires**: Make a point to use up food before it expires, especially perishable items like dairy products and meat.\n\n9. **Avoid overbuying**: Avoid buying too much food, especially if you know you won\'t be able to use it before it expires.\n\n10. **Donate extra food**: Consider donating extra food to a local food bank or soup kitchen to help reduce food waste and support those in need.\n\n11. **Use up food scraps in creative ways**: Get creative with food scraps by using them to make broth, stock, or even compost tea.\n\n12. **Keep track of expiration dates**: Keep track of expiration dates and plan your meals around the food that\'s approaching its expiration date.\n\n13. **Use up food in soups and stews**: Use up food scraps by adding them to soups and stews, which can be a great way to reduce waste and create a nutritious meal.\n\n14. **Make a "use-up" meal**: Plan a meal specifically to use up food that\'s approaching its expiration date, such as a "use-up" stir-fry or soup.\n\n15. **Avoid food packaging waste**: Avoid buying food with excessive packaging, such as single-serving snacks or individually wrapped items, to reduce waste.\n\nBy', token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 1160, 315, 5528, 311, 8108, 3691, 12571, 1473, 16, 13, 3146, 81668, 9293, 96618, 9878, 701, 21644, 369, 279, 2046, 11, 323, 1304, 264, 30687, 1160, 28178, 13, 1115, 690, 1520, 499, 5766, 12096, 2288, 1790, 3691, 430, 1253, 733, 311, 12571, 382, 17, 13, 3146, 20381, 701, 38681, 323, 69357, 1176, 96618, 13538, 2133, 30687, 12185, 11, 1935, 5708, 315, 1148, 499, 2736, 617, 520, 2162, 323, 3197, 701, 21644, 2212, 1884, 14293, 382, 18, 13, 3146, 10464, 709, 93267, 96618, 9878, 311, 1005, 93267, 304, 11782, 5627, 11, 1778, 439, 13353, 1566, 3814, 596, 14177, 1139, 16986, 596, 16163, 477, 1701, 65543, 24822, 304, 264, 19724, 477, 23935, 2269, 894, 382, 19, 13, 3146, 6221, 3691, 10489, 96618, 7557, 2771, 311, 3637, 3691, 304, 264, 2154, 492, 24794, 323, 2567, 701, 38681, 323, 69357, 17057, 311, 1520, 499, 2567, 383