Output~2025-04-24 16:36:18.590178: [RequestOutput(request_id=151, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Given two strings, check whether one string is a rotation of another? ### Input: s1 = ‘waterbottle’\\ns2 = ‘erbottlewat’ ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 11, 35526, 449, 459, 1988, 430, 5825, 4726, 2317, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 16644, 1403, 9246, 11, 1817, 3508, 832, 925, 374, 264, 12984, 315, 2500, 30, 17010, 5688, 25, 274, 16, 284, 3451, 13284, 65, 63218, 529, 59, 4511, 17, 284, 3451, 41599, 63218, 59147, 529, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="A nice problem!\n\nTo check if one string is a rotation of another, we can concatenate the first string with itself and then check if the second string is a substring of the concatenated string.\n\nHere's the Python code to do that:\n```python\ndef is_rotation(s1, s2):\n    return s2 in s1 + s1\n\ns1 = 'waterbottle'\ns2 = 'erbottlewat'\nprint(is_rotation(s1, s2))  # Output: True\n```\nIn this code, we define a function `is_rotation` that takes two strings `s1` and `s2` as input. We concatenate `s1` with itself using the `+` operator, which creates a new string that is twice the length of `s1`. Then, we check if `s2` is a substring of the concatenated string using the `in` operator. If `s2` is a substring, it means that `s2` is a rotation of `s1`, and we return `True`. Otherwise, we return `False`.\n\nIn the example, we call the `is_rotation` function with `s1 = 'waterbottle'` and `s2 = 'erbottlewat'`, and the output is `True`, indicating that `s2` is indeed a rotation of `s1`.", token_ids=[32, 6555, 3575, 2268, 1271, 1817, 422, 832, 925, 374, 264, 12984, 315, 2500, 11, 584, 649, 78884, 279, 1176, 925, 449, 5196, 323, 1243, 1817, 422, 279, 2132, 925, 374, 264, 39549, 315, 279, 98634, 925, 382, 8586, 596, 279, 13325, 2082, 311, 656, 430, 512, 74694, 12958, 198, 755, 374, 45913, 1161, 16, 11, 274, 17, 997, 262, 471, 274, 17, 304, 274, 16, 489, 274, 16, 271, 82, 16, 284, 364, 13284, 65, 63218, 1270, 82, 17, 284, 364, 41599, 63218, 59147, 1270, 1374, 9820, 45913, 1161, 16, 11, 274, 17, 595, 220, 674, 9442, 25, 3082, 198, 14196, 4077, 644, 420, 2082, 11, 584, 7124, 264, 734, 1595, 285, 45913, 63, 430, 5097, 1403, 9246, 1595, 82, 16, 63, 323, 1595, 82, 17, 63, 439, 1988, 13, 1226, 78884, 1595, 82, 16, 63, 449, 5196, 1701, 279, 1595, 10, 63, 5793, 11, 902, 11705, 264, 502, 925, 430, 374, 11157, 279, 3160, 315, 1595, 82, 16, 29687, 5112, 11, 584, 1817, 422, 1595, 82, 17, 63, 374, 264, 39549, 315, 279, 98634, 925, 1701, 279, 1595, 258, 63, 5793, 13, 1442, 1595, 82, 17, 63, 374, 264, 39549, 11, 433, 3445, 430, 1595, 82, 17, 63, 374, 264, 12984, 315, 1595, 82, 16, 7964, 323, 584, 471, 1595, 2575, 29687, 18715, 11, 584, 471, 1595, 4139, 63438, 644, 279, 3187, 11, 584, 1650, 279, 1595, 285, 45913, 63, 734, 449, 1595, 82, 16, 284, 364, 13284, 65, 63218, 6, 63, 323, 1595, 82, 17, 284, 364, 41599, 63218, 59147, 6, 7964, 323, 279, 2612, 374, 1595, 2575, 7964, 19392, 430, 1595, 82, 17, 63, 374, 13118, 264, 12984, 315, 1595, 82, 16, 29687, 128009], cumulative_logprob=None, logprobs=None, finish_reason=stop, stop_reason=None)], finished=True, metrics=None, lora_request=None, num_cached_tokens=None, multi_modal_placeholders={})]
