Output~2025-04-24 16:36:29.530856: [RequestOutput(request_id=154, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Given a binary tree, check if it is a binary search tree. Write a Java function to do it. Assume the Node class is implemented. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 16644, 264, 8026, 5021, 11, 1817, 422, 433, 374, 264, 8026, 2778, 5021, 13, 9842, 264, 8102, 734, 311, 656, 433, 13, 63297, 279, 6146, 538, 374, 11798, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="Here is a Java function that checks if a given binary tree is a binary search tree (BST):\n\n```java\npublic class Solution {\n    public boolean isValidBST(Node root) {\n        return isValidBST(root, Long.MIN_VALUE, Long.MAX_VALUE);\n    }\n\n    public boolean isValidBST(Node root, long min, long max) {\n        if (root == null) {\n            return true;\n        }\n        if (root.val <= min || root.val >= max) {\n            return false;\n        }\n        return isValidBST(root.left, min, root.val) && isValidBST(root.right, root.val, max);\n    }\n}\n```\n\nIn this function, we use a helper function `isValidBST` that takes three parameters: the current node, the minimum value that the node's value can be, and the maximum value that the node's value can be. \n\nIf the current node is null, it means we have reached the end of the tree, so we return true. \n\nIf the current node's value is less than or equal to the minimum value or greater than or equal to the maximum value, it means the tree is not a BST, so we return false. \n\nIf the current node's value is within the valid range, we recursively call `isValidBST` on the left and right subtrees, updating the valid range for each subtree. \n\nThe main function `isValidBST` calls the helper function with the root node and the initial valid range as (Long.MIN_VALUE, Long.MAX_VALUE).", token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 8102, 734, 430, 12621, 422, 264, 2728, 8026, 5021, 374, 264, 8026, 2778, 5021, 320, 62106, 7887, 74694, 10248, 198, 898, 538, 12761, 341, 262, 586, 2777, 27263, 62106, 22853, 3789, 8, 341, 286, 471, 27263, 62106, 9387, 11, 5843, 38570, 7628, 11, 5843, 17006, 7628, 317, 262, 557, 262, 586, 2777, 27263, 62106, 22853, 3789, 11, 1317, 1332, 11, 1317, 1973, 8, 341, 286, 422, 320, 2959, 624, 854, 8, 341, 310, 471, 837, 280, 286, 457, 286, 422, 320, 2959, 11072, 2717, 1332, 1393, 3789, 11072, 2669, 1973, 8, 341, 310, 471, 905, 280, 286, 457, 286, 471, 27263, 62106, 9387, 8436, 11, 1332, 11, 3789, 11072, 8, 1024, 27263, 62106, 9387, 9707, 11, 3789, 11072, 11, 1973, 317, 262, 457, 534, 14196, 19884, 644, 420, 734, 11, 584, 1005, 264, 13438, 734, 1595, 30292, 62106, 63, 430, 5097, 2380, 5137, 25, 279, 1510, 2494, 11, 279, 8187, 907, 430, 279, 2494, 596, 907, 649, 387, 11, 323, 279, 7340, 907, 430, 279, 2494, 596, 907, 649, 387, 13, 4815, 2746, 279, 1510, 2494, 374, 854, 11, 433, 3445, 584, 617, 8813, 279, 842, 315, 279, 5021, 11, 779, 584, 471, 837, 13, 4815, 2746, 279, 1510, 2494, 596, 907, 374, 2753, 1109, 477, 6273, 311, 279, 8187, 907, 477, 7191, 1109, 477, 6273, 311, 279, 7340, 907, 11, 433, 3445, 279, 5021, 374, 539, 264, 44641, 11, 779, 584, 471, 905, 13, 4815, 2746, 279, 1510, 2494, 596, 907, 374, 2949, 279, 2764, 2134, 11, 584, 53947, 1650, 1595, 30292, 62106, 63, 389, 279, 2163, 323, 1314, 42129, 8016, 11, 21686, 279, 2764, 2134, 369, 1855, 54564, 13, 4815, 791, 1925, 734, 1595, 30292, 62106, 63, 6880, 279, 13438, 734, 449, 279, 3789, 2494, 323, 279, 2926, 2764, 2134, 439, 320, 6720, 38570, 7628, 1