Output~2025-04-24 16:36:45.211363: [RequestOutput(request_id=158, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Create a timeline describing the history of the internet ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 4324, 264, 25845, 23524, 279, 3925, 315, 279, 7757, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="Here is a timeline describing the history of the internet:\n\n**1960s: The Early Years**\n\n* 1962: The United States Department of Defense's Advanced Research Projects Agency (ARPA) begins funding a project to create a network of computers that could communicate with each other, known as ARPANET.\n* 1965: The first network, called Network Control Protocol (NCP), is developed by Vint Cerf and Bob Kahn, two pioneers in the field of computer networking.\n* 1969: The first message is sent over ARPANET, from one computer to another, marking the birth of the internet.\n\n**1970s: Expansion and Development**\n\n* 1971: The first email is sent over ARPANET, from one user to another.\n* 1972: The first international connection is made, linking the United States to the United Kingdom.\n* 1973: The Internet Protocol (IP) is developed, allowing different networks to communicate with each other.\n* 1978: The Domain Name System (DNS) is developed, allowing users to access websites using easy-to-remember domain names instead of IP addresses.\n\n**1980s: The Internet Goes Public**\n\n* 1983: The Internet Protocol (IP) is adopted as the standard for the internet, replacing NCP.\n* 1985: The Internet Relay Chat (IRC) is developed, allowing users to communicate with each other in real-time.\n* 1989: The World Wide Web (WWW) is invented by Tim Berners-Lee, making it easy for users to access and share information using web browsers and hyperlinks.\n\n**1990s: The Internet Goes Mainstream**\n\n* 1991: The World Wide Web is made available to the public, and the internet begins to grow rapidly.\n* 1993: The first web browser, Mosaic, is released, making it easy for users to access the internet.\n* 1995: The first online shopping website, Amazon, is launched.\n* 1998: Google is founded, and becomes the dominant search engine on the internet.\n\n**2000s: The Rise of Social Media and Cloud Computing**\n\n* 2004: Facebook is launched, and becomes one of the most popular social media platforms.\n* 2005: YouTube is launched, and becomes a major platform for video sharing.\n* 2006: Cloud computing becomes popular, with the launch of services like Amazon Web Services (AWS) and Microsoft Azure.\n* 2007: The", token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 25845, 23524, 279, 3925, 315, 279, 7757, 1473, 334, 5162, 15, 82, 25, 578, 23591, 23116, 57277, 9, 220, 5162, 17, 25, 578, 3723, 4273, 6011, 315, 16777, 596, 21844, 8483, 32323, 16784, 320, 946, 8201, 8, 12302, 11006, 264, 2447, 311, 1893, 264, 4009, 315, 19002, 430, 1436, 19570, 449, 1855, 1023, 11, 3967, 439, 92437, 1111, 1372, 627, 9, 220, 5162, 20, 25, 578, 1176, 4009, 11, 2663, 8304, 7935, 25590, 320, 45, 7269, 705, 374, 8040, 555, 650, 396, 28764, 69, 323, 14596, 99666, 11, 1403, 83407, 304, 279, 2115, 315, 6500, 29130, 627, 9, 220, 5162, 24, 25, 578, 1176, 1984, 374, 3288, 927, 92437, 1111, 1372, 11, 505, 832, 6500, 311, 2500, 11, 36024, 279, 7342, 315, 279, 7757, 382, 334, 4468, 15, 82, 25, 55654, 323, 11050, 57277, 9, 220, 4468, 16, 25, 578, 1176, 2613, 374, 3288, 927, 92437, 1111, 1372, 11, 505, 832, 1217, 311, 2500, 627, 9, 220, 4468, 17, 25, 578, 1176, 6625, 3717, 374, 1903, 11, 31799, 279, 3723, 4273, 311, 279, 3723, 15422