Output~2025-04-24 16:38:01.041411: [RequestOutput(request_id=202, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Write a short story about a day in the life of a software engineer. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 9842, 264, 2875, 3446, 922, 264, 1938, 304, 279, 2324, 315, 264, 3241, 24490, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="It was 8:00 AM on a typical Monday morning, and I, Alex, a software engineer at TechCorp, was already sipping on my coffee as I settled into my cubicle. I had a big project deadline looming, and I needed to make some progress today. I booted up my laptop and dove into the code, trying to shake off the lingering sleepiness.\n\nMy first task was to tackle a pesky bug that had been plaguing our team's latest app. I spent the next hour pouring over lines of code, trying to identify the source of the issue. My coworker, Rachel, poked her head into my cubicle, asking if I needed any help. I appreciated the offer, but I was determined to crack the code on my own.\n\nAfter a few more hours of debugging, I finally found the culprit – a misplaced semicolon that was causing the app to crash. I felt a sense of accomplishment as I fixed the bug and watched the app run smoothly.\n\nNext, I turned my attention to a new feature I was tasked with implementing. I spent the next few hours designing and coding the new functionality, working closely with our product manager to ensure it met the requirements. The collaboration was seamless, and I was impressed by how well our team worked together.\n\nAt lunchtime, I grabbed a sandwich from the cafeteria and headed to the break room to catch up with my colleagues. We chatted about everything from our weekends to our favorite TV shows. It was a much-needed break from the intensity of coding.\n\nThe afternoon was filled with more coding and testing, but I was in the zone. I was so focused that I didn't even notice when my manager stopped by to check on my progress. He was pleased with my work and gave me a nod of approval.\n\nAs the day drew to a close, I took a moment to review my tasks and prioritize my work for the next day. I was proud of what I had accomplished and felt confident that I was on track to meet my deadline.\n\nAs I packed up my things and headed home, I couldn't help but feel grateful for my job. I loved the challenge of solving complex problems and the sense of satisfaction that came with creating something new. It was a good day to be a software engineer.", token_ids=[2181, 574, 220, 23, 25, 410, 6912, 389, 264, 14595, 7159, 6693, 11, 323, 358, 11, 8683, 11, 264, 3241, 24490, 520, 17829, 95895, 11, 574, 2736, 274, 5772, 389, 856, 11033, 439, 358, 23183, 1139, 856, 19250, 2045, 13, 358, 1047, 264, 2466, 2447, 22143, 65564, 11, 323, 358, 4460, 311, 1304, 1063, 5208, 3432, 13, 358, 712, 9437, 709, 856, 21288, 323, 48322, 1139, 279, 2082, 11, 4560, 311, 27116, 1022, 279, 64610, 6212, 1918, 382, 5159, 1176, 3465, 574, 311, 22118, 264, 18541, 8050, 10077, 430, 1047, 1027, 39137, 7623, 1057, 2128, 596, 5652, 917, 13, 358, 7543, 279, 1828, 6596, 51513, 927, 5238, 315, 2082, 11, 4560, 311, 10765, 279, 2592, 315, 279, 4360, 13, 3092, 61068, 261, 11, 32532, 11, 281, 11059, 1077, 2010, 1139, 856, 19250, 2045, 11, 10371, 422, 358, 4460, 904, 1520, 13, 358, 26893, 279, 3085, 11, 719, 358, 574, 11075, 311, 17944, 279, 2082, 389, 856, 1866, 382, 6153, 264, 2478, 810, 4207, 315, 28803, 11, 358, 5616, 1766, 279, 75283, 1389, 264, 90660, 5347, 39617, 430, 574, 14718, 2