Output~2025-04-24 16:39:32.863655: [RequestOutput(request_id=251, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Research about a famous scientist and provide a short biography about him/her. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 8483, 922, 264, 11495, 28568, 323, 3493, 264, 2875, 48345, 922, 1461, 39007, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="Here is a short biography about a famous scientist:\n\n**Marie Curie**\n\nMarie Curie (1867-1934) was a Polish-born physicist and chemist who made groundbreaking discoveries in the fields of radioactivity and nuclear physics. She is the first woman to win a Nobel Prize, and the first person to win two Nobel Prizes in different fields - physics in 1903 and chemistry in 1911.\n\nBorn Maria Skłodowska in Warsaw, Poland, Curie was raised in a family of intellectuals and was encouraged to pursue her love of learning from a young age. She studied physics and mathematics at the Flying University, a secret institution that offered education to women, as women were not allowed to attend the University of Warsaw at the time.\n\nIn 1891, Curie moved to Paris to continue her studies at the Sorbonne University, where she met her future husband, Pierre Curie. Together, they began researching radioactivity, a phenomenon discovered by Henri Becquerel in 1896. The Curies isolated two new radioactive elements, polonium and radium, and developed techniques for isolating and purifying these elements.\n\nMarie Curie's work on radioactivity led to the development of new medical treatments and diagnostic tools, and she was the first woman to become a professor at the University of Paris. She also founded the Curie Institutes in Warsaw and Paris, which remain leading centers for research in nuclear physics and medicine.\n\nThroughout her career, Curie faced many challenges as a woman in a male-dominated field, but she persevered and became an international celebrity. Her legacy continues to inspire women and girls around the world to pursue careers in science and technology.", token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 2875, 48345, 922, 264, 11495, 28568, 1473, 334, 12331, 648, 13182, 648, 57277, 12331, 648, 13182, 648, 320, 9714, 22, 12, 7285, 19, 8, 574, 264, 33084, 40260, 83323, 323, 8590, 380, 889, 1903, 64955, 54098, 304, 279, 5151, 315, 9063, 7323, 323, 11499, 22027, 13, 3005, 374, 279, 1176, 5333, 311, 3243, 264, 48078, 32293, 11, 323, 279, 1176, 1732, 311, 3243, 1403, 48078, 2394, 4861, 304, 2204, 5151, 482, 22027, 304, 220, 7028, 18, 323, 30903, 304, 220, 7529, 16, 382, 59204, 23880, 4923, 4697, 347, 4336, 4657, 304, 73276, 11, 28702, 11, 13182, 648, 574, 9408, 304, 264, 3070, 315, 83936, 323, 574, 21190, 311, 23564, 1077, 3021, 315, 6975, 505, 264, 3995, 4325, 13, 3005, 20041, 22027, 323, 38696, 520, 279, 47152, 3907, 11, 264, 6367, 15244, 430, 9076, 6873, 311, 3278, 11, 439, 3278, 1051, 539, 5535, 311, 9604, 279, 3907, 315, 73276, 520, 279, 892, 382, 644, 220, 9378, 16, 11, 13182, 648, 7882, 311, 12366, 311, 3136, 1077, 7978, 520, 279, 30631, 6098, 818, 3907, 11, 1405, 1364, 2322, 1077, 3938, 10177, 11, 38077, 13182, 648, 13, 32255, 11, 814, 6137, 45243, 9063, 7323, 11, 264, 25885, 11352, 555, 74310, 32146, 16339, 301, 304, 220, 9378, 21, 13, 578, 356, 10612, 25181, 1403, 502, 59862, 5540, 11, 1499, 90344, 323, 9038, 2411, 11, 323, 8040, 12823, 369, 13399, 1113, 323, 4087, 7922, 1521, 5540, 382, 12331, 648, 13182, 648, 596, 990, 389, 9063, 7323, 6197, 311, 279, 4500, 315, 502, 6593, 22972, 323, 15439, 7526, 11, 32