Output~2025-04-24 16:45:29.603705: [RequestOutput(request_id=397, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Three fair, standard six-sided dice are rolled. What is the probability that the sum of the numbers on the top faces is 18? Express your answer as a common fraction. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 14853, 6762, 11, 5410, 4848, 50858, 22901, 527, 23255, 13, 3639, 374, 279, 19463, 430, 279, 2694, 315, 279, 5219, 389, 279, 1948, 12580, 374, 220, 972, 30, 17855, 701, 4320, 439, 264, 4279, 19983, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='A nice probability problem!\n\nSince the dice are fair and standard six-sided, each die has an equal probability of landing on any of the numbers 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, or 6.\n\nTo find the probability that the sum of the numbers on the top faces is 18, we need to consider all possible combinations of three dice that add up to 18.\n\nHere are the only possible combinations:\n\n* (6, 6, 6) - This is the only combination that adds up to 18.\n\nSince there is only one way to get a sum of 18, the probability is the number of favorable outcomes (1) divided by the total number of possible outcomes.\n\nThe total number of possible outcomes is 6^3 = 216, since each die has 6 possible outcomes.\n\nSo, the probability that the sum of the numbers on the top faces is 18 is:\n\n1/216 = 1/216\n\nExpressed as a common fraction, the answer is:\n\n1/216', token_ids=[32, 6555, 19463, 3575, 2268, 12834, 279, 22901, 527, 6762, 323, 5410, 4848, 50858