deral student loans have a fixed interest rate of 4.53% for undergraduate loans, while in Canada, the interest rate is around 5.4% for federal student loans.\n2. **Loan forgiveness programs**: The US has a more comprehensive loan forgiveness program, including Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) and Teacher Loan Forgiveness. In Canada, there are limited forgiveness programs, and forgiveness is typically only available for certain professions, such as teaching and nursing.\n3. **Government support**: The Canadian government provides more comprehensive support for students, including a non-repayable grant program and a more generous student loan forgiveness program. In the US, the government has been criticized for not doing enough to address the student debt crisis.\n4. **Tuition fees**: Tuition fees are generally higher in the US than in Canada, which can contribute to higher debt levels. In the US, the average tuition fee for a four-year public college is around $10,000 per year, while in Canada, it's around $6,000 per year.\n\n**Conclusion:**\n\nWhile both the US and Canada face a student debt crisis, there are significant differences in the nature and scope of the issue. The US has a more comprehensive loan forgiveness program, but higher interest", token_ids=[791, 5575, 11897, 11501, 374, 264, 26422, 4360, 304, 2225, 279, 3723, 4273, 323, 7008, 11, 449, 11990, 315, 4236, 20558, 311, 10299, 872, 11897, 323, 11322, 6020, 20334, 1306, 39554, 13, 6104, 2225, 5961, 4430, 1063, 43874, 11, 1070, 527, 1101, 1063, 1401, 12062, 304, 279, 7138, 323, 7036, 315, 279, 11501, 382, 334, 35502, 1385, 25, 57277, 16, 13, 3146, 49, 3876, 11897, 5990, 96618, 763, 2225, 279, 2326, 323, 7008, 11, 5575, 11897, 706, 1027, 7859, 43071, 927, 279, 3347, 2478, 11026, 13, 763, 279, 2326, 11, 5575, 11941, 11897, 706, 15042, 505, 400, 8273, 7239, 304, 220, 1049, 19, 311, 927, 400, 16, 13, 22, 32610, 304, 220, 2366, 15, 13, 763, 7008, 11, 5575, 11897, 706, 7319, 505, 400, 605, 7239, 304, 220