Output~2025-04-24 16:51:04.972962: [RequestOutput(request_id=527, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Outline the events of the following movie: The Great Gatsby. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 53009, 279, 4455, 315, 279, 2768, 5818, 25, 578, 8681, 480, 36614, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="Here is an outline of the events of the movie The Great Gatsby:\n\nI. Introduction\n\n* The movie opens with Nick Carraway, a young man from the Midwest, moving to Long Island's West Egg to work in the bond business.\n* Nick rents a small house next to a grand mansion owned by the mysterious millionaire Jay Gatsby.\n\nII. Gatsby's Mysterious Past\n\n* Nick learns that Gatsby and his neighbor, Tom Buchanan, were once friends at Oxford University.\n* Gatsby's past is shrouded in mystery, and Nick becomes curious about his background.\n* Gatsby and Nick become friends, and Gatsby confides in Nick about his love for Daisy Buchanan, Tom's wife.\n\nIII. The Party\n\n* Gatsby throws a lavish party, hoping to attract Daisy's attention.\n* Daisy and Tom's marriage is troubled, and Daisy is unhappy in her relationship.\n* Gatsby and Daisy reunite at the party, and their love for each other is rekindled.\n\nIV. The Love Triangle\n\n* Gatsby and Daisy's affair begins, but their love is complicated by Tom's possessiveness and jealousy.\n* Tom's mistress, Myrtle Wilson, is also involved in the love triangle, and her husband, George, is suspicious of her infidelity.\n* The tension between the characters builds as the love triangle becomes more intense.\n\nV. The Tragic Confrontation\n\n* George Wilson, Myrtle's husband, discovers her infidelity and seeks revenge against Gatsby, believing he is the one who was having an affair with his wife.\n* George finds Gatsby's car in his garage and mistakenly assumes it belongs to Gatsby, leading him to shoot and kill Gatsby.\n* Daisy, who was driving the car, is unharmed but traumatized by the event.\n\nVI. The Aftermath\n\n* Tom and Daisy return to their wealthy lifestyle, but their relationship is now tainted by the tragic events.\n* Nick is disillusioned by the excesses and superficiality of the wealthy elite and decides to return to the Midwest.\n* The movie ends with Nick reflecting on the emptiness and tragedy of the characters' lives, and the loss of the American Dream.\n\nThis outline provides a general overview of the events in the movie The Great Gatsby.", token_ids=[8586, 374, 459, 21782, 315, 279, 4455, 315, 279, 5818, 578, 8681, 480, 36614, 1473, 40, 13, 29438, 271, 9, 578, 5818, 16264, 449, 15341, 3341, 1059, 352, 11, 264, 3995, 893, 505, 279, 52257, 11, 7366, 311, 5843, 10951, 596, 4410, 42313, 311, 990, 304, 279, 11049, 2626, 627, 9, 15341, 63090, 264, 2678, 3838, 1828, 311, 264, 6800, 52528, 13234, 555, 279, 26454, 90044, 19455, 480, 36614, 382, 5660, 13, 480, 36614, 596, 386, 97499, 24561, 271, 9, 15341, 47310, 430, 480, 36614, 323, 813, 9760, 11, 8529, 85290, 11, 1051, 3131, 4885, 520, 26275, 3907, 627, 9, 480, 36614, 596, 3347, 374, 559, 583, 9988, 304, 23347, 11, 323, 15341, 9221, 22999, 922, 813, 4092, 627, 9, 480, 36614, 323, 15341, 3719, 4885, 11, 323, 480, 36614, 2389, 3422, 304, 15341, 922, 813, 3021, 369, 71264, 85290, 11, 8529, 596, 7555, 382, 23440, 13, 578, 8722, 271, 9, 480, 36614, 3872, 264, 80234, 4717, 11, 16026, 311, 9504, 71264, 596, 6666, 627, 9, 71264, 323, 8529, 596, 11103, 374, 42132, 11, 323, 71264, 374, 43251, 304, 1077, 5133, 627, 9, 480, 36614, 