Output~2025-04-24 16:51:07.343929: [RequestOutput(request_id=528, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Calculate the area of a triangle with the following sides: 10, 14, 8. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 21157, 279, 3158, 315, 264, 22217, 449, 279, 2768, 11314, 25, 220, 605, 11, 220, 975, 11, 220, 23, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="To calculate the area of a triangle, we need to know the base and height of the triangle. Since we are given the lengths of all three sides, we can use Heron's formula to find the area.\n\nFirst, we need to find the semi-perimeter of the triangle, which is the sum of the lengths of all three sides divided by 2:\n\ns = (10 + 14 + 8) / 2 = 32 / 2 = 16\n\nNext, we need to calculate the area using Heron's formula:\n\nArea = √(s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c))\n\nwhere a, b, and c are the lengths of the sides. Plugging in the values, we get:\n\nArea = √(16(16-10)(16-14)(16-8))\n= √(16(6)(2)(8))\n= √(384)\n= 19.6\n\nSo, the area of the triangle is approximately 19.6 square units.", token_ids=[1271, 11294, 279, 3158, 315, 264, 22217, 11, 584, 1205, 311, 1440, 279, 2385, 323, 2673, 315, 279, 22217, 13, 8876, 584, 527, 2728, 279, 29416, 315, 682, 2380, 11314, 11, 584, 649, 1005, 6385, 263, 596, 15150, 311, 1505, 279, 3158, 382, 5451, 11, 584, 1205, 311, 1505, 279, 18768, 17453, 26402, 315, 279, 22217, 11, 902, 374, 279, 2694, 315, 279, 29416, 315, 682, 2380, 11314, 18255, 555, 220, 17, 1473, 82, 284, 320, 605, 489, 220, 975, 489, 220, 2