Output~2025-04-24 16:52:25.935683: [RequestOutput(request_id=556, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Describe the impact of the Tour de France on the history of cycling ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 61885, 279, 5536, 315, 279, 14986, 409, 9822, 389, 279, 3925, 315, 33162, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="The Tour de France, first held in 1903, has had a profound impact on the history of cycling. As the most prestigious and iconic cycling event in the world, it has not only shaped the sport itself but also influenced the development of cycling culture, technology, and global popularity.\n\nOne of the most significant impacts of the Tour de France is its role in popularizing cycling as a global sport. The event has attracted millions of fans worldwide, making it a major spectator sport. The Tour's global reach has led to the growth of professional cycling teams, riders, and events, creating a thriving industry that generates significant revenue and employment opportunities.\n\nThe Tour de France has also driven innovation in cycling technology. The event has pushed manufacturers to develop lighter, stronger, and more aerodynamic bikes, as well as advanced components and accessories. The pursuit of speed and efficiency has led to the creation of new materials, designs, and manufacturing techniques, which have trickled down to the amateur and recreational cycling community.\n\nThe Tour de France has also had a profound impact on the sport's culture and tradition. The event has created a sense of national pride and identity, with each country's team and riders competing fiercely for victory. The Tour's iconic yellow jersey, worn by the leader of the general classification, has become a symbol of excellence and achievement in the sport.\n\nFurthermore, the Tour de France has played a significant role in shaping the careers of many legendary cyclists. The event has provided a platform for riders to showcase their skills, gain recognition, and secure sponsorship deals. Many of the sport's greatest champions, such as Jacques Anquetil, Eddy Merckx, Bernard Hinault, and Lance Armstrong, have won the Tour de France multiple times, cementing their places in cycling history.\n\nIn addition, the Tour de France has had a lasting impact on the development of road cycling infrastructure and tourism. The event has led to the construction of new roads, bike paths, and cycling facilities, making it easier for people to ride and enjoy the sport. The Tour's route, which passes through some of the most beautiful and scenic regions of France, has also boosted local economies and promoted tourism.\n\nIn conclusion, the Tour de France has had a profound and lasting impact on the history of cycling. From popularizing the sport globally to driving innovation in technology and culture, the event has left an indelible mark on the sport. Its influence can be seen in the development of professional cycling teams, the creation of new technologies, and the growth of cycling culture and tourism.", token_ids=[791, 14986, 409, 9822, 11, 1176, 5762, 304, 220, 7028, 18, 11, 706, 1047, 264, 28254, 5536, 389, 279, 3925, 315, 33162, 13, 1666, 279, 1455, 41385, 323, 27373, 33162, 1567, 304, 279, 1917, 11, 433, 706, 539, 1193, 27367, 279, 10775, 5196, 719, 1101, 28160, 279, 4500, 315, 33162, 7829, 11, 5557, 11, 323, 3728, 23354, 382, 4054, 315, 279, 1455, 5199, 25949, 315, 279, 14986, 409, 9822, 374, 1202, 3560, 304, 5526, 4954, 33162, 439, 264, 3