Output~2025-04-24 16:55:05.407056: [RequestOutput(request_id=634, prompt='<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{\'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Explain the term "impeachment" ### Response:\'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n', prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 83017, 279, 4751, 330, 318, 375, 9064, 1, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Impeachment is a constitutional process in the United States government that allows Congress to remove a government official from office for "treason, bribery, or other high crimes and misdemeanors." The process is outlined in Article II, Section 4 of the United States Constitution, which states that the President, Vice President, and all civil officers can be impeached and removed from office if they commit treason, bribery, or other high crimes and misdemeanors.\n\nThe impeachment process typically begins in the House of Representatives, where a majority vote is required to pass articles of impeachment, which are formal charges against the official. The articles of impeachment are then sent to the Senate, where a two-thirds majority vote is required to convict and remove the official from office.\n\nImpeachment is often confused with removal from office, but they are not the same thing. Impeachment is the process of charging an official with wrongdoing, while removal from office is the actual removal of the official from their position. In other words, impeachment is the accusation, while removal is the punishment.\n\nIn the history of the United States, there have been two instances of a President being impeached: Andrew Johnson in 1868 and Bill Clinton in 1998. Both were acquitted by the Senate and remained in office. Richard Nixon resigned from office in 1974 before he could be impeached, and Donald Trump was impeached by the House of Representatives in 2019, but was acquitted by the Senate in 2020.\n\nIn summary, impeachment is a constitutional process that allows Congress to remove a government official from office for wrongdoing, and it is an important check on the power of the executive branch to ensure that officials are held accountable for their actions.', token_ids=[1453, 375, 9064, 374, 264, 25543, 1920, 304, 279, 3723, 4273, 3109, 430, 6276, 8151, 311, 4148, 264, 3109, 4033, 505, 5274, 369, 330, 10367, 1525, 11, 93137, 11, 477, 1023, 1579, 17073, 323, 51726, 1105, 1210, 578, 1920, 374, 33740, 304, 13659, 8105, 11, 11360, 220, 19, 315, 279, 3723, 4273, 18039, 11, 902, 5415, 430, 279, 4900, 11, 23270, 4900, 11, 323, 682, 8431, 9808, 649, 387, 36126, 3939, 323, 7108, 505, 5274, 422, 814, 5379, 79359, 11, 93137, 11, 477, 1023, 1579, 17073, 323, 51726, 1105, 382, 791, 64754, 1920, 11383, 12302, 304, 279, 4783, 315, 40845, 11, 1405, 264, 8857, 7055, 374, 2631, 311, 1522, 9908, 315, 64754, 11, 902, 527, 16287, 10405, 2403, 279, 4033, 13, 578, 9908, 315, 64754, 527, 1243, 3288, 311, 279, 10092, 11, 1405, 264, 1403, 45726, 8857, 7055, 374, 2631, 311, 91134, 323, 4148, 279, 4033, 505, 5274, 382, 1453, 375, 9064, 374, 3629, 22568, 449, 17065, 505, 5274, 11, 719, 814, 527, 539, 279, 1890, 3245, 13, 2417, 375, 9064, 374, 279, 1920, 315, 23468, 459, 4033, 449, 65328, 11, 1418, 17065, 505, 5274, 374, 279, 5150, 17065, 315, 279, 4033, 505, 872, 2361, 13, 763, 1023, 4339, 11, 64754, 374, 279, 65506, 11, 1418, 17065, 374, 279, 25060, 382, 644, 279, 3925, 315, 279, 3723, 4273, 11, 1070, 617, 1027, 1403, 13422, 315, 264, 4900, 1694, 36126, 3939, 25, 13929, 11605, 304, 220, 9714, 23, 323, 8766, 8283, 304, 220, 2550, 23, 13, 11995, 1051, 91533, 555, 279, 10092, 323, 14958, 30