Output~2025-04-24 16:58:00.685175: [RequestOutput(request_id=693, prompt='<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{\'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Write a summary of the book "The Catcher in the Rye". ### Response:\'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n', prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 9842, 264, 12399, 315, 279, 2363, 330, 791, 21603, 261, 304, 279, 432, 9188, 3343, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here is a summary of the book "The Catcher in the Rye":\n\n"The Catcher in the Rye" is a classic coming-of-age novel written by J.D. Salinger, published in 1951. The story follows the protagonist, Holden Caulfield, a 16-year-old high school student, as he navigates the challenges of adolescence and grapples with the phoniness and superficiality of the adult world.\n\nThe story takes place over the course of three days, during which Holden is expelled from a prestigious boarding school, Pencey Prep, due to poor grades. Feeling disconnected and disillusioned, Holden travels to New York City, where he spends the night in a hotel room, reflecting on his relationships, his future, and the phoniness of the world around him.\n\nThroughout the novel, Holden struggles with feelings of alienation and disconnection, particularly with his peers and the adults in his life. He is disenchanted with the idea of growing up and becoming like the phonies he perceives around him. He is also haunted by the death of his younger brother, Allie, which has left a deep emotional scar.\n\nThe novel\'s title, "The Catcher in the Rye," refers to Holden\'s fantasy of becoming the "catcher in the rye," protecting children from falling off a cliff and into the abyss of phoniness and corruption. This symbolizes his desire to preserve childhood innocence and protect others from the corrupting influences of the adult world.\n\nThrough Holden\'s experiences and observations, the novel explores themes of identity, alienation, rebellion, and the struggles of growing up. The book has become a classic of American literature, widely regarded as a relatable and poignant portrayal of adolescent angst and the challenges of transitioning from childhood to adulthood.', token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 12399, 315, 279, 2363, 330, 791, 21603, 261, 304, 279, 432, 9188, 52518, 10227, 21603, 261, 304, 279, 432, 9188, 1, 374, 264, 11670, 5108, 8838, 44041, 11775, 5439, 555, 622, 920, 13, 8375, 5248, 11, 4756, 304, 220, 6280, 16, 13, 578, 3446, 11263, 279, 46684, 11, 87485, 90538, 2630, 11, 264, 220, 845, 4771, 6418, 1579, 2978, 5575, 11, 439, 568, 34512, 988, 279, 11774, 315, 83909, 323, 1099, 680, 645, 449, 279, 51923, 1918, 323, 59915, 488, 315, 279, 6822, 1917, 382, 791, 3446, 5097, 2035, 927, 279, 3388, 315, 2380, 2919, 11, 2391, 902, 87485, 374, 67331, 505, 264, 41385, 50069, 2978, 11, 47060, 88, 49169, 11, 4245, 311, 8009, 28711, 13, 74658, 40186, 323, 98009, 291, 11, 87485, 35292, 311, 1561, 4356, 4409, 11, 1405, 568, 38202, 279, 3814, 304, 264, 9689, 3130, 11, 42852, 389, 813, 12135, 11, 813, 3938, 11, 323, 279, 51923, 1918, 315, 279, 1917, 2212, 1461, 382, 60105, 279, 11775, 11, 87485, 28970, 449, 16024, 315, 20167, 367, 323, 834, 7898, 11, 8104, 449, 813, 26081, 323, 279, 12884, 304, 813, 2324, 13, 1283, 374, 834, 20345, 7719, 449, 279, 4623, 315, 7982, 709, 323, 10671, 1093, 279, 51923, 552, 568, 62822, 1924, 2212, 1461, 13, 1283, 374, 1101, 57775, 555, 279, 4648, 315, 813, 14992, 10868, 11, 2052, 648, 11, 902, 706, 2163, 264, 5655, 14604, 23087, 382, 791, 11775, 596, 2316, 11, 330, 791, 21603, 261, 304, 279, 432, 9188, 1359, 19813, 311, 87485, 596, 18