Output~2025-04-24 16:58:12.069989: [RequestOutput(request_id=700, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Explain the significance of the Battle of Gettysburg. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 83017, 279, 26431, 315, 279, 16506, 315, 2175, 83, 1065, 10481, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="The Battle of Gettysburg, fought from July 1 to July 3, 1863, was a pivotal event in the American Civil War, marking a turning point in the conflict and having significant consequences for the future of the United States. The battle was fought between the Union Army of the Potomac, led by General George Meade, and the Confederate Army of Northern Virginia, led by General Robert E. Lee.\n\nThe battle was significant for several reasons:\n\n1. **Turning point of the war**: The Battle of Gettysburg was a decisive defeat for the Confederate Army, marking a turning point in the war. It was the bloodiest battle of the Civil War, with over 50,000 casualties (killed, wounded, or missing). The Confederate Army never fully recovered from this loss, and the Union Army gained momentum, ultimately leading to the defeat of the Confederacy.\n2. **Union victory**: The Union victory at Gettysburg was a crucial moment in the war, as it prevented the Confederate Army from invading the North and potentially winning the war. The battle showed that the Union Army was capable of defeating the Confederate Army on its own territory, boosting morale and confidence among Union troops.\n3. **Emancipation Proclamation**: The Battle of Gettysburg coincided with the issuance of the Emancipation Proclamation by President Abraham Lincoln on January 1, 1863. The battle's outcome reinforced the importance of the Emancipation Proclamation, which declared freedom for all slaves in Confederate territory.\n4. **Gettysburg Address**: The battle also led to one of the most famous speeches in American history, the Gettysburg Address, delivered by President Lincoln on November 19, 1863. In the speech, Lincoln honored the fallen Union soldiers and reiterated the principles of equality and liberty upon which the United States was founded.\n5. **Impact on the war's outcome**: The Battle of Gettysburg marked a shift in the war's momentum, as the Union Army gained the upper hand and the Confederacy began to lose ground. The battle's outcome set the stage for the eventual defeat of the Confederacy and the abolition of slavery.\n\nIn conclusion, the Battle of Gettysburg was a crucial event in American history, marking a turning point in the Civil War and having significant consequences for the future of the United States. The battle's outcome reinforced the Union's commitment to preserving the Union and ending slavery, and it remains an important symbol of American sacrifice", token_ids=[791, 16506, 315, 2175, 83, 1065, 10481, 11, 21095, 505, 5887, 220, 16, 311, 5887, 220, 18, 11, 220, 9714, 18, 11, 574, 264, 60850, 1567, 304, 279, 3778, 16803, 5111, 11, 36024, 264, 13353, 1486, 304, 279, 12324, 323, 3515, 5199, 16296, 369, 279, 3938, 315, 279, 3723, 4273, 13, 578, 8209, 574, 21095, 1990, 279, 9323, 13309, 315, 279, 14020, 316, 582, 11, 6197, 555, 3331, 10058, 2206, 1037, 11, 323, 279, 57457, 13309, 315, 17355, 13286, 11, 6197, 555, 3331, 8563, 469, 13, 12336, 382, 791, 8209, 574, 5199, 369, 3892, 8125, 1473, 16, 13, 3146, 98951, 1486, 315, 279, 4208, 96618, 578, 16506, 315, 2175, 83, 1065, 10481, 574, 264, 51391, 18506, 369, 279, 57457, 13309, 11, 36024, 264, 13353, 1486, 304, 279, 4208, 13, 1102, 574, 279, 6680, 13744, 8209, 315, 279, 16803, 5111, 11, 449, 927, 220, 1135, 11, 931, 48988, 320, 74, 4473, 11, 28593, 11, 477, 7554, 570, 578, 57457, 13309, 2646, 7373, 26403, 505, 420, 4814, 11, 323, 279, 9323, 13309, 18661, 24151, 11, 13967, 6522, 311, 279, 18506, 315, 279, 39144, 2826, 627, 17, 13, 3146, 33758, 12845, 96618, 578, 9323, 12845, 520, 2175, 83, 1065, 10481, 574, 264, 16996, 4545, 304, 279, 4208, 11, 439, 433, 32098, 279, 57457, 13309, 505, 83631, 279, 4892, 323, 13893, 11230, 279, 4208, 13, 578, 8209, 8710, 430, 279, 9323, 13309, 574, 13171, 315, 54216, 279, 57457, 13309, 389, 1202, 1866, 18455, 11, 56028, 63683, 323, 12410, 4315, 9323, 17312, 627, 18, 13, 3146, 2321, 1149, 49686, 1322, 34084, 96618, 578, 16506, 315, 2175, 83, 1065, 10481, 23828, 4591, 449, 279, 67599, 315, 279, 5867, 1149, 49686, 1322, 34084, 555, 4900, 37488, 25379, 389, 6186, 220, 16, 11, 220, 9714, 18, 13, 578, 8209, 596, 15632, 49680, 279, 12939, 315, 279, 5867, 1149, 49686, 1322, 34084, 11, 902, 14610, 11542, 369, 682, 32760, 304, 57457, 18455, 627, 19, 13, 3146, 1991, 83, 1065, 10481, 9356, 96618, 578, 8209, 1101, 6197, 311, 832, 315, 279, 1455, 11495, 44440, 304, 3778, 3925, 11, 279, 2175, 83, 1065, 10481, 9356, 11, 12886, 555, 4900, 25379, 389, 6841, 220, 777, 11, 220, 9714, 18, 13, 763, 279, 8982, 11, 25379, 39377, 279, 21536, 9323, 15201, 323, 66847, 279, 16565, 315, 22526, 323, 31220, 5304, 902, 279, 3723, 4273, 574, 18538, 627, 20, 13, 3146, 72603, 389, 279, 4208, 596, 15632, 96618, 578, 16506, 315, 2175, 83, 1065, 10481, 13160, 264, 6541, 304, 279, 4208, 596, 24151, 11, 439, 279, 9323, 13309, 18661, 279, 8582, 1450, 323, 279, 39144, 2826, 6137, 311, 9229, 5015, 13, 578, 8209, 596, 15632, 743, 279, 6566, 369, 279, 42835, 18506, 315, 279, 39144, 2826, 323, 279, 76445, 315, 33792, 382, 644, 17102, 11, 279, 16506, 315, 2175, 83, 1065, 10481, 574, 264, 16996, 1567, 304, 3778, 3925, 11, 36024, 264, 13353, 1486, 304, 279, 16803, 5111, 323, 3515, 51