Output~2025-04-24 17:00:22.236067: [RequestOutput(request_id=760, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Describe the process of thawing frozen food. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 61885, 279, 1920, 315, 86478, 287, 20268, 3691, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="Thawing frozen food is a crucial step in preparing it for cooking and consumption. The process of thawing frozen food involves gradually warming it up to a safe temperature to prevent bacterial growth and foodborne illness. Here's a step-by-step guide on how to thaw frozen food safely:\n\n1. **Plan ahead**: Always plan ahead and allow enough time to thaw frozen food in the refrigerator or in cold water. Never thaw food at room temperature or in warm water, as this can promote bacterial growth.\n2. **Refrigerator Thawing**: Place the frozen food in a leak-proof bag or a covered container on the middle or bottom shelf of the refrigerator. Allow 6-24 hours for thawing, depending on the size and type of food.\n3. **Cold Water Thawing**: Place the frozen food in a leak-proof bag and submerge it in cold water. Change the water every 30 minutes to keep it cold. It may take 30 minutes to several hours to thaw, depending on the size and type of food.\n4. **Microwave Thawing**: Defrost frozen food in the microwave according to the manufacturer's instructions. Cover the food with a microwave-safe lid or plastic wrap to prevent moisture loss. Check and stir the food every 30 seconds to ensure even thawing.\n5. **Cooking**: Once thawed, cook the food immediately to an internal temperature of at least 165°F (74°C) to ensure food safety.\n\n**Important Safety Tips**:\n\n* Always wash your hands before and after handling frozen food.\n* Prevent cross-contamination by separating raw meat, poultry, and seafood from ready-to-eat foods.\n* Cook frozen food to the recommended internal temperature to prevent foodborne illness.\n* Never refreeze thawed food without cooking it first.\n\nBy following these steps and safety tips, you can safely thaw frozen food and enjoy a delicious and healthy meal.", token_ids=[1016, 675, 287, 20268, 3691, 374, 264, 16996, 3094, 304, 20646, 433, 369, 17677, 323, 15652, 13, 578, 1920, 315, 86478, 287, 20268, 3691, 18065, 27115, 24808, 433, 709, 311, 264, 6220, 9499, 311, 5471, 45964, 6650, 323, 3691, 32096, 17563, 13, 5810, 596, 264, 3094, 14656, 30308, 8641, 389, 1268, 311, 86478, 20268, 3691, 21676, 1473, 16, 13, 3146, 21119, 8469, 96618, 24119, 3197, 8469, 323, 2187, 3403, 892, 311, 86478, 20268, 3691, 304, 279, 46044, 477, 304, 9439, 3090, 13, 15037, 86478, 3691, 520, 3130, 9499, 477, 304, 8369, 3090, 11, 439, 420, 649, 12192, 45964, 6650, 627, 17, 13, 3146, 697, 1658, 7420, 859, 666, 675, 287, 96618, 11004, 279, 20268, 3691, 304, 264, 24237, 60267, 9145, 477, 264, 9960, 5593, 389, 279, 6278, 477, 5740, 28745, 315, 279, 46044, 13, 27628, 220, 21, 12, 1187, 4207, 369, 86478, 287, 11, 11911, 389, 279, 1404, 323, 955, 315, 3691, 627, 18, 13, 3146, 77518, 10164, 666, 675, 287, 96618, 11004, 279, 20268, 3691, 304, 264, 24237, 60267, 9145, 323, 1207, 19590, 433, 304, 9439, 3090, 13, 10604, 279, 3090, 1475, 220, 966, 4520, 311, 2567, 433, 9439, 13, 1102, 1253, 1935, 220, 966, 4520, 311, 3892, 4207, 311, 86478, 11, 11911, 389, 279, 1404, 323, 955, 315, 3691, 627, 19, 13, 3146, 98402, 34803, 666, 675, 287, 96618, 3979, 42602, 20268, 3691, 304, 279, 42374, 4184, 311, 279, 14290, 596, 11470, 13, 18230, 279, 3691, 449, 264, 42374, 56219, 27431, 4