Output~2025-04-24 17:01:46.143030: [RequestOutput(request_id=797, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Create a timeline of the key events surrounding the 2004 Indian Ocean earthquake and tsunami. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 4324, 264, 25845, 315, 279, 1401, 4455, 14932, 279, 220, 1049, 19, 7904, 22302, 38413, 323, 72155, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="Here is a timeline of the key events surrounding the 2004 Indian Ocean earthquake and tsunami:\n\n**December 26, 2004**\n\n* 00:58:53 UTC (07:58:53 local time): A massive undersea earthquake with a magnitude of 9.1-9.3 strikes off the coast of Indonesia's northern province of Aceh, triggering a massive tsunami.\n* 01:00 UTC (08:00 local time): The tsunami waves begin to hit the coast of Indonesia, causing widespread destruction and loss of life.\n\n**December 26, 2004 (continued)**\n\n* 01:30 UTC (08:30 local time): The tsunami waves reach the coast of Thailand, causing significant damage and loss of life in popular tourist areas such as Phuket, Khao Lak, and Phang Nga.\n* 02:00 UTC (09:00 local time): The tsunami waves hit the coast of Sri Lanka, causing widespread destruction and loss of life.\n* 02:30 UTC (09:30 local time): The tsunami waves reach the coast of India, causing significant damage and loss of life in the states of Tamil Nadu, Andhra Pradesh, and Kerala.\n* 03:00 UTC (10:00 local time): The tsunami waves hit the coast of Myanmar (Burma), causing significant damage and loss of life.\n\n**December 27, 2004**\n\n* International aid efforts begin, with rescue teams and supplies arriving in affected areas.\n* The death toll begins to rise, with estimates suggesting over 230,000 people have lost their lives in 14 countries.\n\n**January 2005**\n\n* The full extent of the disaster becomes clear, with the death toll estimated at over 280,000 people in 14 countries.\n* International aid efforts continue, with many countries and organizations providing support to affected areas.\n\n**February 2005**\n\n* The Indonesian government begins to rebuild and recover, with a focus on rebuilding infrastructure and providing support to affected communities.\n\n**March 2005**\n\n* The tsunami warning system is upgraded, with the Indian Ocean Tsunami Warning and Mitigation System (IOTWS) established to provide early warnings for future tsunamis.\n\n**Ongoing**\n\n* Recovery efforts continue, with many communities still rebuilding and recovering from the disaster.\n* The 2004 Indian Ocean earthquake and tsunami serves as a reminder of the importance of disaster preparedness and early warning systems.\n\nNote: All times are in Coordinated Universal Time (UTC) and local", token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 25845, 315, 279, 1401, 4455, 14932, 279, 220, 1049, 19, 7904, 22302, 38413, 323, 72155, 1473, 334, 33246, 220, 1627, 11, 220, 1049, 19, 57277, 9, 220, 410, 25, 2970, 25, 4331, 28503, 320, 2589, 25, 2970, 25, 4331, 2254, 892, 1680, 362, 11191, 1234, 37541, 38413, 449, 264, 26703, 315, 220, 24, 13, 16, 12, 24, 13, 18, 23170, 1022, 279, 13962, 315, 24922, 596, 18671, 17271, 315, 38807, 71, 11, 52605, 264, 11191, 72155, 627, 9, 220, 1721, 25, 410, 28503, 320, 2318, 25, 410, 2254, 892, 1680, 578, 72155, 17301, 3240, 311, 4295, 279, 13962, 315, 24922, 11, 14718, 24716, 19814, 323, 4814, 315, 2324, 382, 334, 33246, 220, 1627, 11, 220, 1049, 19, 320, 86957, 33395, 271, 9, 220, 1721, 25, 966, 28503, 320, 2318, 25, 966, 2254, 892, 1680, 578, 72155, 17301, 5662, 279, 13962, 