andard atmospheric pressure, while oil has a much higher boiling point, ranging from 150°C to 300°C (302°F to 572°F) depending on the type of oil.\n* **Reactivity:** Water is highly reactive and can react with many substances, including acids and bases. Oil, on the other hand, is relatively inert and does not react with many substances.\n* **Uses:** Water is essential for human consumption, agriculture, and many industrial processes, while oil is primarily used as a fuel source, lubricant, and raw material for the production of various products.\n\nIn summary, while water and oil share some similarities, they have many distinct differences in terms of their physical and chemical properties. Understanding these differences is important for a wide range of applications, from everyday life to industrial processes.", token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 2077, 430, 43565, 323, 83379, 3090, 323, 5707, 1473, 29353, 323, 5707, 527, 1403, 315, 279, 1455, 4279, 33155, 1766, 389, 9420, 11, 3686, 814, 617, 1690, 12062, 304, 3878, 315, 872, 7106, 323, 11742, 6012, 13, 5810, 527, 1063, 315, 279, 1925, 43874, 323, 12062, 1990, 279, 1403, 1473, 334, 35502, 1385, 25, 57277, 9, 11995, 3090, 323, 5707, 527, 67849, 520, 3130, 9499, 627, 9, 11995, 527, 2867, 323, 18300, 11, 10923, 3177, 311, 1522, 1555, 1124, 627, 9, 11995, 649, 387, 1766, 304, 7138, 11, 449, 3090, 1694, 264, 16595, 3777, 315, 279, 9420, 596, 26031, 323, 5707, 1694, 264, 5933, 5211, 28532, 505, 279, 5015, 382, 334, 35, 59426, 25, 57277, 9, 3146, 67819, 68063, 10164, 374, 39950, 261, 1109, 5707, 11, 449, 264, 17915, 315, 13489, 220, 16, 23882, 824, 2606, 321, 2058, 320, 70, 93422, 705, 1418, 5707, 706, 264, 17915, 315, 2212, 220, 15, 13, 23, 12, 15, 13, 24, 342, 93422, 627, 9, 3146, 3198, 86218, 68063, 15895, 374, 59884, 323, 810, 59665, 788, 1109, 3090, 11, 3339, 433, 810, 31785, 311, 6530, 13, 10164, 11, 389, 279, 1023, 1450, 11, 374, 65355, 323, 810, 15962, 627, 9, 3146, 49912, 392, 1429, 68063, 10164, 374, 264, 25685, 43030, 1