Output~2025-04-24 17:03:22.607068: [RequestOutput(request_id=833, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Come up with 3 tips for writing effective dialogue. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 15936, 709, 449, 220, 18, 10631, 369, 4477, 7524, 21976, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here are three tips for writing effective dialogue:\n\n**Tip 1: Listen to the way people speak**\n\nEffective dialogue should sound natural and authentic. To achieve this, pay attention to the way people speak in real life. Listen to the rhythm, cadence, and idioms of everyday conversation. Notice how people use contractions, filler words (like "um" or "like"), and colloquialisms. Incorporate these elements into your dialogue to make it sound more realistic.\n\n**Tip 2: Use subtext to add depth**\n\nDialogue can convey more than just the literal meaning of the words. Subtext refers to the underlying emotions, motivations, or intentions that characters may not explicitly state. Use subtext to add depth and complexity to your dialogue. For example, a character may say "I\'m fine" when they\'re actually upset or angry. This can create tension and interest in the conversation.\n\n**Tip 3: Vary sentence structure and length**\n\nDialogue should not be a series of monologues or a string of identical sentences. Vary the length and structure of your sentences to create a natural flow. Short, snappy sentences can convey excitement or urgency, while longer, more complex sentences can show a character\'s thoughtfulness or introspection. Mixing up the sentence structure can also help to create a sense of rhythm and make the dialogue more engaging to read.', token_ids=[8586, 527, 2380, 10631, 369, 4477, 7524, 21976, 1473, 334, 16394, 220, 16, 25, 33249, 311, 279, 1648, 1274, 6604, 57277, 68639, 21976, 1288, 5222, 5933, 323, 13513, 13, 2057, 11322, 420, 11, 2343, 6666, 311, 279, 1648, 1274, 6604, 304, 1972, 2324, 13, 33249, 311, 279, 37390, 11, 19973, 768, 11, 323, 41760, 7085, 315, 18254, 10652, 13, 25773, 1268, 1274, 1005, 6155, 4109, 11, 55810, 4339, 320, 4908, 330, 372, 1, 477, 330, 4908, 4063, 323, 82048, 447, 532, 13978, 13, 54804, 349, 1521, 5540, 1139, 701, 21976, 311, 1304, 433, 5222, 810, 26569, 382, 334, 16394, 220, 17, 25, 5560, 1207, 1342, 311, 923, 8149, 57277, 83990, 649, 20599, 810, 1109, 1120, 279, 24016, 7438, 315, 279, 4339, 13, 3804, 1342, 19813, 311, 279, 16940, 21958, 11, 65931, 11, 477, 34334, 430, 5885, 1253, 539, 21650, 1614, 13, 5560, 1207, 1342, 311, 923, 8149, 323, 23965, 311, 701, 21976, 13, 1789, 3187, 11, 264, 3752, 1253, 2019, 330, 40, 2846, 7060, 1, 994, 814, 2351, 3604, 23268, 477, 19021, 13, 1115, 649, 1893, 24408, 323, 2802, 304, 279, 10652, 382, 334, 16394, 220, 18, 25, 650, 661, 11914, 6070, 323, 3160, 57277, 83990, 1288, 539, 387, 264, 4101, 315, 1647, 1640, 1157, 477, 264, 925, 315, 20086, 23719, 13, 650, 661, 279, 3160, 323, 6070, 315, 701, 23719, 311, 1893, 264, 5933, 6530, 13, 10928, 11, 4224, 11392, 23719, 649, 20599, 28361, 477, 54917, 11, 1418, 5129, 11, 810, 6485, 23719, 649, 1501, 264, 3752, 596, 3463, 31514, 477, 26609, 16463, 13, 97699, 709, 279, 11914, 6070, 649, 1101, 1520, 311, 1893, 264, 5647, 315, 37390, 323, 1304, 279, 21976, 810, 23387, 311, 1373, 13, 128009], cumulative_logprob=None, logprobs=None, finish_reason=stop, stop_reason=None)], finished=True, metrics=None, lora_request=None, num_cached_tokens=None, multi_modal_placeholders={})]
