Output~2025-04-24 17:03:45.021042: [RequestOutput(request_id=840, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Describe the process of making a basic omelette and list 3 different ways to customize it. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 61885, 279, 1920, 315, 3339, 264, 6913, 297, 2727, 10010, 323, 1160, 220, 18, 2204, 5627, 311, 32187, 433, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="Here is a response that completes the request:\n\nMaking a basic omelette is a simple process that requires just a few ingredients and some basic cooking skills. Here's a step-by-step guide:\n\n**Basic Omelette Recipe:**\n\nIngredients:\n\n* 2 eggs\n* Salt and pepper to taste\n* 1 tablespoon butter or oil\n\nInstructions:\n\n1. Crack the eggs into a bowl and whisk them together with a fork until the whites and yolks are fully incorporated. Add a pinch of salt and pepper to taste.\n2. Heat a small non-stick pan over medium heat and add the butter or oil. Once the butter has melted or the oil is hot, pour in the egg mixture.\n3. Let the eggs cook for about 30 seconds until the edges start to set.\n4. Use a spatula to gently lift and fold the edges of the omelette towards the center, allowing the uncooked egg to flow to the edges.\n5. Continue cooking and folding the omelette for another 30-60 seconds, until the eggs are almost set.\n6. Use the spatula to fold the omelette in half or into a third, depending on your desired shape.\n7. Slide the omelette out of the pan onto a plate and serve hot.\n\n**Customizing Your Omelette:**\n\nHere are three different ways to customize your basic omelette:\n\n1. **Cheesy Delight:** Add shredded cheddar, mozzarella, or feta cheese to the eggs before cooking. You can also sprinkle some grated Parmesan on top of the omelette after it's cooked.\n2. **Veggie Delight:** Add diced bell peppers, onions, mushrooms, spinach, or any other vegetables you like to the eggs before cooking. You can also add some chopped fresh herbs like parsley or chives on top.\n3. **Meat Lover's Omelette:** Add diced ham, bacon, sausage, or cooked chicken to the eggs before cooking. You can also add some chopped fresh herbs like parsley or chives on top.\n\nThese are just a few ideas to get you started. Feel free to experiment with different fillings and toppings to create your own unique omelette creations!", token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 2077, 430, 45695, 279, 1715, 1473, 43346, 264, 6913, 297, 2727, 10010, 374, 264, 4382, 1920, 430, 7612, 1120, 264, 2478, 14293, 323, 1063, 6913, 17677, 7512, 13, 5810, 596, 264, 3094, 14656, 30308, 8641, 1473, 334, 16323, 507, 2727, 10010, 26371, 25, 57277, 46847, 1473, 9, 220, 17, 19335, 198, 9, 28138, 323, 25349, 311, 12945, 198, 9, 220, 16, 62611, 14432, 477, 5707, 271, 56391, 1473, 16, 13, 56045, 279, 19335, 1139, 264, 19763, 323, 41759, 1124, 3871, 449, 264, 23243, 3156, 279, 22632, 323, 94582, 2857, 527, 7373, 32762, 13, 2758, 264, 50346, 315, 12290, 323, 25349, 311, 12945, 627, 17, 13, 27162, 264, 2678, 2536, 5594, 875, 7363, 927, 11298, 8798, 323, 923, 279, 14432, 477, 5707, 13, 9843, 279, 14432, 706, 50459, 477, 279, 5707, 374, 4106, 11, 5019, 304, 279, 19151, 21655, 627, 18, 13, 6914, 279, 19335, 4394, 369, 922, 220, 966, 6622, 3156, 279, 13116, 1212, 311, 743, 627, 19, 13, 5560, 264, 63983, 5724, 311, 30373, 12157, 323, 11816, 279, 13116, 315, 279, 297, 2727, 10010, 7119, 279, 4219, 11, 10923, 279, 653, 99797, 19151, 311, 6530, 311, 279, 13116, 627, 20, 13, 15353, 17677, 323, 45842, 279, 297, 2727