Output~2025-04-24 17:06:09.923846: [RequestOutput(request_id=895, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Provide a plan to get good sleep each night. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 40665, 264, 3197, 311, 636, 1695, 6212, 1855, 3814, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="Here's a plan to help you get good sleep each night:\n\n**Step 1: Establish a Consistent Sleep Schedule**\n\n* Set a regular sleep schedule and stick to it, even on weekends. Go to bed and wake up at the same time every day.\n* Aim for 7-9 hours of sleep each night to help your body get the rest it needs.\n\n**Step 2: Create a Bedtime Routine**\n\n* Develop a calming pre-sleep routine to signal to your body that it's time to wind down. This can include activities such as:\n\t+ Reading a book or magazine\n\t+ Taking a warm bath or shower\n\t+ Practicing gentle stretches or yoga\n\t+ Listening to soothing music or nature sounds\n\t+ Writing in a journal or reflecting on your day\n\n**Step 3: Create a Sleep-Conducive Environment**\n\n* Make your bedroom a sleep haven by:\n\t+ Keeping it dark, quiet, and at a comfortable temperature\n\t+ Investing in a comfortable mattress and pillows\n\t+ Using blackout curtains, earplugs, or a white noise machine if necessary\n\t+ Removing electronic devices, such as TVs and computers, from the bedroom\n\n**Step 4: Avoid Stimulants Before Bed**\n\n* Avoid consuming caffeine, nicotine, and electronic screens (e.g., phones, tablets, or laptops) at least an hour before bedtime, as they can interfere with your ability to fall asleep.\n* Avoid heavy meals or heavy exercise within a few hours of bedtime, as they can disrupt your sleep.\n\n**Step 5: Limit Exposure to Blue Light**\n\n* Blue light, which is emitted by electronic devices, can suppress the production of melatonin, the hormone that regulates sleep. To minimize exposure:\n\t+ Use blue light filtering glasses, apps, or software\n\t+ Dim the brightness of your devices or use night mode\n\t+ Avoid using electronic devices at least an hour before bedtime\n\n**Step 6: Get Ready for Bed**\n\n* Brush your teeth, change into comfortable pajamas, and prepare your body for sleep.\n* Avoid stimulating activities, such as watching TV or engaging in intense conversations, within 30 minutes of bedtime.\n\n**Step 7: Practice Relaxation Techniques**\n\n* Try relaxation techniques, such as deep breathing, progressive muscle relaxation, or meditation, to help calm your mind and body before sleep.\n* Consider keeping a journal or writing down your thoughts and concerns to clear your mind before bed.\n\n**Step 8: Get Out of Bed**\n\n* If you", token_ids=[8586, 596, 264, 3197, 311, 1520, 499, 636, 1695, 6212, 1855, 3814, 1473, 334, 8468, 220, 16, 25, 40498, 264, 7440, 18620, 24708, 24416, 57277, 9, 2638, 264, 5912, 6212, 9899, 323, 9396, 311, 433, 11, 1524, 389, 38102, 13, 6122, 311, 4950, 323, 15508, 709, 520, 279, 1890, 892, 1475, 1938, 627, 9, 71715, 369, 220, 22, 12, 24, 4207, 315, 6212, 1855, 3814, 311, 1520, 701, 2547, 636, 279, 2800, 433, 3966, 382, 334, 8468, 220, 17, 25, 4324, 264, 13394, 1712, 72162, 57277, 9, 8000, 264, 78729, 864, 1355, 3583, 14348, 311, 8450, 311, 701, 2547, 430, 433, 596, 892, 311, 10160, 1523, 13, 1115, 649, 2997, 7640, 1778, 439, 512, 197, 10, 18242, 264, 2363, 477, 14756, 198, 197, 10, 36925, 264, 8369, 9061, 477, 17639, 198, 197, 10, 18373, 10332, 22443, 50699, 477, 27102, 198, 197, 10, 77797, 311, 65464, 4731, 477, 7138, 10578, 198, 197, 10, 2