Output~2025-04-24 17:06:32.016907: [RequestOutput(request_id=910, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Generate a piece of advice to someone who is feeling unmotivated. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 20400, 264, 6710, 315, 9650, 311, 4423, 889, 374, 8430, 38531, 354, 55786, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here\'s a piece of advice for someone who is feeling unmotivated:\n\n"Hey there, friend! I totally get it - sometimes life can feel overwhelming and it\'s hard to muster up the energy to do anything, let alone tackle that to-do list or pursue your passions. But here\'s the thing: you are not alone in this feeling. We all go through periods of unmotivation, and it\'s okay to acknowledge and accept it.\n\nFirst, take a deep breath and give yourself permission to feel this way. Don\'t beat yourself up over it or try to push through it - that usually just makes things worse. Instead, take a step back and ask yourself what\'s really going on. Is it burnout, stress, or something else? Once you identify the root cause, you can start to address it.\n\nNext, take small steps towards doing something you enjoy. It doesn\'t have to be a grand, monumental task - just something that brings you a tiny bit of joy. Whether it\'s reading a chapter in a book, taking a short walk, or cooking a favorite meal, do something that feels good. This can help shift your mood and give you a sense of accomplishment.\n\nRemember, motivation is like a muscle that needs to be exercised. The more you use it, the stronger it gets. So, start small and build up gradually. Celebrate your tiny wins, and don\'t be too hard on yourself if you don\'t see immediate results.\n\nLastly, be kind to yourself and acknowledge that it\'s okay to not be okay. You\'re doing the best you can, and that\'s something to be proud of. Keep in mind that this too shall pass, and the motivation will come back around. Until then, take care of yourself and focus on the present moment.\n\nYou got this, friend!"', token_ids=[8586, 596, 264, 6710, 315, 9650, 369, 4423, 889, 374, 8430, 38531, 354, 55786, 1473, 1, 19182, 1070, 11, 4333, 0, 358, 12756, 636, 433, 482, 7170, 2324, 649, 2733, 22798, 323, 433, 596, 2653, 311, 84750, 709, 279, 4907, 311, 656, 4205, 11, 1095, 7636, 22118, 430, 311, 30659, 1160, 477, 23564, 701, 58724, 13, 2030, 1618, 596, 279, 3245, 25, 499, 527, 539, 7636, 304, 420, 8430, 13, 1226, 682, 733, 1555, 18852, 315, 38531, 354, 40227, 11, 323, 433, 596, 17339, 311, 25670, 323, 4287, 433, 382, 5451, 11, 1935, 264, 5655, 11745, 323, 3041, 6261, 8041, 311, 2733, 420, 1648, 13, 4418, 956, 9567, 6261, 709, 927, 433, 477, 1456, 311, 4585, 1555, 433, 482, 430, 6118, 1120, 3727, 2574, 11201, 13, 12361, 11, 1935, 264, 3094, 1203, 323, 2610, 6261, 1148, 596, 2216, 2133, 389, 13, 2209, 433, 8395, 412, 11, 8631, 11, 477, 2555, 775, 30, 9843, 499, 10765, 279, 3789, 5353, 11, 499, 649, 1212, 311, 2686, 433, 382, 5971, 11, 1935, 2678, 7504, 7119, 3815, 2555, 499, 4774, 13, 1102, 3250, 956, 617, 311, 387, 264, 6800, 11, 78856, 3465, 482, 1120, 2555, 430, 12716, 499, 264, 13987, 2766, 315, 16267, 13, 13440, 433, 596, 5403, 264, 12735, 304, 264, 2363, 11, 4737, 264, 2875, 4321, 11, 477, 17677, 264, 7075, 15496, 11, 656, 2555, 430, 11321, 1695, 13, 1115, 649, 1520, 6541, 701, 20247, 323, 3041, 499, 264, 5647, 315, 61238, 382, 29690, 11, 25835, 374, 1093, 264, 16124, 430, 3966, 311, 387, 62113, 13, 578, 810, 499, 1005, 433, 11, 279, 16643, 433, 5334, 13, 2100, 11, 1