Output~2025-04-24 17:09:10.251659: [RequestOutput(request_id=967, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Generate a list of tips to improve metabolism. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 20400, 264, 1160, 315, 10631, 311, 7417, 39097, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here are some tips to help improve your metabolism:\n\n**1.** **Stay Hydrated**: Drinking plenty of water throughout the day can help boost your metabolism by increasing the amount of calories you burn. Aim for at least 8-10 glasses of water per day.\n\n**2.** **Eat Protein-Rich Foods**: Protein takes more energy to digest than carbohydrates or fat, which can help increase your metabolism. Include protein-rich foods like lean meats, fish, eggs, tofu, and legumes in your diet.\n\n**3.** **Incorporate HIIT (High-Intensity Interval Training)**: HIIT workouts have been shown to increase metabolism and burn more calories than traditional cardio exercises. Try incorporating short bursts of intense exercise into your routine.\n\n**4.** **Get Enough Sleep**: Lack of sleep can slow down your metabolism, so aim for 7-9 hours of sleep per night to help keep your metabolism running smoothly.\n\n**5.** **Eat More Fiber**: Fiber can help speed up digestion and increase metabolism. Include fiber-rich foods like fruits, vegetables, whole grains, and legumes in your diet.\n\n**6.** **Strength Train**: Building muscle through strength training can help increase your resting metabolic rate, which can help you burn more calories at rest.\n\n**7.** **Eat More Spicy Foods**: Spicy foods can increase your metabolism by increasing your body temperature and heart rate. Try incorporating spicy dishes into your meals.\n\n**8.** **Get Enough Vitamin D**: Vitamin D deficiency has been linked to a slower metabolism. Spend time outdoors, take vitamin D supplements, or eat vitamin D-rich foods like fatty fish, egg yolks, and mushrooms.\n\n**9.** **Avoid Processed Foods**: Processed foods are often high in sugar, salt, and unhealthy fats, which can slow down your metabolism. Opt for whole, unprocessed foods instead.\n\n**10.** **Get Enough Omega-3 Fatty Acids**: Omega-3 fatty acids have been shown to increase metabolism and improve overall health. Find omega-3 rich foods like salmon, walnuts, and chia seeds in your diet.\n\nRemember, a healthy metabolism is just one part of overall health. Combine these tips with a balanced diet and regular exercise for optimal results.', token_ids=[8586, 527, 1063, 10631, 311, 1520, 7417, 701, 39097, 1473, 334, 16, 13, 334, 3146, 39202, 10320, 3696, 660, 96618, 83681, 11510, 315, 3090, 6957, 279, 1938, 649, 1520, 7916, 701, 39097, 555, 7859, 279, 3392, 315, 25247, 499, 8395, 13, 71715, 369, 520, 3325, 220, 23, 12, 605, 29247, 315, 3090, 824, 1938, 382, 334, 17, 13, 334, 3146, 89711, 49475, 11151, 718, 40160, 96618, 49475, 5097, 810, 4907, 311, 21552, 1109, 62345, 477, 8834, 11, 902, 649, 1520, 5376, 701, 39097, 13, 30834, 13128, 41947, 15657, 1093, 16025, 63875, 11, 7795, 11, 19335, 11, 80247, 11, 323, 2531, 19131, 304, 701, 10173, 382, 334, 18, 13, 334, 3146, 644, 6133, 61721, 34511, 964, 320, 12243, 12, 77982, 41684, 16543, 33395, 25, 34511, 964, 46944, 617, 1027, 6982, 311, 5376, 39097, 323, 8395, 810, 25247, 1109, 8776, 32844, 23783, 13, 9934, 52913, 2875, 66801, 315, 19428, 10368, 1139, 701, 14348, 382, 334, 19, 13, 334, 3146, 1991, 62692, 24708, 96618, 68502, 315, 6212, 649, 6435, 1523, 701, 39097, 11, 779, 9395, 369, 220, 22, 12, 24, 42