Output~2025-04-24 17:09:28.329482: [RequestOutput(request_id=974, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Calculate the area of a triangle with sides measuring 8cm, 5cm, and 6cm. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 21157, 279, 3158, 315, 264, 22217, 449, 11314, 30090, 220, 23, 6358, 11, 220, 20, 6358, 11, 323, 220, 21, 6358, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="To calculate the area of a triangle, we need to use Heron's formula, which is:\n\nArea = √(s(s-a)(s-b)(s-c))\n\nwhere s is the semi-perimeter, and a, b, and c are the lengths of the sides.\n\nFirst, we need to calculate the semi-perimeter:\n\ns = (a + b + c) / 2\n= (8 + 5 + 6) / 2\n= 19 / 2\n= 9.5\n\nNow, we can plug in the values into Heron's formula:\n\nArea = √(9.5(9.5-8)(9.5-5)(9.5-6))\n= √(9.5 × 1.5 × 4.5 × 3.5)\n= √(103.25 × 16.25)\n= √1675\n= 40.5 cm²\n\nTherefore, the area of the triangle is 40.5 cm².", token_ids=[1271, 11294, 279, 3158, 315, 264, 22217, 11, 584, 1205, 311, 1005, 6385, 263, 596, 15150, 11, 902, 374, 1473, 8900, 284, 122371, 7, 82, 1161, 7561, 2432, 82, 1481, 2432, 82, 1824, 4489, 2940, 274, 374, 279, 18768, 17453, 26402, 11, 323, 264, 11, 293, 11, 323, 272, 527, 279, 29416, 315, 279, 11314, 382, 5451, 11, 584, 1205, 311, 11294, 279, 18768, 17453, 26402, 1473, 82, 284, 320, 64, 489, 293, 489, 272, 8, 611, 220, 17, 198, 28, 320, 23, 489, 220, 20, 489, 220, 21, 8, 611, 220, 17, 198, 28, 220, 777, 611, 220, 17, 198, 28, 220, 24, 13, 20, 271, 7184, 11, 584, 649, 20206, 304, 27