Output~2025-04-24 17:12:17.344986: [RequestOutput(request_id=1062, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Write a function that censors curse words inside a string. It takes those curse words from an SQL database. The curse words table is called CURSE_WORDS_TABLE. The curse word column is called WORD. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 9842, 264, 734, 430, 272, 27627, 41100, 4339, 4871, 264, 925, 13, 1102, 5097, 1884, 41100, 4339, 505, 459, 8029, 4729, 13, 578, 41100, 4339, 2007, 374, 2663, 19058, 937, 89521, 16424, 13, 578, 41100, 3492, 3330, 374, 2663, 37991, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here is a Python function that censors curse words inside a string by taking the curse words from an SQL database:\n```\nimport sqlite3\n\ndef censor_curse_words(input_string):\n    # Connect to the database\n    conn = sqlite3.connect(\'curse_words.db\')\n    cursor = conn.cursor()\n\n    # Query the curse words from the database\n    cursor.execute("SELECT WORD FROM CURSE_WORDS_TABLE")\n    curse_words = [row[0] for row in cursor.fetchall()]\n\n    # Censor the curse words in the input string\n    for curse_word in curse_words:\n        input_string = input_string.replace(curse_word, \'*\' * len(curse_word))\n\n    # Return the censored string\n    return input_string\n```\nHere\'s an explanation of the code:\n\n1. We connect to the SQLite database using the `sqlite3` library.\n2. We query the `CURSE_WORDS_TABLE` table and retrieve the list of curse words.\n3. We iterate through the curse words and replace each one in the input string with a string of asterisks (`*`) of the same length as the curse word.\n4. We return the censored string.\n\nNote that this function assumes that the curse words are stored in a single column called `WORD` in the `CURSE_WORDS_TABLE` table, and that the input string is a single string. You may need to modify the function to accommodate different table and column names, or to handle multiple input strings.', token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 13325, 734, 430, 272, 27627, 41100, 4339, 4871, 264, 925, 555, 4737, 279, 41100, 4339, 505, 459, 8029, 4729, 512, 14196, 4077, 475, 22775, 18, 271, 755, 40065, 19492, 325, 19518, 5498, 3991, 997, 262, 674, 13313, 311, 279, 4729, 198, 262, 4635, 284, 22775, 18, 11034, 493, 2407, 325, 19518, 7221, 1329, 262, 8291, 284, 4635, 21361, 2892, 262, 674, 11615, 279, 41100, 4339, 505, 279, 4729, 198, 262, 8291, 7925, 446, 4963, 37991, 4393, 19058, 937, 89521, 16424, 1158, 262, 41100, 19518, 284, 510, 654, 58, 15, 60, 369, 2872, 304, 8291, 43230, 93208, 262, 674, 356, 3890, 279, 41100, 4339, 304, 279, 1988, 925, 198, 262, 369, 41100, 13843, 304, 41100, 19518, 512, 286, 1988, 3991, 284, 1988, 3991, 7125, 18053, 325, 13843, 11, 31801, 353, 2479, 18053, 325, 13843, 4489, 262, 674, 3494, 279, 272, 56878, 925, 198, 262, 471, 1988, 3991, 198, 14196, 4077, 8586, 596, 459, 16540, 315, 279, 2082, 1473, 16, 13, 1226, 4667, 311, 279, 29434, 4729, 1701, 279, 1595, 38142, 18, 63, 6875, 627, 17, 13, 1226, 3319, 279, 1595, 39891, 937, 89521, 16424, 63, 2007, 323, 17622, 279, 1160, 315, 41100, 4339, 627, 18, 13, 1226, 30729, 1555, 279, 41100, 4339, 323, 8454, 1855, 832, 304, 279, 1988, 925, 449, 264, 925, 315, 35037, 93934, 29754, 9, 33981, 315, 279, 1890, 3160, 439, 279, 41100, 3492, 627, 19, 13, 1226, 471, 279, 272, 56878, 925, 382, 9290, 430, 420, 734, 22204, 430, 279, 41100, 4339, 527, 9967, 304, 264, 3254, 3330, 2663, 1595, 7375, 63, 304, 279, 1595, 39891, 937, 89521, 16424, 63, 