ill output:\n\n```\nexample.com\n```\n\nThis is because the regex "example\\\\.com" matches the string "example.com" in the input string. The `\\\\.` in the regex is an escaped dot, which matches a literal dot in the string.', token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 8102, 734, 430, 5829, 279, 1595, 16137, 63, 323, 1595, 38654, 63, 6989, 311, 1505, 682, 9248, 315, 264, 2728, 20791, 4871, 264, 925, 1473, 74694, 10248, 198, 475, 1674, 2013, 44218, 77552, 280, 475, 1674, 2013, 44218, 53126, 401, 898, 538, 4802, 341, 262, 586, 1118, 742, 1925, 2292, 1318, 2897, 8, 341, 286, 935, 610, 284, 330, 2028, 374, 459, 3187, 925, 449, 459, 2686, 3788, 1129, 2185, 7880, 916, 15656, 286, 935, 20791, 284, 330, 8858, 68257, 884, 886, 286, 1194, 43570, 4293, 11, 20791, 317, 262, 557, 262, 586, 1118, 742, 1194, 43570, 2292, 610, 11, 935, 20791, 8, 341, 286, 19365, 5497, 284, 19365, 19458, 62657, 317, 286, 61732, 37152, 284, 5497, 50327, 4293, 317, 286, 1418, 320, 71926, 2725, 2189, 341, 310, 744, 2594, 2986, 26473, 261, 6306, 1449, 286, 457, 262, 457, 534, 14196, 19884, 4599, 499, 1629, 420, 2068, 11, 433, 690, 2612, 1473, 14196, 4077, 8858, 916, 198, 14196, 19884, 2028, 374, 1606, 279, 20791, 330, 8858, 68257, 884, 1, 9248, 279, 925, 330, 8858, 916, 1, 304, 279, 1988, 925, 13, 578, 1595, 3505, 15254, 304, 279, 20791, 374, 459, 28883, 13046, 11, 902, 9248, 264, 24016, 13046, 304, 279, 925, 13, 128009], cumulative_logprob=None, logprobs=None, finish_reason=stop, stop_reason=None)], finished=True, metrics=None, lora_request=None, num_cached_tokens=None, multi_modal_placeholders={})]
