Output~2025-04-24 17:14:48.312433: [RequestOutput(request_id=1136, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: List two benefits of using design thinking. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 1796, 1403, 7720, 315, 1701, 2955, 7422, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="Here is a response that completes the request:\n\nTwo benefits of using design thinking are:\n\n1. **Improved Problem-Solving**: Design thinking encourages a human-centered approach to problem-solving, which helps to identify and address the needs and desires of the end-user. This leads to more effective and innovative solutions that are tailored to the specific needs of the target audience. By considering the user's perspective, design thinking helps to develop solutions that are more user-friendly, intuitive, and effective.\n2. **Increased Creativity and Innovation**: Design thinking fosters a culture of creativity and experimentation, which enables individuals to think outside the box and come up with novel solutions. By embracing failure as a learning opportunity and encouraging experimentation, design thinking helps to build a culture of innovation and continuous improvement. This leads to the development of new and innovative products, services, and experiences that can give organizations a competitive edge in the market.", token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 2077, 430, 45695, 279, 1715, 1473, 11874, 7720, 315, 1701, 2955, 7422, 527, 1473, 16, 13, 3146, 82210, 22854, 6354, 20222, 96618, 7127, 742