Output~2025-04-24 17:15:00.476534: [RequestOutput(request_id=1142, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: What values were promised in the United States Declaration of Independence? ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 3639, 2819, 1051, 19487, 304, 279, 3723, 4273, 42021, 315, 44177, 30, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="The United States Declaration of Independence, adopted on July 4, 1776, is a foundational document of American history that outlines the principles and values that the thirteen American colonies declared as the basis for their independence from Great Britain. The document promises several values, including:\n\n1. **Life**: The right to life is considered an unalienable right, meaning it cannot be taken away by any government or individual.\n2. **Liberty**: The document asserts the right to liberty, which includes the freedom to make choices and live one's life as one sees fit, as long as it does not infringe on the rights of others.\n3. **Pursuit of Happiness**: The Declaration of Independence states that individuals have the right to pursue their own happiness, which is often interpreted as the right to pursue one's own goals, dreams, and aspirations.\n4. **Equality**: The document asserts that all men are created equal, meaning that all individuals have the same inherent value and worth, regardless of their social status, wealth, or position.\n5. **Unalienable Rights**: The Declaration of Independence states that these three values - life, liberty, and the pursuit of happiness - are unalienable, meaning they cannot be taken away by any government or individual.\n6. **Consent of the Governed**: The document asserts that government derives its power from the consent of the governed, meaning that government exists to serve the people, not the other way around.\n7. **Protection of Individual Rights**: The Declaration of Independence promises that the government will protect the individual rights of its citizens, including the right to life, liberty, and the pursuit of happiness.\n\nThese values have had a profound impact on American history and continue to shape American society and politics to this day.", token_ids=[791, 3723, 4273, 42021, 315, 44177, 11, 18306, 389, 5887, 220, 19, 11, 220, 11242, 21, 11, 374, 264, 89328, 2246, 315, 3778, 3925, 430, 50729, 279, 16565, 323, 2819, 430, 279, 61759, 3778, 49028, 14610, 439, 279, 8197, 369, 872, 24589, 505, 8681, 13527, 13, 578, 2246, 21300, 3892, 2819, 11, 2737, 1473, 16, 13, 3146, 26833, 96618, 578, 1314, 311, 2324, 374, 6646, 459, 653, 56418, 481, 1314, 11, 7438, 433, 4250, 387, 4529, 3201, 555, 904, 3109, 477, 3927, 627, 17, 13, 3146, 9374, 1368, 96618, 578, 2246, 57876, 279, 1314, 311, 31220, 11, 902, 5764, 279, 11542, 311, 1304, 11709, 323, 3974, 832, 596, 2324, 439, 832, 16008, 5052, 11, 439, 1317, 439, 433, 1587, 539, 25654, 18177, 389, 279, 3268, 315, 3885, 627, 18, 13, 3146, 47, 1759, 3159, 315, 79244, 96618, 578, 42021, 315, 44177, 5415, 430, 7931, 617, 279, 1314, 311, 23564, 872, 1866, 23871, 11, 902, 374, 3629, 33398, 439, 279, 1314, 311, 23564, 832, 596, 1866, 9021, 11, 19226, 11, 323, 58522, 627, 19, 13, 3146, 51845, 96618, 578, 2246, 57876, 430, 682, 3026, 527, 3549, 6273, 11, 7438, 430, 682, 7931, 617, 279, 1890, 38088, 907, 323, 5922, 11, 15851, 315, 872, 3674, 2704, 11, 12205, 11, 477, 2361, 627, 20, 13, 3146, 1844, 56418, 481, 10734, 96618, 578, 42021, 315, 44177, 5415, 430, 1521, 2380, 2819, 482, 2324, 11, 31220, 11, 323, 279, 33436,