Output~2025-04-24 17:20:39.507046: [RequestOutput(request_id=1284, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Write an original story with a beginning, middle, and end. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 9842, 459, 4113, 3446, 449, 264, 7314, 11, 6278, 11, 323, 842, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here is an original story with a beginning, middle, and end:\n\n**The Mysterious Library**\n\nAs I pushed open the creaky door, a warm golden light spilled out onto the street, beckoning me to enter. The sign above the entrance read "The Whispering Pages," and I had heard whispers of its existence for years. Rumors of a library that held the secrets of the past, where books came alive and stories unfolded like magic. I had to see it for myself.\n\nAs I stepped inside, the door creaked shut behind me, and I was enveloped in the musty scent of old parchment and leather. The air was thick with the whispers of forgotten tales, and I felt a shiver run down my spine. The room was dimly lit, with rows upon rows of shelves stretching towards the ceiling, each one packed tightly with books of every shape and size.\n\nI wandered the aisles, running my fingers over the spines of the books, feeling the raised letters and intricate illustrations. The titles seemed to whisper secrets in my ear, drawing me deeper into the stacks. I stumbled upon a section dedicated to ancient myths and legends, and my eyes landed on a book bound in worn, supple leather. The cover was adorned with a golden symbol that seemed to pulse with a soft, blue light.\n\nAs I opened the book, the pages crackled with age, releasing a puff of dust into the air. The words within were written in a language I didn\'t recognize, but as I touched the page, the text began to shift, rearranging itself into a language I could understand. The story unfolded before me, a tale of a great hero who had braved the unknown to retrieve a powerful artifact.\n\nAs I read on, the room around me began to fade away, and I found myself standing in the midst of the hero\'s journey. I walked alongside him, feeling the weight of his quest, as we navigated treacherous landscapes and battled fearsome creatures. The story was alive, and I was a part of it.\n\nWhen I finally emerged from the book, the room was quiet once more, the whispers of the library hushed. I closed the book, feeling changed, as if I had been a part of something greater than myself. As I left the Whispering Pages, I knew that I would return, for I had discovered a secret: the stories within these walls were not just words on a page, but doorways to other worlds, waiting to be explored.\n\n**The', token_ids=[8586, 374, 459, 4113, 3446, 449, 264, 7314, 11, 6278, 11, 323, 842, 1473, 334, 791, 386, 97499, 11896, 57277, 2170, 358, 15753, 1825, 279, 272, 1127, 88, 6134, 11, 264, 8369, 21411, 3177, 74125, 704, 8800, 279, 8761, 11, 92186, 20324, 757, 311, 3810, 13, 578, 1879, 3485, 279, 20396, 1373, 330, 791, 98074, 287, 22521, 1359, 323, 358, 1047, 6755, 89248, 315, 1202, 14209, 369, 1667, 13, 46332, 1105, 315, 264, 6875, 430, 5762, 279, 24511, 315, 279, 3347, 11, 1405, 6603, 3782, 13989, 323, 7493, 76782, 1093, 11204, 13, 358, 1047, 311, 1518, 433, 369, 7182, 382, 2170, 358, 25319, 4871, 11, 279, 6134, 272, 1127, 291, 9495, 4920, 757, 11, 323, 358, 574, 54285, 291, 304, 279, 2011, 88, 41466, 315, 2362, 87204, 323, 18012, 13, 578, 3805, 574, 12314, 449, 279, 89248, 315, 25565, 37565, 11, 323, 358, 6612, 264, 559, 1553, 1629, 