Output~2025-04-24 17:22:54.628259: [RequestOutput(request_id=1344, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Tell me a horror story that takes place in an abandoned house. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 25672, 757, 264, 22169, 3446, 430, 5097, 2035, 304, 459, 23838, 3838, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='As I stepped out of the car and onto the crumbling driveway, a shiver ran down my spine. The once-grand Victorian mansion loomed before me, its turrets and gargoyles reaching towards the moon like skeletal fingers. The wind whispered secrets in my ear, and I could feel the weight of years of neglect and decay settling upon me.\n\nI had always been drawn to the abandoned house on the hill, despite the warnings from the townsfolk. They called it the "Devil\'s Den," and whispered tales of strange occurrences and unexplained noises that echoed through its empty halls. But I was a skeptic, a seeker of truth and reason. I had to see it for myself.\n\nAs I approached the entrance, I noticed that the front door hung crookedly on its hinges, as if it had been forced open by some unseen hand. I pushed it creaking open, and stepped inside.\n\nThe air inside was thick with dust and the stench of rot. Cobwebs clung to the chandeliers, and the walls were covered in a thick layer of grime. I fumbled for my flashlight and turned it on, casting flickering shadows across the walls.\n\nAs I explored the ground floor, I began to feel a creeping sense of unease. Every creak of the floorboards, every groan of the old wooden beams, made me jump. I told myself it was just my imagination, but deep down, I knew something was off.\n\nI made my way upstairs, my heart pounding in my chest. The stairs creaked beneath my feet, and I could have sworn I heard a faint whispering in my ear. "Get out while you still can." I spun around, but there was no one there.\n\nThe second floor was a labyrinth of narrow corridors and dark, musty rooms. I stumbled upon a nursery, the walls adorned with faded wallpaper and a crib that seemed to stare at me like an empty eye socket. I felt a chill run down my spine as I realized that this was where the children had once slept.\n\nAs I turned to leave, I heard a faint cry. It was a child\'s voice, high-pitched and desperate. I spun around, my heart racing, and followed the sound to a door at the end of the hall. It was slightly ajar, and I pushed it open with a sense of trepidation.\n\nInside, I found a room that seemed frozen in time. A child\'s toys and clothes were scattered across the floor, and a rocking chair sat', token_ids=[2170, 358, 25319, 704, 315, 279, 1841, 323, 8800, 279, 89417, 53242, 11, 264, 559, 1553, 10837, 1523, 856, 35776, 13, 578, 3131, 72102, 44277, 52528, 781, 25111, 1603, 757, 11, 1202, 259, 88434, 323, 97183, 2303, 645, 19261, 7119, 279, 18266, 1093, 69397, 19779, 13, 578, 10160, 58366, 24511, 304, 856, 2487, 11, 323, 358, 1436, 2733, 279, 4785, 315, 1667, 315, 39332, 323, 31815, 52945, 5304, 757, 382, 40, 1047, 2744, 1027, 15107, 311, 279, 23838, 3838, 389, 279, 24898, 11, 8994, 279, 19530, 505, 279, 25861, 42031, 13, 2435, 2663, 433, 279, 330, 14934, 321, 596, 9973, 1359, 323, 58366, 37565, 315, 15234, 57115, 323, 653, 81950, 58448, 430, 55212, 1555, 1202, 4384, 52473, 13, 2030, 358, 574, 264, 55950, 11, 264, 90233, 315, 8206, 323, 2944, 13, 358, 1047, 311, 1518, 433, 369, 7182, 382, 2170, 358, 25735, 279, 20396, 11, 358, 14000, 430, 279, 4156, 6134, 18799, 14425, 11059, 398, 389