rdict, which is met with widespread approval from the white community.\n\nThe novel takes a dramatic turn when Bob Ewell, Mayella\'s father and the man who accused Tom, attempts to attack Scout and Jem one night. However, Boo Radley, a reclusive neighbor who has been the subject of local legend and rumors, intervenes and saves the children. In the process, Bob Ewell is killed, and Boo is injured.\n\nAs the story concludes, Scout and her father reflect on the events of the trial and the loss of innocence that has occurred. Atticus\'s defense of Tom has taught Scout and Jem valuable lessons about empathy, compassion, and the importance of doing what is right in the face of overwhelming opposition. The novel ends with Scout realizing that Boo Radley, who has become a symbol of kindness and redemption, has been watching over her and her brother throughout the story, and that he is not the monster she had imagined him to be.', token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 10015, 7234, 12399, 315, 279, 11775, 330, 1271, 27933, 264, 14905, 287, 23414, 1, 555, 33107, 12336, 1473, 1681, 304, 279, 18682, 4987, 2391, 279, 220, 7285, 15, 82, 11, 330, 1271, 27933, 264, 14905, 287, 23414, 1, 374, 264, 11670, 11775, 430, 41424, 4819, 315, 19739, 51215, 11, 25065, 11, 323, 279, 4814, 315, 57311, 13, 578, 3446, 374, 3309, 1555, 279, 6548, 315, 48635, 96333, 11, 264, 3995, 3828, 889, 6439, 449, 1077, 9191, 10868, 622, 336, 323, 872, 7126, 11, 7867, 59344, 11, 304, 279, 44682, 6424, 315, 3297, 22631, 11, 21272, 382, 791, 3446, 19169, 2212, 279, 9269, 315, 8529, 28280, 11, 264, 3776, 893, 889, 374, 61456, 13487, 315, 87546, 264, 4251, 5333, 11, 3297, 6985, 469, 9336, 13, 7867, 59344, 11, 264, 15779, 889, 374, 3967, 369, 813, 51841, 323, 17025, 11, 34008, 311, 10726, 8529, 8994, 14392, 568, 3358, 3663, 48786, 323, 61029, 505, 279, 4029, 13, 1666, 279, 9269, 20414, 11, 48635, 323, 622, 336, 4048, 922, 279, 98753, 1238, 17011, 555, 11904, 9053, 304, 872, 4029, 323, 279, 5655, 7962, 660, 19739, 39510, 430, 3