Output~2025-04-24 17:24:42.912621: [RequestOutput(request_id=1373, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Outline the steps to make an apple pie. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 53009, 279, 7504, 311, 1304, 459, 24149, 4447, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here is the outline of steps to make an apple pie:\n\n**Step 1: Prepare the Ingredients**\n\n* Gather the following ingredients:\n\t+ 2-3 varieties of apples, peeled and sliced\n\t+ 1 cup granulated sugar\n\t+ 2 tablespoons all-purpose flour\n\t+ 1 teaspoon cinnamon\n\t+ 1/4 teaspoon nutmeg\n\t+ 1/4 teaspoon salt\n\t+ 1/2 cup cold unsalted butter, cut into small pieces\n\t+ 1 egg, beaten\n\t+ 1 tablespoon milk\n\t+ 1 pie crust (homemade or store-bought)\n\n**Step 2: Make the Filling**\n\n* In a large bowl, combine the sliced apples, granulated sugar, flour, cinnamon, nutmeg, and salt. Mix until the apples are evenly coated with the dry ingredients.\n* Add the cold butter to the apple mixture and toss until the apples are well-coated with the butter.\n\n**Step 3: Roll Out the Pie Crust**\n\n* If using homemade pie crust, roll it out to a thickness of about 1/8 inch. If using store-bought pie crust, follow the package instructions for thawing and rolling out the crust.\n* Place the rolled-out pie crust into a 9-inch pie dish, trimming any excess crust from the edges.\n\n**Step 4: Fill the Pie Crust**\n\n* Fill the pie crust with the apple mixture, mounding it slightly in the center.\n* Dot the top of the apple mixture with the beaten egg and sprinkle with a little milk.\n\n**Step 5: Top with Another Pie Crust (Optional)**\n\n* If desired, roll out another piece of pie crust to fit the top of the pie. Place the rolled-out pie crust on top of the apple mixture and crimp the edges to seal the pie.\n* Cut a few slits in the top crust to allow steam to escape during baking.\n\n**Step 6: Bake the Pie**\n\n* Preheat the oven to 375°F (190°C).\n* Place the pie on a baking sheet lined with parchment paper and bake for 40-50 minutes, or until the crust is golden brown and the apples are tender.\n* Let the pie cool on a wire rack for at least 30 minutes before serving.\n\nEnjoy your delicious homemade apple pie!', token_ids=[8586, 374, 279, 21782, 315, 7504, 311, 1304, 459, 24149, 4447, 1473, 334, 8468, 220, 16, 25, 32266, 279, 52275, 57277, 9, 50095, 279, 2768, 14293, 512, 197, 10, 220, 17, 12, 18, 36680, 315, 41776, 11, 83612, 323, 48715, 198, 197, 10, 220, 16, 10747, 16109, 7913, 13465, 198, 197, 10, 220, 17, 56588, 682, 59338, 20415, 198, 197, 10, 220, 16, 42384, 51992, 198, 197, 10, 220, 16, 14, 19, 42384, 10184, 71376, 198, 197, 10, 220, 16, 14, 19, 42384, 12290, 198, 197, 10, 220, 16, 14, 17, 10747, 9439, 7120, 62334, 14432, 11, 4018, 1139, 2678, 9863, 198, 197, 10, 220, 16, 19151, 11, 31394, 198, 197, 10, 220, 16, 62611, 14403, 198, 197, 10, 220, 16, 4447, 40712, 320, 35940, 29532, 477, 3637, 1481, 2509, 696, 334, 8468, 220, 17, 25, 7557, 279, 435, 9585, 57277, 9, 763, 264, 3544, 19763, 11, 16343, 279, 48715, 41776, 11, 16109, 7913, 13465, 11, 20415, 11, 51992, 11, 10184, 71376, 11, 323, 12290, 13, 19771, 3156, 279, 41776, 527, 42147, 49482, 449, 279, 9235, 14293, 627, 9, 2758, 279, 9439, 14432, 311, 279, 24149, 21655, 323, 26251, 3156, 279, 41776, 527, 1664, 23283, 660, 449, 279, 14432, 382, 334, 8468, 220, 18, 25, 15028, 4470, 279, 41097, 4656, 592, 57277, 9, 1442, 1701, 36433, 4447, 40712, 11, 6638, 433, 704, 311, 264, 26839, 315, 922, 220, 16, 14, 23, 1