Output~2025-04-24 17:26:22.781450: [RequestOutput(request_id=1416, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: The Happy Valley Kennel has 4 chickens, 2 dogs, and 5 cats. (Some people in Happy Valley like to keep chickens as pets!) In how many ways can the 11 animals be placed in a row of 11 cages, such that all of the animals of each type are in adjacent cages? (Two animals of the same species are considered distinguishable.) ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 578, 24241, 13345, 15739, 301, 706, 220, 19, 54623, 11, 220, 17, 12875, 11, 323, 220, 20, 19987, 13, 320, 8538, 1274, 304, 24241, 13345, 1093, 311, 2567, 54623, 439, 26159, 16715, 763, 1268, 1690, 5627, 649, 279, 220, 806, 10099, 387, 9277, 304, 264, 2872, 315, 220, 806, 81947, 11, 1778, 430, 682, 315, 279, 10099, 315, 1855, 955, 527, 304, 24894, 81947, 30, 320, 11874, 10099, 315, 279, 1890, 9606, 527, 6646, 33137, 481, 6266, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="A classic problem!\n\nLet's break it down step by step:\n\n1. We have 4 chickens, 2 dogs, and 5 cats, for a total of 11 animals.\n2. We want to arrange them in a row of 11 cages, such that all animals of each type are in adjacent cages.\n3. We can start by arranging the 3 types of animals in any order. There are 3! = 6 ways to do this:\n\t* (Chickens, Dogs, Cats)\n\t* (Chickens, Cats, Dogs)\n\t* (Dogs, Chickens, Cats)\n\t* (Dogs, Cats, Chickens)\n\t* (Cats, Chickens, Dogs)\n\t* (Cats, Dogs, Chickens)\n4. Now, for each of these arrangements, we need to arrange the animals within each group. For example, if we have (Chickens, Dogs, Cats), we need to arrange the 4 chickens, 2 dogs, and 5 cats within their respective groups.\n5. For the chickens, there are 4! = 24 ways to arrange them.\n6. For the dogs, there are 2! = 2 ways to arrange them.\n7. For the cats, there are 5! = 120 ways to arrange them.\n8. Since these arrangements are independent, we multiply the number of ways for each group: 24 × 2 × 120 = 5760.\n9. Finally, we multiply this result by the number of ways to arrange the 3 types of animals (6): 5760 × 6 = 34560.\n\nTherefore, there are 34560 ways to place the 11 animals in a row of 11 cages, such that all animals of each type are in adjacent cages.", token_ids=[32, 11670, 3575, 2268, 10267, 596, 1464, 433, 1523, 3094, 555, 3094, 1473, 16, 13, 1226, 617, 220, 19, 54623, 11, 220, 17, 12875, 11, 323, 220, 20, 19987, 11, 369, 264, 2860, 315, 220, 806, 10099, 627, 17, 13, 1226, 1390, 311, 31993, 1124, 304, 264, 2872, 315, 220, 806, 81947, 11, 1778, 430, 682, 10099, 315, 1855, 955, 527, 304, 24894, 81947, 627, 18, 13, 1226, 649, 1212, 555, 77218, 279, 220, 18, 4595, 315, 10099, 304, 904, 2015, 13, 2684, 527, 220, 18, 0, 284, 220, 21, 5627, 311, 656, 420, 512, 197, 9, 320, 1163, 875, 729, 11, 39525, 11, 51849, 340, 197, 9, 320, 1163, 875, 729, 11, 51849, 11, 39525, 340, 197, 9, 320, 35, 27403, 11, 63226, 729, 11, 51849, 340, 197, 9, 320, 35, 27403, 11, 51849, 11, 63226, 729, 340, 197, 9, 320, 34, 1900, 11, 63226, 729, 11, 39525, 340, 197, 9, 320, 34, 1900, 11, 39525, 11, 63226, 729, 340, 19, 13, 4800, 11, 369, 1855, 315, 1521, 28904, 11, 584, 1205, 311, 31993, 279, 10099, 2949, 1855, 1912, 13, 1789, 3187, 11, 422, 584, 617, 320, 1163, 875, 729, 11, 39525, 11, 51849, 705, 584, 1205, 311, 31993, 279, 220, 19, 54623, 11, 220, 17, 12875, 11, 323, 220, 20, 19987, 2949, 872, 20081, 5315, 627, 20, 13, 1789, 279, 54623, 11, 1070, 527, 220, 19, 0, 284, 220, 1187, 5627, 311, 31993, 1124, 627, 21, 13, 1789, 279, 12