h generates the output text. The decoder uses the output from the encoder to predict the next token in the sequence.\n4. **Output Layer:** The final output is a sequence of tokens, which are then decoded back into human-readable text.\n\n**Training:**\n\nGPT-3 is trained on a massive dataset of text, which is sourced from the internet. The model is trained using a process called masked language modeling, where some of the input tokens are randomly replaced with a special [MASK] token. The model is then trained to predict the original token that was replaced.\n\n**How it Works:**\n\nWhen you input a prompt or text into GPT-3, the model uses its training data to generate a response. Here's a high-level overview of the process:\n\n1. **Tokenization:** The input text is tokenized into individual words or characters.\n2. **Encoder:** The input tokens are passed through the encoder layers, which process the input sequence and generate a contextualized representation.\n3. **Decoder:** The output from the encoder is passed through the decoder layer, which generates a sequence of tokens based on the input.\n4. **Output:** The final output is a sequence of tokens, which are decoded back into human-readable text.\n\nGPT-3's ability to generate human-like text is due", token_ids=[334, 4438, 12838, 480, 2898, 12, 18, 5664, 30, 57277, 38, 2898, 12, 18, 320, 5648, 1413, 5075, 70024, 63479, 220, 18, 8, 374, 264, 4221, 1646, 8040, 555, 16197, 15592, 430, 706, 14110, 1534, 279, 2115, 315, 5933, 4221, 8863, 320, 45, 12852, 570, 1102, 596, 264, 955, 315, 43678, 6108, 30828, 4009, 430, 649, 7068, 3823, 12970, 1495, 3196, 389, 279, 1988, 433, 21879, 13, 5810, 596, 264, 44899, 16540, 315, 1268, 433, 4375, 1473, 334, 92051, 25, 57277, 38, 2898, 12, 18, 374, 264, 43678, 6108, 1646, 11, 902, 3445, 433, 596, 5918, 1701, 264, 955, 315, 30828, 4009, 2663, 264, 43678, 13, 1115, 18112, 374, 8104, 1664, 87229, 1639, 369, 8863, 52100, 828, 1093, 1495, 13, 578, 1646, 17610, 315, 3892, 13931, 11, 185