Output~2025-04-24 17:28:17.054234: [RequestOutput(request_id=1472, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Name three types of machine learning algorithms. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 4076, 2380, 4595, 315, 5780, 6975, 26249, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here are three types of machine learning algorithms:\n\n1. **Linear Regression**: This algorithm is used for predicting a continuous output variable based on one or more input features. It is commonly used for regression tasks, such as predicting house prices or stock prices.\n2. **Decision Trees**: This algorithm is used for both classification and regression tasks. It works by splitting the data into subsets based on the values of the input features, and then making predictions based on the majority vote of the subsets.\n3. **Support Vector Machines (SVMs)**: This algorithm is used for classification and regression tasks. It works by finding the hyperplane that maximally separates the classes in the feature space, and then making predictions based on which side of the hyperplane the new data point falls on.', token_ids=[8586, 527, 2380, 4595, 315, 5780, 6975, 26249, 1473, 16, 13, 3146, 32998, 48570, 96618, 1115, 12384, 374, 1511, 369, 52997, 264, 19815, 2612, 3977, 3196, 389, 832, 477, 810, 1988, 4519, 13, 1102, 374, 17037, 1511, 369, 31649, 9256, 11, 1778, 439, 52997, 3838, 7729, 477, 5708, 7729, 627, 17, 13, 3146, 75946, 59984, 96618, 1115, 12384, 374, 1511, 369, 2225, 24790, 323, 31