Output~2025-04-24 17:28:18.897434: [RequestOutput(request_id=1473, prompt='<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{"Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Determine the meaning of the word \'bemused\'. ### Response:"}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n', prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 5018, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 31001, 279, 7438, 315, 279, 3492, 364, 65, 336, 2656, 4527, 17010, 6075, 3047, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='The word "bemused" is an adjective that means being puzzled or perplexed, often in a mild or amused way. It can also imply a sense of being confused or disoriented, but in a non-serious or even playful manner.\n\nFor example, if someone is watching a complex or absurd situation unfold, they might be described as being "bemused" by it. Alternatively, if someone is trying to understand a difficult concept or idea, they might be "bemused" by the complexity of it.\n\nIn general, "bemused" is a polite way to describe a state of being puzzled or confused, without implying that the person is frustrated or upset. It\'s often used to convey a sense of gentle curiosity or amusement at something that is unexpected or unclear.', token_ids=[791, 3492, 330, 65, 336, 2656, 1, 374, 459, 85592, 430, 3445, 1694, 87420, 477, 74252, 291, 11, 3629, 304, 264, 23900, 477, 86324, 1648, 13, 1102, 649, 1101, 34608, 264, 5647, 315, 1694, 22568, 477, 834, 33536, 11, 719, 304, 264, 2536, 26469, 1245, 477, 1524, 57169, 11827, 382, 2520, 3187, 11, 422, 4423, 374, 10307, 264, 6485, 477, 32677, 6671, 28572, 11, 814, 2643, 387, 7633, 439, 1694, 330, 65, 336, 2656, 1, 555, 433, 13, 39578, 11, 422, 4423, 374, 45