Output~2025-04-24 17:29:18.791423: [RequestOutput(request_id=1503, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Explain the rules of the game Soccer. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 83017, 279, 5718, 315, 279, 1847, 38633, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="Here's a comprehensive explanation of the rules of soccer:\n\n**Objective:**\nThe objective of soccer is to score more goals than the opposing team by kicking or heading the ball into the opponent's goal.\n\n**Gameplay:**\n\n1. **Number of Players:** Each team consists of 11 players, including a goalkeeper.\n2. **Game Length:** A standard game is divided into two 45-minute halves, with a 15-minute halftime break in between.\n3. **Ball in and Out of Play:** The ball is out of play when it crosses the goal line or touchline, or when the referee stops play. The ball is in play when it is within the field boundaries.\n4. **Scoring:** A goal is scored when the ball passes entirely over the goal line between the goal posts and under the crossbar.\n5. **Ball Handling:** Players can use any part of their body except their hands and arms to control and move the ball. Goalkeepers are allowed to use their hands and arms to touch the ball within their own penalty area.\n6. ** Fouls:** If a player commits a foul, such as tripping or pushing an opponent, the other team is awarded a free kick. If the foul is more serious, such as tackling an opponent from behind, the opposing team may be awarded a penalty kick.\n7. **Free Kicks:** A free kick is taken from where the foul occurred. The ball must be stationary and kicked forward.\n8. **Penalty Kicks:** A penalty kick is taken from the penalty spot, 12 yards from the goal. The ball must be kicked forward and the goalkeeper must remain on the goal line until the ball is kicked.\n9. **Offside:** A player is offside if they are closer to the opponent's goal line than both the ball and the second-to-last opponent when the ball is played forward.\n10. **Restarts:** The game can be restarted with a kickoff, throw-in, or corner kick, depending on how the ball went out of play.\n11. **Substitutions:** Teams can make three substitutions per game, and players who are substituted out cannot re-enter the game.\n\n**Referee:**\nThe referee is responsible for enforcing the rules and keeping track of the game clock. They can award free kicks, penalty kicks, and yellow or red cards for misconduct.\n\n**Yellow and Red Cards:**\nA yellow card is given for a minor offense, such as unsportsmanlike conduct. A player who receives two yellow cards is given a red", token_ids=[8586, 596, 264, 16195, 16540, 315, 279, 5718, 315, 22963, 1473, 334, 79406, 25, 1035, 791, 16945, 315, 22963, 374, 311, 5573, 810, 9021, 1109, 279, 31322, 2128, 555, 40294, 477, 14836, 279, 5041, 1139, 279, 15046, 596, 5915, 382, 334, 4973, 1387, 25, 57277, 16, 13, 3146, 2903, 315, 25640, 68063, 9062, 2128, 17610, 315, 220, 806, 4311, 11, 2737, 264, 63300, 627, 17, 13, 3146, 4973, 17736, 68063, 362, 5410, 1847, 374, 18255, 1139, 1403, 220, 1774, 24401, 75212, 11, 449, 264, 220, 868, 24401, 79559, 1464, 304, 1990, 627, 18, 13, 3146, 37007, 304, 323, 4470, 315, 7199, 68063, 578, 5041, 374, 704, 315, 1514, 994, 433, 50535, 279, 5915, 1584, 477, 5916, 1074, 11, 477, 994, 279, 55302, 18417, 1514, 13, 578, 5041, 374, 304, 1514, 994, 433, 374, 2949, 279, 2115, 23546, 627, 19, 13, 3146, 3407, 5620, 68063, 362, 5915, 374, 16957, 994, 279, 5041, 16609, 11622, 927, 279, 5915, 1584, 1990, 27