Output~2025-04-24 17:33:31.936489: [RequestOutput(request_id=1596, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Identify the major flaws in the following code snippet. ### Input: def add_numbers(x,y):\\n    return x+y\\n\\nadd_numbers(2) ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 11, 35526, 449, 459, 1988, 430, 5825, 4726, 2317, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 65647, 279, 3682, 41859, 304, 279, 2768, 2082, 44165, 13, 17010, 5688, 25, 711, 923, 34064, 2120, 7509, 90149, 77, 262, 471, 865, 44110, 1734, 1734, 723, 34064, 7, 17, 8, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='The major flaws in the given code snippet are:\n\n1. The function `add_numbers` is defined but it is not being called with two arguments. The function is expecting two numbers to be added, but only one number `2` is being passed.\n\n2. The function `add_numbers` is not handling the case where the input is not a number. If a non-numeric value is passed to the function, it will raise a TypeError.\n\nHere is the corrected code:\n\n```\ndef add_numbers(x, y):\n    if not isinstance(x, (int, float)) or not isinstance(y, (int, float)):\n        raise TypeError("Both inputs must be numbers")\n    return x + y\n\nprint(add_numbers(2, 3))  # This will print 5\n```\n\nIn this corrected code, the function `add_numbers` now checks if both inputs are numbers before attempting to add them. If either input is not a number, it raises a TypeError with a message indicating that both inputs must be numbers.', token_ids=[791, 3682, 41859, 304, 279, 2728, 2082, 44165, 527, 1473, 16, 13, 578, 734, 1595, 723, 34064, 63, 374, 4613, 719, 433, 374, 539, 1694, 2663, 449, 1403, 6105, 13, 578, 734, 374, 23132, 1403, 5219, 311, 387, 3779, 11, 719, 1193, 832, 1396, 1595, 17, 63, 374, 1694, 5946, 382, 17, 13, 578, 734, 1595, 723, 34064, 63, 374, 539, 11850, 279, 1162, 1405, 279, 1988, 374, 539, 264, 1396, 13, 1442, 264, 2536, 12, 20173, 907, 374, 5946, 311, 279, 734, 11, 433, 690, 4933, 264, 26082, 382, 8586, 374, 279, 37065, 2082, 1473, 14196, 4077, 755, 923, 34064, 2120, 11, 379, 997, 262, 422, 539, 11656, 2120, 11, 320, 396, 11, 2273, 595, 477, 539, 11656, 7166, 11, 320, 396, 11, 2273, 10162, 286, 4933, 26082, 446, 21279, 11374, 2011, 387, 5219, 1158, 262, 471, 865, 489, 379, 271, 1374, 26995, 34064, 7, 17, 11, 220, 18, 595, 220, 674, 1115, 690, 1194, 220, 20, 198, 14196, 19884, 644, 420, 37065, 2082, 11, 279, 734, 1595, 723, 34064, 63, 1457, 12621, 422, 2225, 11374, 527, 5219, 1603, 19969, 311, 923, 1124, 13, 1442, 3060, 1988, 374, 539, 264, 1396, 11, 433, 25930, 264, 26082, 449, 264, 1984, 19392, 430, 2225, 11374, 2011, 387, 5219, 13, 128009], cumulative_logprob=None, logprobs=None, finish_reason=stop, stop_reason=None)], finished=True, metrics=None, lora_request=None, num_cached_tokens=None, multi_modal_placeholders={})]
