wed argument, as the truth of a claim is not determined by the number of people who believe it, but rather by evidence and logical reasoning.\n\nAdditionally, this fallacy is also related to the Bandwagon Fallacy, which is a type of fallacy that occurs when someone assumes that a claim is true because many people are doing it or believe it, without considering the evidence or logical reasoning.\n\nIn conclusion, the statement is committing the Appeal to Popularity fallacy, and it is not a valid argument.', token_ids=[791, 5224, 330, 12608, 919, 315, 1274, 4510, 430, 12512, 48473, 706, 6928, 6372, 389, 872, 2890, 323, 1664, 33851, 11, 779, 433, 2011, 387, 837, 1, 42635, 279, 4498, 2826, 315, 62006, 311, 10466, 30079, 382, 2028, 4498, 2826, 13980, 994, 4423, 22204, 430, 279, 8206, 477, 32939, 315, 264, 3802, 374, 11075, 555, 279, 1396, 315, 1274, 889, 4510, 433, 11, 4856, 1109, 555, 6029, 477, 20406, 33811, 13, 763, 420, 1162, 11, 279, 5224, 374, 73967, 430, 1120, 1606, 1690, 1274, 4510, 430, 12512, 48473, 706, 6928, 6372, 389, 872, 2890, 323, 1664, 33851, 11, 433, 2011, 387, 837, 13, 4452, 11, 420, 374, 264, 48008, 5811, 11, 439, 279, 8206, 315, 264, 3802, 374, 539, 11075, 555, 279, 1396, 315, 1274, 889, 4510, 433, 11, 719, 4856, 555, 6029, 323, 20406, 33811, 382, 50674, 11, 420, 4498, 2826, 374, 1101, 5552, 311, 279, 17366, 94219, 15128, 2826, 11, 902, 374, 264, 955, 315, 4498, 2826, 430, 13980, 994, 4423, 22204, 430, 264, 3802, 374, 837, 1606, 1690, 1274, 527, 3815, 433, 477, 4510, 433, 11, 2085, 13126, 279, 6029, 477, 20406, 33811, 382, 644, 17102, 11, 279, 5224, 374, 40583, 279, 62006, 311, 10466, 30079, 4498, 2826, 11, 323, 433, 374, 539, 264, 2764, 5811, 13, 128009], cumulative_logprob=None, logprobs=None, finish_reason=stop, stop_reason=None)], finished=True, metrics=None, lora_request=None, num_cached_tokens=None, multi_modal_placeholders={})]
