The mood shifts to one of wonder and enchantment.\n* "No happiness can it bring": This line brings the mood back down to earth, introducing a sense of melancholy and despair. The word "no" is a strong negation, emphasizing the idea that the beauty of the snow is not enough to bring happiness. The mood is now somber and reflective.\n* "It buries in my trance": This final line creates a sense of disconnection and isolation. The word "buries" implies a sense of being overwhelmed and consumed by the cold, and the phrase "in my trance" suggests a state of numbness and disconnection from the world. The mood is one of desolation and despair.\n\nOverall, the poem takes the reader on a journey from a sense of unease and discomfort to a sense of wonder and enchantment, and finally to a sense of desolation and despair. The different moods are expertly crafted to create a sense of tension and release, drawing the reader into the world of the poem.', token_ids=[791, 33894, 18911, 264, 43120, 323, 3721, 511, 1413, 4096, 315, 264, 12688, 6237, 11, 449, 1855, 1584, 29820, 311, 264, 12742, 20247, 13, 5810, 596, 264, 31085, 315, 1268, 1855, 1584, 11705, 264, 2204, 20247, 1473, 9, 330, 4599, 9439, 2136, 1922, 7270, 856, 6930, 794, 1115, 1584, 7437, 279, 16630, 369, 279, 33894, 11, 33018, 264, 5647, 315, 37401, 323, 44776, 13, 578, 3492, 330, 846, 7270, 1, 24897, 264, 6435, 323, 1672, 80227, 30215, 315, 9439, 2136, 11, 902, 11705, 264, 5647, 315, 6316, 521, 323, 24408, 13, 578, 20247, 374, 1794, 655, 323, 2291, 65, 3785, 627, 9, 330, 1820, 12056, 1344, 324, 4108, 1093, 264, 15612, 794, 1115, 1584, 374, 264, 38246, 13168, 311, 279, 3766, 832, 11, 33018, 264, 5647, 315, 3177, 2136, 323, 7351, 13, 578, 3492, 330, 1517, 324, 4108, 1, 374, 57169, 323, 70205, 950, 11, 323, 279, 12593, 311, 264, 15612, 13533, 264, 2512, 10816, 323, 83212, 16975, 13, 578, 20247, 29735, 311, 832, 315, 5895, 323, 48025, 479, 627, 9, 330, 2822, 23871, 649, 433, 4546, 794, 1115, 1584, 12716, 279, 20247, 1203, 1523