Output~2025-04-24 17:38:04.568854: [RequestOutput(request_id=1674, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Write a brief biography of Marie Curie ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 9842, 264, 10015, 48345, 315, 33116, 13182, 648, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="Here is a brief biography of Marie Curie:\n\nMarie Curie (1867-1934) was a Polish-born physicist and chemist who made groundbreaking discoveries in the fields of radioactivity and nuclear physics. Born Maria Skłodowska in Warsaw, Poland, she was the fifth of seven children to Władysław Skłodowski, a physics teacher, and Bronisława Skłodowska, a teacher of mathematics and literature. Marie's early education was in a secret school for girls, as education for women was limited in Poland at the time.\n\nIn 1891, Marie traveled to Paris to continue her education at the Sorbonne University, where she met her future husband, Pierre Curie. The couple began working together on research projects, and in 1897, they discovered the elements polonium and radium. Their work on radioactivity led to the isolation of these elements, which was a major breakthrough in the field of physics.\n\nMarie Curie's pioneering work earned her numerous awards and accolades, including two Nobel Prizes, one in physics in 1903 and another in chemistry in 1911. She was the first woman to win a Nobel Prize, and the first person to win two Nobel Prizes in different fields.\n\nThroughout her career, Marie Curie was a trailblazer for women in science. She was the first woman to become a professor at the University of Paris and the first woman to be elected to the French Academy of Sciences. Her legacy extends beyond her scientific achievements, as she paved the way for future generations of women in science and inspired countless individuals to pursue careers in research and academia.\n\nMarie Curie's life was marked by tragedy, including the loss of her husband Pierre in 1906 and her daughter Irène Joliot-Curie, who died of leukemia caused by her own exposure to radiation. Despite these challenges, Marie continued to work tirelessly until her own death in 1934, leaving behind a legacy that continues to inspire and influence scientists around the world.", token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 10015, 48345, 315, 33116, 13182, 648, 1473, 12331, 648, 13182, 648, 320, 9714, 22, 12, 7285, 19, 8, 574, 264, 33084, 40260, 83323, 323, 8590, 380, 889, 1903, 64955, 54098, 304, 279, 5151, 315, 9063, 7323, 323, 11499, 22027, 13, 38916, 23880, 4923, 4697, 347, 4336, 4657, 304, 73276, 11, 28702, 11, 1364, 574, 279, 18172, 315, 8254, 2911, 311, 468, 45971, 1065, 98348, 4923, 4697, 347, 29384, 11, 264, 22027, 11326, 11, 323, 20407, 285, 4697, 14406, 4923, 4697, 347, 4336, 4657, 11, 264, 11326, 315, 38696, 323, 17649, 13, 33116, 596, 4216, 6873, 574, 304, 264, 6367, 2978, 369, 7724, 11, 439, 6873, 369, 3278, 574, 7347, 304, 28702, 520, 279, 892, 382, 644, 220, 9378, 16, 11, 33116, 31796, 311, 12366, 311, 3136, 1077, 6873, 520, 279, 30631, 6098, 818, 3907, 11, 1405, 1364, 2322, 1077, 3938, 10177, 11, 38077, 13182, 648, 13, 578, 5743, 6137, 3318, 3871, 389, 3495, 7224, 11, 323, 304, 220, 9378, 22, 11, 814, 11352, 279, 5540, 1499, 90344, 323, 9038, 2411, 13, 11205, 990, 389, 9063, 7323, 6197, 311, 279, 31398, 315, 1521, 5540, 11, 902, 574, 264, 3682, 42445, 304, 279, 2115, 315, 22027, 382, 12331, 648, 13182, 648, 596, 71674, 990, 15662, 1077, 12387, 23146, 323, 86643, 3536, 11, 2737, 1403, 48078, 2394, 4861, 11, 832, 304, 22