Output~2025-04-24 17:39:26.324175: [RequestOutput(request_id=1701, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Identify and describe the different types tropical storms ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 65647, 323, 7664, 279, 2204, 4595, 35148, 44583, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here is a response that completes the request:\n\nTropical storms are a type of severe weather phenomenon that occurs over the warm waters of the Atlantic Ocean, Caribbean Sea, and the Gulf of Mexico. There are several types of tropical storms, which are classified based on their wind speed and potential damage. Here are the different types of tropical storms:\n\n1. **Tropical Depression**: A tropical depression is a rotating low-pressure system with maximum sustained winds of 38 mph (33 knots) or less. It is characterized by a circular motion and a closed circulation. Tropical depressions are not strong enough to cause significant damage, but they can still bring heavy rainfall and strong winds.\n2. **Tropical Storm**: A tropical storm is a rotating low-pressure system with maximum sustained winds of 39-73 mph (34-63 knots). It is characterized by a circular motion and a closed circulation. Tropical storms can cause significant damage, including flooding, power outages, and property damage.\n3. **Hurricane**: A hurricane is a rotating low-pressure system with maximum sustained winds of 74 mph (64 knots) or higher. It is characterized by a circular motion and a closed circulation. Hurricanes are the most destructive type of tropical storm, causing catastrophic damage and loss of life.\n4. **Typhoon**: A typhoon is a tropical cyclone that occurs in the western Pacific Ocean. It is similar to a hurricane, but is referred to as a typhoon in the western Pacific. Typhoons are characterized by strong winds, heavy rainfall, and storm surges.\n5. **Cyclone**: A cyclone is a tropical cyclone that occurs in the Indian Ocean and the southern Pacific Ocean. It is similar to a hurricane or typhoon, but is referred to as a cyclone in these regions. Cyclones are characterized by strong winds, heavy rainfall, and storm surges.\n6. **Tropical Cyclone**: A tropical cyclone is a general term that refers to any rotating low-pressure system that forms over warm ocean waters. It can include tropical depressions, tropical storms, hurricanes, typhoons, and cyclones.\n\nIn summary, tropical storms are classified based on their wind speed and potential damage. The different types of tropical storms include tropical depressions, tropical storms, hurricanes, typhoons, cyclones, and tropical cyclones. Each type of storm has its own characteristics and potential impact on the affected areas.', token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 2077, 430, 45695, 279, 1715, 1473, 51, 51172, 44583, 527, 264, 955, 315, 15748, 9282, 25885, 430, 13980, 927, 279, 8369, 21160, 315, 279, 23179, 22302, 11, 35374, 15379, 11, 323, 279, 27945, 315, 12550, 13, 2684, 527, 3892, 4595, 315, 35148, 44583, 11, 902, 527, 21771, 3196, 389, 872, 10160, 4732, 323, 4754, 5674, 13, 5810, 527, 279, 2204, 4595, 315, 35148, 44583, 1473, 16, 13, 3146, 51, 51172, 46904, 96618, 362, 35148, 18710, 374, 264, 42496, 3428, 89561, 1887, 449, 7340, 29759, 29592, 315, 220, 1987, 35061, 320, 1644, 61317, 8, 477, 2753, 13, 1102, 374, 32971, 555, 264, 28029, 11633, 323, 264, 8036, 35855, 13, 71343, 39300, 919, 527, 539, 3831, 3403, 311, 5353, 5199, 5674, 11, 719, 814, 649, 2103, 4546, 8987, 53958, 323, 3831, 29592, 627, 17, 13, 3