Output~2025-04-24 17:42:37.987136: [RequestOutput(request_id=1765, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Tell me something interesting about the language of birdsong. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 25672, 757, 2555, 7185, 922, 279, 4221, 315, 20229, 647, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='What a fascinating topic! Did you know that the language of birdsong is incredibly complex and nuanced? In fact, some species of birds have been found to have vocabularies that rival those of primates and even humans! For example, the song of the northern cardinal, a common North American bird, consists of over 20 different notes, which can be combined in various ways to convey different meanings. In fact, researchers have identified over 200 distinct songs in the repertoire of a single male cardinal, which he uses to communicate with potential mates, warn off rivals, and even signal the location of food sources.\n\nBut that\'s not all - birdsong is also incredibly melodic and musical. Many species have been found to have a sense of rhythm and pitch, and some even have a concept of harmony. For example, the song of the zebra finch, a small bird found in the deserts of Australia, consists of a series of melodic phrases that are sung in a specific order, with a clear beginning, middle, and end. And get this - the finch\'s song is so complex that it\'s been described as having a "musical structure" that\'s similar to human music!\n\nBut what\'s truly remarkable about birdsong is its ability to convey information. In addition to the obvious functions of attracting a mate or warning off predators, birdsong has been found to convey information about everything from the location of food sources to the presence of predators. For example, some species of birds will change their song in response to changes in their environment, such as the arrival of a new predator or the presence of a rival bird. And some species have even been found to have a "dialect" that\'s specific to their geographic region, similar to human languages!\n\nSo there you have it - the language of birdsong is a truly remarkable and complex phenomenon that\'s still not fully understood. But one thing is clear: it\'s a language that\'s full of beauty, complexity, and nuance, and it\'s a reminder of the incredible diversity and adaptability of the natural world.', token_ids=[3923, 264, 27387, 8712, 0, 14910, 499, 1440, 430, 279, 4221, 315, 20229, 647, 374, 17235, 6485, 323, 82891, 30, 763, 2144, 11, 1063, 9606, 315, 20229, 617, 1027, 1766, 311, 617, 24757, 1299, 552, 430, 21425, 1884, 315, 9036, 988, 323, 1524, 12966, 0, 1789, 3187, 11, 279, 5609, 315, 279, 18671, 56980, 11, 264, 4279, 4892, 3778, 12224, 11, 17610, 315, 927, 220, 508, 2204, 8554, 11, 902, 649, 387, 11093, 304, 5370, 5627, 311, 20599, 2204, 50800, 13, 763, 2144, 11, 12074, 617, 11054, 927, 220, 1049, 12742, 11936, 304, 279, 77768, 315, 264, 3254, 8762, 56980, 11, 902, 568, 5829, 311, 19570, 449, 4754, 55616, 11, 8985, 1022, 35938, 11, 323, 1524, 8450, 279, 3813, 315, 3691, 8336, 382, 4071, 430, 596, 539, 682, 482, 20229, 647, 374, 1101, 17235, 10804, 53860, 323, 18273, 13, 9176, 9606, 617, 1027, 1766, 311, 617, 264, 5647, 315, 37390, 323, 9846, 11, 323, 1063, 1524, 617, 264, 7434, 315, 26348, 13, 1789, 3187, 11, 279, 5609, 315, 279, 1167, 51313, 1913, 331, 11, 264, 2678, 12224, 1766, 304, 279, 951, 15916, 315, 8494, 11, 17610, 315, 264, 4101, 315, 10804, 53860, 32847, 430, 527, 40439, 304, 264, 323