Output~2025-04-24 17:45:35.330702: [RequestOutput(request_id=1841, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: 23 people attend a party. Each person shakes hands with at most 22 other people. What is the maximum possible number of handshakes, assuming that any two people can shake hands at most once? ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 220, 1419, 1274, 9604, 264, 4717, 13, 9062, 1732, 63130, 6206, 449, 520, 1455, 220, 1313, 1023, 1274, 13, 3639, 374, 279, 7340, 3284, 1396, 315, 1450, 939, 2094, 11, 26619, 430, 904, 1403, 1274, 649, 27116, 6206, 520, 1455, 3131, 30, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="Let's analyze the situation:\n\nEach person can shake hands with at most 22 other people, so the total number of handshakes that each person can make is 22.\n\nSince there are 23 people, the total number of handshakes that can be made is the sum of the number of handshakes each person can make, which is:\n\n23 people × 22 handshakes/person = 506 handshakes\n\nHowever, this is an overcount, because each handshake involves two people. To avoid double-counting, we need to divide the total number of handshakes by 2:\n\n506 handshakes ÷ 2 = 253 handshakes\n\nTherefore, the maximum possible number of handshakes is 253.", token_ids=[10267, 596, 24564, 279, 6671, 1473, 4959, 1732, 649, 27116, 6206, 449, 520, 1455, 220, 1313, 1023, 1274, 11, 779, 279, 2860, 1396, 315, 1450, 939, 2094, 430, 1855, 1732, 649, 1304, 374, 220, 1313, 382, 12834, 1070, 527, 220, 1419, 1274, 11, 2