Output~2025-04-24 17:50:23.086557: [RequestOutput(request_id=1958, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Write a story about a talking dog. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 9842, 264, 3446, 922, 264, 7556, 5679, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Once upon a time, in a small town surrounded by rolling hills and green pastures, there lived a dog like no other. His name was Max, and he was a golden retriever with a fluffy coat and a wagging tail that never seemed to stop. But what made Max truly special was that he could talk.\n\nAs a puppy, Max had stumbled upon a magical bone that granted him the gift of speech. At first, his owners, the Smiths, were shocked and amazed by this newfound ability. They would sit for hours, listening to Max\'s tales of chasing squirrels and playing fetch.\n\nAs Max grew older, he became a beloved fixture in the community. People would come from all over to hear him tell stories and share his wisdom. Max\'s favorite topic was the importance of kindness and compassion. He would regale his audience with tales of helping those in need, from rescuing kittens from trees to comforting the lonely.\n\nOne day, a severe storm rolled in, bringing heavy rain and strong winds. The Smiths\' house was flooded, and they were forced to evacuate. Max, being the loyal companion he was, refused to leave their side. He swam through the chest-deep water, his tail wagging bravely, as he guided his family to safety.\n\nAs they huddled together in the shelter, Max began to tell a story. "You see, my friends," he said, "in times of trouble, it\'s easy to get scared and lose hope. But that\'s when we must dig deep and find the courage to face the storm head-on. Just like I did today, we must swim against the currents and keep moving forward."\n\nThe Smiths and the other evacuees were inspired by Max\'s words. They hugged him tightly, grateful for his bravery and wisdom. As the storm passed, the sun broke through the clouds, casting a warm glow over the town. Max, exhausted but triumphant, curled up beside his family, his tail still wagging softly.\n\nFrom that day on, Max was known as the hero of the town. His story was told and retold, inspiring generations to come. And as he grew old and grey, his words of wisdom continued to guide those around him, reminding them that even in the darkest of times, there is always hope and always a way forward.', token_ids=[12805, 5304, 264, 892, 11, 304, 264, 2678, 6424, 23712, 555, 20700, 35231, 323, 6307, 3347, 1439, 11, 1070, 12439, 264, 5679, 1093, 912, 1023, 13, 5414, 836, 574, 7639, 11, 323, 568, 574, 264, 21411, 10992, 424, 449, 264, 68661, 23724, 323, 264, 65425, 3252, 9986, 430, 2646, 9508, 311, 3009, 13, 2030, 1148, 1903, 7639, 9615, 3361, 574, 430, 568, 1436, 3137, 382, 2170, 264, 42289, 11, 7639, 1047, 50157, 5304, 264, 24632, 17685, 430, 11938, 1461, 279, 8352, 315, 8982, 13, 2468, 1176, 11, 813, 7980, 11, 279, 9259, 82, 11, 1051, 27718, 323, 46304, 555, 420, 94621, 5845, 13, 2435, 1053, 2503, 369, 4207, 11, 14624, 311, 7639, 596, 37565, 315, 43931, 47050, 54883, 323, 5737, 7963, 382, 2170, 7639, 14264, 9191, 11, 568, 6244, 264, 28530, 12790, 304, 279, 4029, 13, 9029, 1053, 2586, 505, 682, 927, 311, 6865, 1461, 3371, 7493, 323, 4430, 813, 24278, 13, 7639, 596, 7075, 8712, 574, 279, 12939, 315, 45972, 323, 30481, 13, 1283, 1053, 1239, 1604, 813, 10877, 449, 37565, 315, 10695, 1884, 304, 1205, 11, 505, 13208, 7623, 83190, 505, 12690, 311, 69130, 279, 40666,