Output~2025-04-24 17:54:39.324899: [RequestOutput(request_id=2045, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Write an efficient function to check if an integer is a prime number. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 9842, 459, 11297, 734, 311, 1817, 422, 459, 7698, 374, 264, 10461, 1396, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="Here is an efficient function to check if an integer is a prime number:\n```\ndef is_prime(n):\n    if n <= 1:\n        return False\n    for i in range(2, int(n ** 0.5) + 1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            return False\n    return True\n```\nHere's an explanation of the code:\n\n1. If `n` is less than or equal to 1, it's not a prime number, so we return `False`.\n2. We only need to check divisibility up to the square root of `n`, because if `n` is divisible by a number greater than its square root, it would have already been caught by a smaller divisor. We use `int(n ** 0.5) + 1` to calculate the upper bound.\n3. We iterate from 2 to the upper bound, and for each `i`, we check if `n` is divisible by `i` using the modulo operator (`n % i == 0`). If it is, `n` is not a prime number, so we return `False`.\n4. If we reach the end of the loop without finding a divisor, `n` is a prime number, so we return `True`.\n\nThis function has a time complexity of O(√n), which is much faster than checking all the way up to `n` (which would have a time complexity of O(n)).", token_ids=[8586, 374, 459, 11297, 734, 311, 1817, 422, 459, 7698, 374, 264, 10461, 1396, 512, 14196, 4077, 755, 374, 39317, 1471, 997, 262, 422, 308, 2717, 220, 16, 512, 286, 471, 3641, 198, 262, 369, 602, 304, 2134, 7, 17, 11, 528, 1471, 3146, 220, 15, 13, 20, 8, 489, 220, 16, 997, 286, 422, 308, 1034, 602, 624, 220, 15, 512, 310, 471, 3641, 198, 262, 471, 3082, 198, 14196, 4077, 8586, 596, 459, 16540, 315, 279, 2082, 1473, 16, 13, 1442, 1595, 77, 63, 374, 2753, 1109, 477, 6273, 311, 220, 16, 11, 433, 596, 539, 264, 10461, 1396, 11, 779, 584, 471, 1595, 4139, 19154, 17, 13, 1226, 1193, 1205, 311, 1817, 50468, 3225, 709, 311, 279, 9518, 3789, 315, 1595, 77, 7964, 1606, 422, 1595, 77, 63, 374, 76016, 555, 264, 1396, 7191, 1109, 1202, 9518, 3789, 11, 433, 1053, 617, 2736, 1027, 10791, 555, 264, 9333, 50209, 13, 1226, 1005, 1595, 396, 1471, 3146, 220, 15, 13, 20, 8, 489, 220, 16, 63, 311, 11294, 279, 8582, 6965, 627, 18, 13, 1226, 30729, 505, 220, 17, 311, 279, 8582, 6965, 11, 323, 369, 1855, 1595, 72, 7964, 584, 1817, 422, 1595, 77, 63, 374, 76016, 555, 1595, 72, 63, 1701, 279, 60964, 5793, 29754, 77, 1034, 602, 624, 220, 15, 60310, 1442, 433, 374, 11, 1595, 77, 63, 374, 539, 264, 10461, 1396, 11, 779, 584, 471, 1595, 4139, 19154, 19, 13, 1442, 584, 5662, 279, 842, 315, 279, 6471, 2085, 9455, 264, 50209, 11, 1595, 77, 63, 374, 264, 10461, 1396, 11, 779, 584, 471, 1595, 2575, 63438, 2028, 734, 706, 264, 892, 23965, 315, 507, 7, 110682, 77, 705, 902, 374, 1790, 10819, 1109, 13598, 682, 279, 1648, 709, 311, 1595, 77, 63, 320, 8370, 1053, 617, 264, 892, 23965, 315, 507, 1471, 4682, 128009], cumulative_logprob=None, logprobs=None, finish_reason=stop, stop_reason=None)], finished=True, metrics=None, lora_request=None, num_cached_tokens=None, multi_modal_placeholders={})]
