Output~2025-04-24 17:54:56.528049: [RequestOutput(request_id=2056, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Name five places where paper can be recycled. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 4076, 4330, 7634, 1405, 5684, 649, 387, 47658, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here are five places where paper can be recycled:\n\n1. Local Recycling Centers: Most cities and towns have designated recycling centers where you can drop off your paper waste, such as newspapers, cardboard, and mixed paper.\n2. Curbside Recycling: Many communities offer curbside recycling programs that collect paper and other recyclable materials from your home.\n3. Office Recycling Bins: Many offices and workplaces have recycling bins where employees can deposit their paper waste, such as printer paper, cardboard, and junk mail.\n4. Community Recycling Drop-Offs: Some communities have designated drop-off locations where you can take your paper waste, such as community centers, libraries, and schools.\n5. Paper Recycling Facilities: Some companies and organizations have their own paper recycling facilities where they collect and process paper waste from their operations, such as office buildings, schools, and hospitals.\n\nRemember to always check with your local authorities or the specific facility to confirm what types of paper are accepted for recycling.', token_ids=[8586, 527, 4330, 7634, 1405, 5684, 649, 387, 47658, 1473, 16, 13, 8949, 81685, 41991, 25, 7648, 9919, 323, 25861, 6