Output~2025-04-24 17:55:51.273985: [RequestOutput(request_id=2072, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Formalize the following solution into an appropriate mathematical equation ### Input: y is 24 when x is 8 ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 11, 35526, 449, 459, 1988, 430, 5825, 4726, 2317, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 80467, 553, 279, 2768, 6425, 1139, 459, 8475, 37072, 24524, 17010, 5688, 25, 379, 374, 220, 1187, 994, 865, 374, 220, 23, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Based on the input that y is 24 when x is 8, we can formalize the solution into a mathematical equation as follows:\n\ny = kx + b\n\nwhere k is the slope and b is the y-intercept.\n\nSince we know that y is 24 when x is 8, we can substitute these values into the equation to get:\n\n24 = k(8) + b\n\nTo solve for k, we can subtract 8k from both sides of the equation:\n\n24 - 8k = b\n\nNow, we can solve for b by subtracting 24 from both sides:\n\n-8k = -24 + b\n\nDividing both sides by -8, we get:\n\nk = 3\n\nNow that we have found k, we can substitute it back into the original equation to solve for b:\n\n24 = 3(8) + b\n\nSubtracting 24 from both sides, we get:\n\n0 = 24 - 24 + b\n\nb = 0\n\nSo, the equation is:\n\ny = 3x + 0\n\nThis equation represents a straight line with a slope of 3 and a y-intercept of 0.', token_ids=[29815, 389, 279, 1988, 430, 379, 374, 220, 1187, 994, 865, 374, 220, 23, 11, 584, 649, 16287, 553, 279, 6425, 1139, 264, 37072, 24524, 439,