n\n**Taxes:**\n\n* The US has a federal income tax system, while Canada has a federal and provincial income tax system. The overall tax burden is generally higher in Canada, with an average tax rate of around 30-40% compared to around 20-30% in the US.\n* Sales taxes are also higher in Canada, with a combined federal and provincial rate of around 13-15% compared to around 8-10% in the US.\n\n**Healthcare:**\n\n* Healthcare is generally more expensive in the US, with a higher cost of medical procedures and prescription medications.\n* Canada has a publicly-funded healthcare system, while the US has a mixed system with both public and private options.\n\n**Other expenses:**\n\n* Utilities, such as electricity, water, and internet, are generally more expensive in Canada than in the US.\n* Entertainment and leisure activities, such as movies, concerts, and sporting events, can be more expensive in the US, especially in major cities like New York and Los Angeles.\n\nOverall, the cost of living in the US can be lower than in Canada, especially for housing and food. However, the cost of healthcare and taxes can be higher in the US. Ultimately, the cost of living in", token_ids=[791, 2853, 315, 5496, 304, 279, 2326, 323, 7008, 649, 13592, 12207, 11911, 389, 3892, 9547, 1778, 439, 279, 3813, 11, 19433, 11, 323, 4443, 11709, 13, 4452, 11, 1618, 527, 1063, 4689, 12062, 304, 279, 2853, 315, 5496, 1990, 279, 1403, 5961, 1473, 334, 39, 22485, 25, 57277, 9, 763, 279, 2326, 11, 279, 23369, 2162, 3430, 374, 2212, 400, 10914, 11, 931, 11, 1418, 304, 7008, 11, 433, 596, 2212, 400, 11738, 11, 931, 627, 9, 30837, 304, 279, 2326, 649, 2134, 505, 400, 16, 11, 931, 311, 400, 17, 11, 931, 824, 2305, 369, 264, 832, 67967, 13455, 11, 1418, 304, 7008, 11, 433, 649, 2134, 505, 400, 16, 11, 2636, 311, 400, 18, 11, 931, 824, 2305, 382, 334, 27844, 25, 57277, 9, 12369, 7729, 304, 279, 2326, 527, 8965, 4827, 1109, 304, 7008, 11, 449, 264, 14351, 315, 6913, 66508, 54824, 2212, 220, 605, 12, 508, 4, 