Output~2025-04-06 23:36:03.628946: [RequestOutput(request_id=28, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: How can I prepare my house for a power outage? ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 2650, 649, 358, 10772, 856, 3838, 369, 264, 2410, 89229, 30, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="Preparing your house for a power outage can help ensure your safety and comfort during an unexpected outage. Here's a comprehensive checklist to help you prepare:\n\n**Before the Outage:**\n\n1. **Create an emergency kit**: Assemble a kit with essential items such as:\n\t* Flashlights, extra batteries, and a battery-powered radio\n\t* First aid kit\n\t* Non-perishable food and water (at least 3 days' supply)\n\t* Manual can opener\n\t* Blankets and warm clothing\n\t* Important medications and medical equipment\n\t* Cash and credit cards\n2. **Charge your devices**: Charge your cell phone, laptop, and any other essential devices in case the power outage lasts for an extended period.\n3. **Unplug appliances**: Unplug sensitive electronics and appliances to protect them from power surges when the power is restored.\n4. **Prepare your refrigerator and freezer**: Keep your refrigerator and freezer doors closed as much as possible to maintain the temperature. Consider moving perishable food to a cooler with ice packs if the outage is expected to last for an extended period.\n5. **Install a backup power source**: Consider investing in a portable generator or installing a whole-house generator to provide backup power during outages.\n\n**During the Outage:**\n\n1. **Stay informed**: Monitor local news and weather reports for updates on the power outage and any necessary safety precautions.\n2. **Use flashlights**: Avoid using candles or open flames, as they can be hazardous.\n3. **Keep your refrigerator and freezer doors closed**: This will help keep your food from spoiling and reduce the risk of foodborne illness.\n4. **Use a battery-powered radio**: Stay informed about the status of the power outage and any necessary safety precautions.\n5. **Stay safe**: Avoid downed power lines, and never try to touch or approach them.\n\n**After the Outage:**\n\n1. **Wait for the all-clear**: Wait for official notification from your utility company or local authorities before attempting to use electrical appliances or re-enter your home.\n2. **Check for damage**: Inspect your home for any damage caused by the power outage, such as water damage or electrical issues.\n3. **Report any issues**: Report any issues or concerns to your utility company or local authorities.\n\nBy following these steps, you'll be well-prepared to handle a power outage and minimize any disruptions to your daily life.", token_ids=[98291, 701, 3838, 369, 264, 2410, 89229, 649, 1520, 6106, 701, 7296, 323, 6981, 2391, 459, 16907, 89229, 13, 5810, 596, 264, 16195, 53673, 311, 1520, 499, 10772, 1473, 334, 10438, 279, 4470, 425, 25, 57277, 16, 13, 3146, 4110, 459, 13147, 16530, 96618, 1666, 16167, 264, 16530, 449, 7718, 3673, 1778, 439, 512, 197, 9, 17710, 14146, 11, 5066, 27360, 11, 323, 264, 11863, 41503, 9063, 198, 197, 9, 5629, 12576, 16530, 198, 197, 9, 11842, 17453, 819, 481, 3691, 323, 3090, 320, 266, 3325, 220, 18, 2919, 6, 8312, 340, 197, 9, 14881, 649, 36253, 198, 197, 9, 43541, 1441, 323, 8369, 17895, 198, 197, 9, 44921, 31010, 323, 6593, 7241, 198, 197, 9, 23139, 323, 6807, 7563, 198, 17, 13, 3146, 56463, 701, 7766, 96618, 37895, 701, 2849, 4641, 11, 21288, 11, 323, 904, 1023, 7