Output~2025-04-06 23:38:44.809494: [RequestOutput(request_id=78, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Identify the key differences between the two computer memory storages. ### Input: RAM (Random Access Memory)\\nROM (Read-only Memory) ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 11, 35526, 449, 459, 1988, 430, 5825, 4726, 2317, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 65647, 279, 1401, 12062, 1990, 279, 1403, 6500, 5044, 34789, 1154, 13, 17010, 5688, 25, 22813, 320, 14326, 9742, 14171, 10929, 77, 3442, 320, 4518, 15744, 14171, 8, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="The key differences between RAM (Random Access Memory) and ROM (Read-only Memory) are:\n\n**RAM (Random Access Memory):**\n\n* Volatile memory: Data stored in RAM is lost when the power is turned off.\n* Temporary storage: RAM is used to store data that is being actively used by the CPU (Central Processing Unit) for processing.\n* Data can be written, read, and erased multiple times.\n* Capacity: Typically measured in gigabytes (GB) or terabytes (TB).\n* Examples: System RAM, video RAM, graphics card RAM.\n\n**ROM (Read-only Memory):**\n\n* Non-volatile memory: Data stored in ROM is retained even when the power is turned off.\n* Permanent storage: ROM is used to store data that does not need to be changed, such as the basic instructions for a computer's boot process.\n* Data can only be written once during the manufacturing process; it cannot be changed or erased.\n* Capacity: Typically measured in kilobytes (KB) or megabytes (MB).\n* Examples: BIOS (Basic Input/Output System), firmware, and some types of flash memory.\n\nIn summary, RAM is used for temporary storage of data that is being actively used by the CPU, while ROM is used for permanent storage of data that does not need to be changed.", token_ids=[791, 1401, 12062, 1990, 22813, 320, 14326, 9742, 14171, 8, 323, 31786, 320, 4518, 15744, 14171, 8, 527, 1473, 334, 35005, 320, 14326, 9742, 14171, 1680, 57277, 9, 11119, 9187, 5044, 25, 2956, 9967, 304, 22813, 374, 5675, 994, 279, 2410, 374, 6656, 1022, 627, 9, 55548, 5942, 25, 22813, 374, 1511, 311, 3637, 828, 430, 374, 1694, 22815, 1511, 555, 279, 14266, 320, 44503, 29225, 8113, 8, 369, 8863, 627, 9, 2956, 649, 387, 5439, 11, 1373, 11, 323, 64800, 5361, 3115, 627, 9, 41210, 25, 46402, 17303, 304, 23401, 72229, 320, 5494, 8, 477, 2024, 72229, 320, 32260, 4390, 9, 26379, 25, 744, 22813, 11, 2835, 22813, 11, 14515, 3786, 22813, 382, 334, 3442, 320, 4518, 15744, 14171, 1680, 57277, 9, 11842, 8437, 26598, 5044, 25, 2956, 9967, 304, 31786, 374, 35363, 1524, 994, 279, 2410, 374, 6656, 1022, 627, 9, 57316, 5942, 25, 31786, 374, 1511, 311, 3637, 828, 430, 1587, 539, 1205, 311, 387, 5614, 11, 1778, 439, 279, 6913, 11470, 369, 264, 6500, 596, 10677, 1920, 627, 9, 2956, 649, 1193, 387, 5439, 3131, 2391, 279, 15266, 1920, 26, 433, 4250, 387, 5614, 477, 64800, 627, 9, 41210, 25, 46402, 17303, 304, 15395, 28113, 2392, 320, 30962, 8, 477, 19262, 72229, 320, 8578, 4390, 9, 26379, 25, 53963, 320, 16323, 5688, 14, 5207, 744, 705, 30778, 11, 323, 1063, 4595, 315, 8381, 5044, 382, 644, 12399, 11, 22813, 374, 1511, 369, 13643, 5942, 315, 828, 430, 374, 1694, 22815, 1511, 555, 279, 14266, 11, 1418, 31786, 374, 1511, 369, 15690, 5942, 315, 828, 430, 1587, 539, 1205, 311, 387, 5614, 13, 128009], cumulative_logprob=None, logprobs=None, finish_reason=stop, stop_reason=None)], finished=True, metrics=None, lora_request=None, num_cached_tokens=None, multi_modal_placeholders=