Output~2025-04-06 23:44:27.951098: [RequestOutput(request_id=225, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Name the three Disabilities Rights Law. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 4076, 279, 2380, 98549, 10734, 7658, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='The three major Disabilities Rights Laws in the United States are:\n\n1. **Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) of 1990**: This law prohibits discrimination against individuals with disabilities in employment, transportation, public accommodations, and telecommunications.\n2. **Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973**: This law prohibits discrimination against individuals with disabilities in programs and activities receiving federal financial assistance, including education, healthcare, and employment.\n3. **Individuals with Disabilities Education Act (IDEA) of 1975**: This law ensures that children with disabilities receive a free and appropriate public education, including special education services and accommodations.\n\nThese laws aim to promote equal opportunities and access for individuals with disabilities in various aspects of life.', token_ids=[791, 2380, 3682, 98549, 10734, 42089, 304, 279, 3723, 4273, 527, 1473, 16, 13, 3146, 92786, 449, 98549, 3298, 320, 33393, 8, 315, 220, 2550, 15, 96618, 1115, 2383, 59538, 21934, 2403, 7931, 449, 36801, 304, 14740, 11, 18386, 11, 586, 55713, 11, 323, 62866, 627, 17, 13, 3146, 9817, 220, 18048, 315, 279, 81318, 3298, 315, 220, 4468, 18, 96618, 11