Output~2025-04-06 23:46:30.486337: [RequestOutput(request_id=268, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Suggest three activities for a group of 8-10 year old children at an outdoor party. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 328, 3884, 2380, 7640, 369, 264, 1912, 315, 220, 23, 12, 605, 1060, 2362, 2911, 520, 459, 16166, 4717, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='What a fun party! Here are three activity suggestions for a group of 8-10 year old children at an outdoor party:\n\n**Activity 1: Nature Scavenger Hunt**\nCreate a list of items that can be found in nature, such as leaves, rocks, feathers, and flowers. Divide the children into teams of 2-3 and give each team a copy of the list. Set a time limit (e.g., 20 minutes) and see which team can find the most items on the list. This activity encourages teamwork, problem-solving, and exploration of the outdoors.\n\n**Activity 2: Outdoor Games**\nSet up a few outdoor games that are perfect for a group of 8-10 year olds. Some ideas include:\n\t* Capture the Flag: A classic game of tag where each team has a flag to defend and capture.\n\t* Four Square: Draw a large square on the ground with chalk and divide the children into teams. Players take turns bouncing a ball and trying to make it land in another player\'s square.\n\t* Red Light, Green Light: Choose one child to be the "stoplight" and have them stand at one end of the party area. The other children start at the other end and must try to reach the stoplight without being caught. When the stoplight says "green light," the children can move towards them. When they say "red light," they must freeze in place.\n\n**Activity 3: Outdoor Art**\nSet up a designated area for outdoor art, such as a large piece of paper or a canvas on an easel. Provide a variety of art supplies, such as sidewalk chalk, paint, markers, and crayons. Encourage the children to get creative and make their own outdoor masterpieces. You could also set up a "collaborative mural" where everyone contributes to a single piece of art.\n\nRemember to always supervise the children during these activities and ensure their safety. With these activities, you\'ll have a fun and memorable outdoor party that the kids will cherish!', token_ids=[3923, 264, 2523, 4717, 0, 5810, 527, 2380, 5820, 18726, 369, 264, 1912, 315, 220, 23, 12, 605, 1060, 2362, 2911, 520, 459, 16166, 4717, 1473, 334, 4142, 220, 16, 25, 22037, 2522, 402, 10214, 27690, 1035, 4110, 264, 1160, 315, 3673, 430, 649, 387, 1766, 304, 7138, 11, 1778, 439, 11141, 11, 23902, 11, 56994, 11, 323, 19837, 13, 64002, 279, 2911, 1139, 7411, 315, 220, 17, 12, 18, 323, 3041, 1855, 2128, 264, 3048, 315, 279, 1160, 13, 2638, 264, 892, 4017, 320, 68, 1326, 2637, 220, 508, 4520, 8, 323, 1518, 902, 2128, 649, 1505, 279, 1455, 3673, 389, 279, 1160, 13, 1115, 5820, 37167, 84633, 11, 3575, 99246, 11, 323, 27501, 315, 279, 34632, 382, 334, 4142, 220, 17, 25, 33782, 11871, 1035, 1681, 709, 264, 2478, 16166, 3953, 430, 527, 4832, 369, 264, 1912, 315, 220, 23, 12, 605, 1060, 79573, 13, 4427, 6848, 2997, 512, 197, 9, 40985, 279, 23497, 25, 362, 11670, 1847, 315, 4877, 1405, 1855, 2128, 706, 264, 5292, 311, 10726, 323, 12602, 627, 197, 9, 13625, 15992, 25, 12261, 264, 3544, 9518, 389, 279, 5015, 449, 43459, 323, 22497, 279, 2911, 1139, 7411, 13, 25640, 1935, 10800, 65128, 264, 5041, 323, 4560, 311, 1304, 433, 4363, 304, 2500, 2851, 596, 9518, 627, 197, 9, 3816, 8828, 11, 7997, 8828, 25, 22991, 832, 1716, 311, 387, 279, 330