Output~2025-04-06 23:53:24.866457: [RequestOutput(request_id=412, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: How can I properly clean a wooden cutting board? ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 2650, 649, 358, 10489, 4335, 264, 23162, 14713, 4580, 30, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="**Properly Cleaning a Wooden Cutting Board**\n\nCleaning your wooden cutting board regularly is essential to prevent the buildup of bacteria, germs, and other contaminants that can affect the quality of your food and the longevity of the board. Here's a step-by-step guide on how to properly clean and maintain your wooden cutting board:\n\n**Step 1: Wipe Down the Board**\n\nAfter each use, wipe the cutting board clean with a damp cloth or paper towel to remove any food residue, crumbs, or spills. This will prevent the buildup of bacteria and make the cleaning process easier.\n\n**Step 2: Mix a Cleaning Solution**\n\nIn a small bowl, mix 1 tablespoon of mild dish soap with 1 cup of warm water. Dip a soft cloth into the solution, wring it out thoroughly, and wipe down the entire cutting board. Make sure to cover all surfaces, including the edges and grooves.\n\n**Step 3: Scrub the Board**\n\nUse a soft-bristled brush or a non-abrasive scrubber to gently scrub the board, paying particular attention to any areas with stubborn stains or residue. Avoid using harsh chemicals, abrasive cleaners, or scouring pads, as they can damage the wood.\n\n**Step 4: Rinse and Dry**\n\nRinse the cutting board thoroughly with clean water to remove any soap residue. Use a clean, dry cloth to wipe down the board and remove any excess moisture. This will help prevent warping or cracking.\n\n**Step 5: Dry and Oil (Optional)**\n\nTo maintain the wood's natural finish and prevent drying out, apply a small amount of food-safe wood oil or mineral oil to the board. Use a clean cloth to spread the oil evenly, making sure to cover all surfaces. Let the oil sit for 15-30 minutes before wiping off any excess with a clean cloth.\n\n**Additional Tips:**\n\n* Avoid using bleach or other harsh chemicals, as they can damage the wood or strip away its natural finish.\n* Don't put your wooden cutting board in the dishwasher, as the high heat and harsh detergents can damage the wood.\n* For tough stains or stubborn residue, mix equal parts water and white vinegar in a spray bottle and spray the area. Let it sit for 10-15 minutes before wiping clean.\n* Regularly cleaning and maintaining your wooden cutting board will help extend its lifespan and keep it looking like new.\n\nBy following these simple steps, you'll be able to keep your wooden cutting board clean, hygienic, and in", token_ids=[334, 1360, 716, 398, 47755, 264, 63592, 63525, 8925, 57277, 98281, 701, 23162, 14713, 4580, 15870, 374, 7718, 311, 5471, 279, 86765, 315, 24032, 11, 17684, 1026, 11, 323, 1023, 88959, 430, 649, 7958, 279, 4367, 315, 701, 3691, 323, 279, 58219, 315, 279, 4580, 13, 5810, 596, 264, 3094, 14656, 30308, 8641, 389, 1268, 311, 10489, 4335, 323, 10519, 701, 23162, 14713, 4580, 1473, 334, 8468, 220, 16, 25, 468, 3527, 6419, 279, 8925, 57277, 6153, 1855, 1005, 11, 40194, 279, 14713, 4580, 4335, 449, 264, 41369, 28392, 477, 5684, 43713, 311, 4148, 904, 3691, 49232, 11, 97677, 11, 477, 84051, 13, 1115, 690, 5471, 279, 86765, 315, 24032, 323, 1304, 279, 16204, 1920, 8831, 382, 334, 8468, 220, 17, 25, 19771, 264, 47755, 12761, 57277, 644, 264, 2678, 19763, 11, 6651, 220, 16, 62611, 315, 23900, 12269, 27883, 