sequence of events, which requires mathematical calculations to ensure a coherent and engaging narrative.\n2. Camera angles and movements: The use of trigonometry and geometry to determine the optimal camera angles and movements to capture the desired shots.\n3. Lighting: The application of mathematical principles, such as the inverse square law, to calculate the intensity and distribution of light in a scene.\n4. Special effects: The use of mathematical models and algorithms to create realistic simulations of explosions, fire, water, and other visual effects.\n5. Sound design: The application of mathematical concepts, such as frequency analysis and wave propagation, to create realistic sound effects and music.\n6. Editing: The use of mathematical techniques, such as pattern recognition and sequence analysis, to assemble the final cut of the film.\n7. Budgeting and scheduling: The application of mathematical models to manage the production budget and schedule, ensuring that the film is completed on time and within budget.\n\nBy understanding these mathematical concepts, filmmakers can create a cohesive and engaging film that captivates audiences worldwide.", token_ids=[791, 38696, 315, 5818, 5788, 374, 264, 62387, 582, 25489, 2115, 430, 33511, 32692, 11, 12624, 11, 323, 11156, 5540, 311, 4546, 264, 4632, 505, 5429, 311, 4264, 13, 17681, 15749, 4007, 279, 38696, 315, 11633, 6945, 5788, 311, 8895, 264, 16195, 8830, 315, 279, 4553, 1920, 11, 505, 5429, 4500, 311, 1620, 2027, 13, 1115, 6485, 1920, 18065, 5370, 37072, 19476, 11, 1778, 439, 1473, 16, 13, 15457, 38669, 25, 578, 9886, 315, 264, 9302, 13340, 315, 279, 4632, 596, 8668, 315, 4455, 11, 902, 7612, 37072, 29217, 311, 6106, 264, 56887, 323, 23387, 19775, 627, 17, 13, 14669, 27030, 323, 19567, 25, 578, 1005, 315, 54033, 263, 7133, 323, 17484, 311, 8417, 279, 23669, 6382, 27030, 323, 19567, 311, 12602, 279, 12974, 15300, 627, 18, 13, 45623, 25, 578, 3851, 315, 37072, 16565, 11, 1778, 439, 279, 29049, 9518, 2383, 11,