Output~2025-04-06 23:56:29.124468: [RequestOutput(request_id=484, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Write a function to calculate the body mass index of a person. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 9842, 264, 734, 311, 11294, 279, 2547, 3148, 1963, 315, 264, 1732, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here is a Python function that calculates the body mass index (BMI) of a person:\n```\ndef calculate_bmi(weight, height):\n    """\n    Calculate the body mass index (BMI) of a person.\n\n    Args:\n        weight (float): The person\'s weight in kilograms.\n        height (float): The person\'s height in meters.\n\n    Returns:\n        float: The person\'s BMI.\n    """\n    bmi = weight / (height ** 2)\n    return bmi\n```\nYou can use this function by passing in the person\'s weight and height as arguments, like this:\n```\nweight = 70  # in kg\nheight = 1.75  # in meters\nbmi = calculate_bmi(weight, height)\nprint(bmi)\n```\nThis would output the person\'s BMI, which you can then use to determine their health status based on the WHO BMI categories:\n\n* Underweight: BMI < 18.5\n* Normal weight: BMI = 18.5-24.9\n* Overweight: BMI = 25-29.9\n* Obese: BMI ≥ 30\n\nNote that this function assumes that the input values are in the correct units (kg for weight and meters for height). You may want to add error handling to handle invalid input values.', token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 13325, 734, 430, 48517, 279, 2547, 3148, 1963, 320, 96626, 8, 315, 264, 1732, 512, 14196, 4077, 755, 11294, 890, 8318, 57232, 11, 2673, 997, 262, 3270, 262, 21157, 279, 2547, 3148, 1963, 320, 96626, 8, 315, 264, 1732, 382, 262, 18161, 512, 286, 4785, 320, 3733, 1680, 578, 1732, 596, 4785, 304, 85402, 627, 286, 2673, 320, 3733, 1680, 578, 1732, 596, 2673, 304, 20645, 382, 262, 5295, 512, 286, 2273, 25, 578, 1732, 596, 47224, 627, 262, 3270, 262, 92997, 284, 4785, 611, 320, 2627, 3146, 220, 17, 340, 262, 471, 92997, 198, 14196, 4077, 2675, 649, 1005, 420, 734, 555, 12579, 304, 279, 1732, 596, 4785, 323, 2673, 439, 6105, 11, 1093, 420, 512, 14196, 4077, 4870, 284, 220, 2031, 220, 674, 304, 21647, 198, 2627, 284, 220, 16, 13, 2075, 220, 674, 304, 20645, 198, 65, 8318, 284, 11294, 890, 8318, 57232, 11, 2673, 340, 1374, 1921, 8318, 340, 14196, 4077, 2028, 1053, 2612, 279, 1732, 596, 47224, 11, 902, 499, 649, 1243, 1005, 311, 8417, 872, 2890, 2704, 3196, 389, 279, 40312, 47224, 11306, 1473, 9, 9636, 4870, 25, 47224, 366, 220, 972, 13, 20, 198, 9, 18944, 4785, 25, 47224, 284, 220, 972, 13, 20, 12, 1187, 13, 24, 198, 9, 6193, 4870, 25, 47224, 284, 220, 914, 12, 1682, 13, 24, 198, 9, 4761, 2423, 25, 47224, 63247, 220, 966, 271, 9290, 430, 420, 734, 22204, 430, 279, 1988, 2819, 527, 304, 279, 4495, 8316, 320, 7501, 369, 4785, 323, 20645, 369, 2673, 570, 1472, 1253, 1390, 311, 923, 1493, 11850, 311, 3790, 8482, 1988, 2819, 13, 128009], cumulative_logprob=None, logprobs=None, finish_reason=stop, stop_reason=None)], finished=True, metrics=None, lora_request=None, num_cached_tokens=None, multi_modal_placeholders={})]
