Output~2025-04-06 23:59:53.597485: [RequestOutput(request_id=556, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Explain why a given phenomenon occurs. ### Input: El Niño ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 11, 35526, 449, 459, 1988, 430, 5825, 4726, 2317, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 83017, 3249, 264, 2728, 25885, 13980, 13, 17010, 5688, 25, 4072, 22652, 14871, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='El Niño is a complex weather phenomenon that occurs when there is an abnormal warming of the surface waters in the eastern Pacific Ocean, near the equator. This warming of the ocean water is accompanied by changes in the atmospheric circulation patterns, leading to significant impacts on global climate and weather patterns.\n\nThe primary cause of El Niño is the trade winds, which are the winds that blow from east to west along the equator in the Pacific Ocean. Normally, these winds push the warm water of the western Pacific towards Asia, creating a high-pressure system. However, during an El Niño event, the trade winds weaken or even reverse direction, allowing the warm water to flow back towards the eastern Pacific. This warming of the ocean water is fueled by the increased evaporation of water from the surface, which in turn leads to an increase in atmospheric moisture and cloud formation.\n\nAs the ocean water warms, it releases heat into the atmosphere, which in turn warms the air. This warming of the air causes the atmospheric pressure to decrease, leading to an increase in the formation of low-pressure systems. These low-pressure systems can lead to heavy rainfall and flooding in some areas, while also causing droughts in others.\n\nThe weakening of the trade winds also allows the jet stream, a fast-moving band of air that plays a significant role in shaping global weather patterns, to shift its position. This shift in the jet stream can lead to changes in the path of storms and the formation of extreme weather events such as hurricanes and typhoons.\n\nEl Niño events can have significant impacts on global climate and weather patterns, including:\n\n* Heavy rainfall and flooding in some areas, such as South America and Southeast Asia\n* Droughts in other areas, such as Australia and Africa\n* Increased hurricane activity in the Atlantic Ocean\n* Changes in the frequency and intensity of wildfires\n* Impacts on global food production and economic stability\n\nOverall, El Niño is a complex phenomenon that is influenced by a combination of atmospheric and oceanic factors, and its impacts can be far-reaching and significant.', token_ids=[6719, 22652, 14871, 374, 264, 6485, 9282, 25885, 430, 13980, 994, 1070, 374, 459, 35663, 24808, 315, 279, 7479, 21160, 304, 279, 24024, 16867, 22302, 11, 3221, 279, 3312, 859, 13, 1115, 24808, 315, 279, 18435, 3090, 374, 24895, 555, 4442, 304, 279, 45475, 35855, 12912, 11, 6522, 311, 5199, 25949, 389, 3728, 10182, 323, 9282, 12912, 382, 791, 6156, 5353, 315, 4072, 22652, 14871, 374, 279, 6696, 29592, 11, 902, 527, 279, 29592, 430, 12523, 505, 11226, 311, 9909, 3235, 279, 3312, 859, 304, 279, 16867, 22302, 13, 52783, 11, 1521, 29592, 4585, 279, 8369, 3090, 315, 279, 19001, 16867, 7119, 13936, 11, 6968, 264, 1579, 89561, 1887, 13, 4452, 11, 2391, 459, 4072, 22652, 14871, 1567, 11, 279, 6696, 29592, 33556, 477, 1524, 10134, 5216, 11, 10923, 279, 8369, 3090, 311, 6530, 1203, 7119, 279, 24024, 16867, 13, 1115, 24808, 315, 279, 18435, 3090, 374, 59461, 555, 279, 7319, 3721, 966