Output~2025-04-07 00:01:38.593326: [RequestOutput(request_id=593, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Name three pieces of technology that were invented in the last decade. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 4076, 2380, 9863, 315, 5557, 430, 1051, 36592, 304, 279, 1566, 13515, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here are three pieces of technology that were invented in the last decade (2010-2019):\n\n1. **Smart Speakers (2014)**: Amazon Echo (Alexa) and Google Home were introduced in 2014, revolutionizing the way we interact with technology in our homes. These smart speakers use voice assistants to perform tasks, play music, set alarms, and answer questions.\n2. **Foldable Smartphones (2019)**: Samsung and Huawei introduced the first foldable smartphones in 2019, allowing users to have a larger screen in a smaller form factor. These devices feature flexible OLED displays that can be folded and unfolded, offering a new way to interact with mobile devices.\n3. **5G Networks (2019)**: The first commercial 5G networks were launched in 2019, offering faster data speeds, lower latency, and greater connectivity. 5G technology enables new use cases such as widespread adoption of IoT devices, remote healthcare, and immersive entertainment experiences.\n\nThese are just a few examples of the many innovative technologies that have emerged in the last decade.', token_ids=[8586, 527, 2380, 9863, 315, 5557, 430, 1051, 36592, 304, 279, 1566, 13515, 320, 679, 15,