es of 14 and 18 can be employed in certain industries, such as agriculture, but only with a valid permit.\n2. **The Equal Remuneration Act, 1976**: This law also applies to young workers, ensuring that they receive equal pay for equal work, regardless of their age.\n3. **The Payment of Gratuity (Amendment) Act, 2018**: This law provides for a minimum amount of gratuity (a payment made to employees upon retirement or termination) to be paid to employees who have completed at least five years of service, regardless of their age.\n\n**Other key labor laws:**\n\n1. **The Factories Act, 1948**: This law regulates the working conditions in factories, including the maximum working hours, leave, and safety measures.\n2. **The Payment of Wages Act, 1936**: This law ensures that employees receive their wages on time and in accordance with the law.\n3. **The Industrial Disputes Act, 1947**: This law provides for the settlement of industrial disputes through conciliation, arbitration, or adjudication.\n4. **The Trade Unions Act, 1926**: This law regulates the formation and functioning of trade unions, which are essential for collective bargaining and protecting workers' rights.\n\nThese labor laws aim to promote a", token_ids=[34648, 706, 264, 16195, 9511, 2383, 12914, 430, 22262, 311, 6144, 279, 3268, 315, 7487, 4028, 5370, 82428, 323, 17051, 13, 5810, 596, 459, 24131, 315, 279, 1401, 9511, 7016, 304, 6890, 1473, 334, 30014, 6108, 9511, 7016, 25, 57277, 16, 13, 3146, 3066, 5031, 359, 21597, 3298, 11, 220, 4468, 21, 96618, 1115, 2383, 26420, 6273, 2343, 369, 6273, 990, 369, 2225, 3026, 323, 3278, 13, 1102, 59538, 21934, 304, 279, 8323, 315, 23998, 389, 279, 8197, 315, 10026, 627, 17, 13, 3146, 11836, 34719, 67450, 320, 6219, 14988, 8, 3298, 11, 220, 679, 22, 96618, 1115, 2383, 5825, 369, 220, 1627, 5672, 315, 7318, 71271, 5387, 311, 3278, 8420, 11, 449, 459, 5217, 220, 717, 5672, 315, 5387, 369, 3278, 889, 617, 44736, 11, 24657, 2641, 11, 477, 810, 2911, 627, 18, 13, 3146, 791,