Output~2025-04-07 00:06:45.058820: [RequestOutput(request_id=707, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Construct an algorithm for calculating prime numbers. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 19196, 459, 12384, 369, 38714, 10461, 5219, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here is a step-by-step algorithm for calculating prime numbers:\n\n**Algorithm: Prime Number Checker**\n\n**Input:** An integer `n` greater than 1\n\n**Output:** A boolean value indicating whether `n` is a prime number or not\n\n**Step 1:** Initialize a variable `is_prime` to `true`\n\n**Step 2:** If `n` is less than 2, set `is_prime` to `false` and return `false`\n\n**Step 3:** Iterate from 2 to the square root of `n` (inclusive)\n\n**Step 4:** For each integer `i` in the iteration, check if `n` is divisible by `i` (i.e., `n % i == 0`)\n\n**Step 5:** If `n` is divisible by `i`, set `is_prime` to `false` and break out of the loop\n\n**Step 6:** If the loop completes without finding a divisor, set `is_prime` to `true`\n\n**Step 7:** Return `is_prime`\n\n**Pseudocode:**\n```\nfunction is_prime(n):\n  is_prime = true\n  if n < 2:\n    return false\n  for i from 2 to sqrt(n):\n    if n % i == 0:\n      is_prime = false\n      break\n  return is_prime\n```\n**Example usage:**\n\n* `is_prime(5)` returns `true`\n* `is_prime(6)` returns `false`\n* `is_prime(23)` returns `true`\n* `is_prime(48)` returns `false`\n\nThis algorithm has a time complexity of O(√n), making it efficient for large values of `n`.', token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 3094, 14656, 30308, 12384, 369, 38714, 10461, 5219, 1473, 334, 28947, 25, 12801, 5742, 81778, 57277, 334, 2566, 68063, 1556, 7698, 1595, 77, 63, 7191, 1109, 220, 16, 271, 334, 5207, 68063, 362, 2777, 907, 19392, 3508, 1595, 77, 63, 374, 264, 10461, 1396, 477, 539, 271, 334, 8468, 220, 16, 68063, 9185, 264, 3977, 1595, 285, 39317, 63, 311, 1595, 1904, 19884, 334, 8468, 220, 17, 68063, 1442, 1595, 77, 63, 374, 2753, 1109, 220, 17, 11, 743, 1595, 285, 39317, 63, 311, 1595, 3934, 63, 323, 471, 1595, 3934, 19884, 334, 8468, 220, 18, 68063, 55440, 505, 220, 17, 311, 279, 9518, 3789, 315, 1595, 77, 63, 320, 99461, 696, 334, 8468, 220, 19, 68063, 1789, 1855, 7698, 1595, 72, 63, 304, 279, 20140, 11, 1817, 422, 1595, 77, 63, 374, 76016, 555, 1595, 72, 63, 320, 72, 1770, 2637, 1595, 77, 1034, 602, 624, 220, 15, 63, 696, 334, 8468, 220, 20, 68063, 1442, 1595, 77, 63, 374, 76016, 555, 1595, 72, 7964, 743, 1595, 285, 39317, 63, 311, 1595, 3934, 63, 323, 1464, 704, 315, 279, 6471, 271, 334, 8468, 220, 21, 68063, 1442, 279, 6471, 45695, 2085, 9455, 264, 50209, 11, 743, 1595, 285, 39317, 63, 311, 1595, 1904, 19884, 334, 8468, 220, 22, 68063, 3494, 1595, 285, 39317, 19884, 334, 47, 40512, 44788, 25, 1035, 14196, 4077, 1723, 374, 39317, 1471, 997, 220, 374, 39317, 284, 837, 198, 220, 422, 308, 366, 220, 17, 512, 262, 471, 905, 198, 220, 369, 602, 505, 220, 17, 311, 18430, 1471, 997, 262, 422, 308, 1034, 602, 624, 220, 15, 512, 415, 374, 39317, 284, 905, 198, 415, 1464, 198, 220, 471, 374, 39317, 198, 14196, 4077, 334, 13617, 10648, 25, 57277, 9, 1595, 285, 39317, 7, 20, 47286, 4780, 1595, 1904, 4077, 9, 1595, 285, 39317, 7, 21, 47286, 4780, 1595, 3934, 4077, 9, 1595, 285, 39317, 7, 1419, 47286, 4780, 1595, 1904, 4077, 9, 1595, 285, 39317, 7, 2166, 47286, 4780, 1595, 3934, 19884, 2028, 12384, 706, 264, 892, 23965, 315, 507, 7, 110682, 77, 705, 3339, 433, 11297, 369, 3544, 2819, 315, 1595, 77, 29687, 128009], cumulative_logprob=None, logprobs=