Output~2025-04-07 00:09:59.913320: [RequestOutput(request_id=775, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Compile a list of recommended websites for learning about computer science. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 55567, 264, 1160, 315, 11349, 13335, 369, 6975, 922, 6500, 8198, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here is a list of recommended websites for learning about computer science:\n\n**Online Courses and Tutorials**\n\n1. **Codecademy** (codecademy.com): Interactive coding lessons in a variety of programming languages, including Python, JavaScript, and HTML/CSS.\n2. **Coursera** (coursera.org): University-level courses on computer science and related fields, with options for certification.\n3. **edX** (edx.org): Massive Open Online Courses (MOOCs) from top universities worldwide, including Harvard, MIT, and Stanford.\n4. **FreeCodeCamp** (freecodecamp.org): A non-profit organization offering a comprehensive curriculum in web development and computer science.\n5. **Udemy** (udemy.com): A wide range of courses on computer science and programming, often with a focus on practical applications.\n\n**Programming Communities and Forums**\n\n1. **Stack Overflow** (stackoverflow.com): A Q&A platform for programmers and developers.\n2. **Reddit** (reddit.com/r/learnprogramming): A community-driven forum for learning programming and computer science.\n3. **Hacker News** (news.ycombinator.com): A platform for discussing technology, programming, and computer science.\n\n**Blogs and News Sites**\n\n1. **The Verge** (theverge.com): Technology news and analysis, with a focus on computer science and programming.\n2. **Ars Technica** (arstechnica.com): In-depth technology news and analysis, including coverage of computer science and programming.\n3. **GeeksforGeeks** (geeksforgeeks.org): A blog and community for computer science and programming enthusiasts.\n\n**Resources for Specific Topics**\n\n1. **Algorithms**:\n\t* **GeeksforGeeks** (geeksforgeeks.org): A comprehensive resource for algorithms and data structures.\n\t* **LeetCode** (leetcode.com): A platform for practicing coding challenges and learning algorithms.\n2. **Data Science**:\n\t* **Kaggle** (kaggle.com): A platform for data science competitions and learning.\n\t* **DataCamp** (datacamp.com): Interactive data science courses and tutorials.\n3. **Web Development**:\n\t* **MDN Web Docs** (developer.mozilla.org): Official documentation for web development, including HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.\n\t* **W3Schools** (w3schools.com): A website for learning web development, including tutorials and reference materials.\n\nThese resources should provide a solid foundation', token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 1160, 315, 11349, 13335, 369, 6975, 922, 6500, 8198, 1473, 334, 20171, 48778, 323, 350, 56027, 57277, 16, 13, 3146, 2123, 35555, 4625, 334, 320, 1889, 35555, 4625, 916, 1680, 42966, 11058, 18872, 304, 264, 8205, 315, 15840, 15823, 11, 2737, 13325, 11, 13210, 11, 323, 9492, 11547, 1242, 627, 17, 13, 3146, 44349, 805, 64, 334, 320, 67971, 805, 64, 2726, 1680, 3907, 11852, 14307, 389, 6500, 8198, 323, 5552, 5151, 11, 449, 2671, 369, 28706, 627, 18, 13, 3146, 291, 55, 334, 320, 72193, 2726, 1680, 82564, 5377, 8267, 48778, 320, 10754, 7767, 82, 8, 505, 1948, 23978, 15603, 11, 2737, 25996, 11, 15210, 11, 323, 31788, 627, 19, 13, 3146, 11180, 2123, 34955, 334, 320, 25746, 762, 536, 26304, 2726, 1680, 362, 2536, 28926, 7471, 10209, 264, 16195, 30676, 304, 3566, 4500, 323, 6500, 