Output~2025-04-07 00:10:52.198534: [RequestOutput(request_id=801, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Explain the concept of RNA interference. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 83017, 279, 7434, 315, 41214, 32317, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='RNA interference (RNAi) is a natural process by which cells regulate gene expression by degrading specific messenger RNA (mRNA) molecules. It is a crucial mechanism for controlling gene expression and maintaining cellular homeostasis.\n\nThe process of RNAi begins with the production of small interfering RNA (siRNA) molecules, which are typically 21-23 nucleotides in length. These siRNAs are generated from longer RNA molecules, such as microRNA (miRNA) or viral RNA, through a process called Dicer-mediated cleavage.\n\nOnce produced, siRNAs are incorporated into a protein complex called the RNA-induced silencing complex (RISC). The RISC complex then searches for and binds to complementary mRNA molecules, which are then degraded by an enzyme called Argonaute.\n\nThe degradation of mRNA prevents the translation of the corresponding protein, effectively silencing the gene. This process is highly specific, as the RISC complex only targets mRNA molecules with perfect or near-perfect complementarity to the siRNA.\n\nRNAi has been widely used as a tool for gene therapy, as it allows for the specific silencing of disease-causing genes or the introduction of therapeutic genes into cells. It has also been used to study gene function and regulation, as well as to develop new treatments for various diseases, including cancer, viral infections, and genetic disorders.\n\nIn addition to its therapeutic applications, RNAi has also been used to study gene function and regulation in various organisms, including plants, animals, and humans. It has been shown to play a crucial role in the regulation of gene expression, particularly in the context of development, differentiation, and disease.\n\nOverall, RNAi is a powerful tool for regulating gene expression and has the potential to revolutionize our understanding of gene function and disease.', token_ids=[31820, 32317, 320, 31820, 72, 8, 374, 264, 5933, 1920, 555, 902, 7917, 37377, 15207, 7645, 555, 409, 33359, 3230, 50596, 41214, 320, 76, 31820, 8, 35715, 13, 1102, 374, 264, 16996, 17383, 369, 26991, 15207, 7645, 323, 20958, 35693, 2162, 537, 10949, 382, 791, 1920, 315, 41214, 72, 12302, 449, 279, 5788, 315, 2678, 75387, 41214, 320, 6455, 31820, 8, 35715, 11, 902, 527, 11383, 220, 1691, 12, 1419, 31484, 354, 3422, 304, 3160, 13, 4314, 4502, 51295, 2170, 527, 8066, 505, 5129, 41214, 35715, 11, 1778, 439, 8162, 31820, 320, 8318, 31820, 8, 477, 29962, 41214, 11, 1555, 264, 1920, 2663, 423, 13296, 82076, 11551, 68256, 382, 12805, 9124, 11, 4502, 51295, 2170, 527, 32762, 1139, 264, 13128, 6485, 2663, 279, 41214, 38973, 5554, 11627, 6485, 320, 49, 28729, 570, 578, 432, 28729, 6485, 1243, 27573, 369, 323, 58585, 311, 58535, 78872, 35715, 11, 902, 527, 1243, 91978, 555, 459, 49242, 2663, 7793, 6863, 1088, 382, 791, 53568, 315, 78872, 29034, 279, 14807, 315, 279, 12435, 13128, 11, 13750, 5554, 11627, 279, 15207, 13, 1115, 1920, 374, 7701, 3230, 11, 439, 279, 432, 28729, 6485, 1193, 11811, 78872, 35715, 449, 4832, 477, 3221, 17453, 3836, 23606, 10981, 311, 279, 4502, 31820, 382, 31820, 72, 706, 1027, 13882, 1511, 439, 264, 5507, 369, 15207, 15419, 11, 439, 433, 6276, 369, 279, 3230, 5554, 11627, 315, 8624, 51877, 985, 21389, 477, 279, 17219,