Output~2025-04-07 00:14:16.663863: [RequestOutput(request_id=875, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: What is the climate like in India? ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 3639, 374, 279, 10182, 1093, 304, 6890, 30, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="India is a vast and geographically diverse country, spanning across the Indian subcontinent and the Indian Ocean. As a result, the climate in India varies greatly depending on the region, season, and elevation. Here's an overview of the different climates found in India:\n\n**Tropical Climate:** The southern and eastern parts of India, including states like Kerala, Tamil Nadu, and Andhra Pradesh, have a tropical climate with high temperatures and high humidity throughout the year. The average temperature ranges from 20°C to 30°C (68°F to 86°F).\n\n**Subtropical Climate:** The northern and western parts of India, including states like Punjab, Haryana, and Gujarat, have a subtropical climate with hot summers and mild winters. The average temperature ranges from 15°C to 35°C (59°F to 95°F).\n\n**Temperate Climate:** The Himalayan regions of India, including states like Jammu and Kashmir, Himachal Pradesh, and Uttarakhand, have a temperate climate with cold winters and mild summers. The average temperature ranges from -10°C to 20°C (14°F to 68°F).\n\n**Desert Climate:** The western state of Rajasthan has a desert climate, with very hot summers and mild winters. The average temperature ranges from 15°C to 45°C (59°F to 113°F).\n\n**Monsoon Climate:** India experiences a monsoon season from June to September, during which the country receives most of its annual rainfall. The monsoon climate is characterized by heavy rainfall, thunderstorms, and flash floods.\n\n**Regional Variations:** India's climate also varies greatly depending on the region. For example, the coastal regions of India tend to be cooler and more humid than the inland regions, while the mountainous regions are generally cooler and more temperate.\n\nOverall, India's climate is diverse and complex, with varying temperatures, humidity, and precipitation patterns across different regions and seasons.", token_ids=[34648, 374, 264, 13057, 323, 3980, 65031, 17226, 3224, 11, 56886, 4028, 279, 7904, 1207, 75695, 323, 279, 7904, 22302, 13, 1666, 264, 1121, 11, 279, 10182, 304, 6890, 35327, 19407, 11911, 389, 279, 5654, 11, 3280, 11, 323, 27255, 13, 5810, 596, 459, 24131, 315, 279, 2204, 92399, 1766, 304, 6890, 1473, 334, 51, 51172, 31636, 68063, 578, 18561, 323, 24024, 5596, 315, 6890, 11, 2737, 5415, 1093, 61507, 11, 44883, 75905, 11, 323, 1628, 73010, 43458, 11, 617, 264, 35148, 10182, 449, 1579, 20472, 323, 1579, 38193, 6957, 279, 1060, 13, 578, 5578, 9499, 21986, 505, 220, 508, 32037, 311, 220, 966, 32037, 320, 2614, 59572, 311, 220, 4218, 59572, 3677, 334, 3214, 83, 51172, 31636, 68063, 578, 18671, 323, 19001, 5596, 315, 6890, 11, 2737, 5415, 1093, 60417, 11, 473, 94074, 11, 323, 62953, 11, 617, 264, 42129, 51172, 10182, 449, 4106, 80769, 323, 23900, 86082, 13, 578, 5578, 9499, 21986, 505, 220, 868, 32037, 311, 220, 1758, 32037, 320, 2946, 59572, 311, 220, 2721, 59572, 3677, 334, 22759, 80213, 31636, 68063, 578, 76438, 44957, 13918, 315, 6890, 11, 2737, 5415, 1093, 622, 88139, 323, 50280, 11, 21058, 613, 278, 43458, 11, 323, 68062, 28985, 10888, 11, 617, 264, 6940, 349, 10182, 449, 9439, 86082, 323, 23900, 80769, 13, 578, 5578, 9499, 21986, 505, 482, 605, 32037, 311, 220, 508, 32037, 320, 975, 59572, 311, 22