n vehicle speed, distance, and pedestrian presence.\n2. **Data Processing:** The CPU processes the data using the machine learning algorithm to identify potential collisions.\n3. **Collision Prediction:** The algorithm predicts the likelihood of a collision and alerts the system.\n4. **Response:** The system triggers a response based on the severity of the predicted collision:\n\t* Mild: The system displays a warning message on the vehicle\'s dashboard and alerts the driver.\n\t* Moderate: The system applies gentle braking to slow down the vehicle.\n\t* Severe: The system applies full braking to prevent or mitigate the collision.\n\n**Additional Features:**\n\n1. **Pedestrian Detection:** The system can detect pedestrians using computer vision and machine learning algorithms, even in low-light conditions.\n2. **Lane Departure Warning:** The system alerts the driver if the vehicle drifts out of its lane.\n3. **Speed Limit Enforcement:** The system can detect speed limit signs and alert the driver if they exceed the limit.\n\n**Benefits:**\n\n1. **Reduced Collisions:** PSN can reduce collisions by up to 90% by detecting potential hazards and responding in real-time.\n2. **Improved Safety:** The system provides an additional layer of safety for pedestrians, cyclists, and other vulnerable road users.\n3. **Increased Efficiency:** PSN can reduce traffic congestion by smoothing traffic flow and reducing the number of accidents.\n\n**Implementation:**\n\n1. **Integration:** PSN can be integrated', token_ids=[334, 15836, 61439, 12761, 311, 53253, 13201, 6948, 1990, 36231, 323, 19878, 478, 36268, 57277, 334, 2374, 35907, 25, 57277, 791, 11223, 15592, 6108, 6425, 11, 42160, 330, 36294, 478, 7414, 19220, 9558, 1, 320, 5119, 45, 705, 374, 264, 16195, 1887, 6319, 311, 8108, 48453, 1990, 9515, 323, 62558, 13, 578, 1887, 60880, 264, 10824, 315, 26148, 11, 18632, 11, 323, 5780, 6975, 26249, 311, 11388, 323, 6013, 311, 4754, 52642, 304, 1972, 7394, 382, 334, 10660, 25, 57277, 16, 13