Output~2025-04-07 00:20:34.614662: [RequestOutput(request_id=1009, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task, paired with an input that provides further context. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Compose a film review for the last film you watched. ### Input: Parasite ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 11, 35526, 449, 459, 1988, 430, 5825, 4726, 2317, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 1219, 2972, 264, 4632, 3477, 369, 279, 1566, 4632, 499, 15746, 13, 17010, 5688, 25, 94137, 635, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="**Film Review: Parasite**\n\nI just emerged from the cinema, still reeling from the thought-provoking and masterfully crafted film, Parasite. Directed by Bong Joon-ho, this South Korean black comedy thriller is a work of genius that will leave you questioning the very fabric of society.\n\nThe story follows the Kims, a poor family of four who scheme their way into the lives of a wealthy family, the Parks. The Kims pose as unrelated, highly qualified individuals and infiltrate the Parks' luxurious mansion, where they begin to take on various roles as a driver, art therapist, and tutor. As they become more entrenched in the Parks' lives, the lines between reality and fiction blur, and the consequences of their actions become increasingly dire.\n\nThe film's greatest strength lies in its razor-sharp script, which is both wickedly funny and devastatingly poignant. The characters are multidimensional and relatable, with each one bringing their own unique brand of humor and pathos to the table. The performances are outstanding, with standout turns from Song Kang-ho and Lee Sun-kyun as the patriarchs of the two families.\n\nVisually, the film is stunning, with a keen attention to detail that immerses the viewer in the world of the characters. The cinematography is breathtaking, capturing the stark contrast between the opulence of the Parks' mansion and the squalor of the Kims' cramped semi-basement apartment.\n\nWhat truly sets Parasite apart, however, is its thought-provoking commentary on class struggle and social inequality. The film is a scathing critique of the exploitation and oppression that occurs when those with power and privilege use it to maintain their status quo. It's a powerful reminder that the divide between the haves and have-nots is not just economic, but also emotional and psychological.\n\nIn short, Parasite is a masterpiece that will leave you laughing, crying, and questioning the world around you. It's a must-see for anyone who loves film, and a testament to the power of cinema to challenge and inspire us.", token_ids=[334, 52587, 10506, 25, 94137, 635, 57277, 40, 1120, 22763, 505, 279, 34292, 11, 2103, 312, 20659, 505, 279, 3463, 10039, 85, 10979, 323, 7491, 3725, 34558, 4632, 11, 94137, 635, 13, 78305, 555, 426, 647, 622, 9186, 2902, 78, 11, 420, 4987, 16526, 3776, 23160, 54461, 374, 264, 990, 315, 35201, 430, 690, 5387, 499, 34685, 279, 1633, 13354, 315, 8396, 382, 791, 3446, 11263, 279, 735, 5861, 11, 264, 8009, 3070, 315, 3116, 889, 13155, 872, 1648, 1139, 279, 6439, 315, 264, 28994, 3070, 11, 279, 39272, 13, 578, 735, 5861, 17477, 439, 46305, 11, 7701, 15337, 7931, 323, 43364, 349, 279, 39272, 6, 43828, 52528, 11, 1405, 814, 3240, 311, 1935, 389, 5370, 13073, 439, 264, 5696, 11, 1989, 42863, 11, 323, 26370, 13, 1666, 814, 3719, 810, 82144, 304, 279, 39272, 6, 6439, 11, 279, 5238, 1990, 8903, 323, 17422, 29613, 11, 323, 279, 16296, 315, 872, 6299, 3719, 15098, 13510, 382, 791, 4632, 596, 12474, 8333, 15812, 304, 1202, 60230, 7666, 8035, 5429, 11, 902, 374