Output~2025-04-07 00:27:33.537625: [RequestOutput(request_id=1173, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Calculate the number of months it will take to double the amount of money in a bank account that earns an annual 6% interest rate. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 21157, 279, 1396, 315, 4038, 433, 690, 1935, 311, 2033, 279, 3392, 315, 3300, 304, 264, 6201, 2759, 430, 64859, 459, 9974, 220, 21, 4, 2802, 4478, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='To calculate the number of months it will take to double the amount of money in a bank account that earns an annual 6% interest rate, we can use the rule of 72.\n\nThe rule of 72 is a rough estimate that states that to find the number of years it takes for an investment to double in value, you can divide 72 by the interest rate. Since the interest rate is 6%, we can divide 72 by 6 to get:\n\n72 ÷ 6 = 12\n\nThis means that it will take approximately 12 years for the investment to double in value.\n\nSince we want to know the number of months, we can multiply the number of years by 12:\n\n12 years × 12 months/year = 144 months\n\nTherefore, it will take approximately 144 months, or 12 years, for the amount of money in the bank account to double if it earns an annual 6% interest rate.', token_ids=[1271, 11294, 279, 1396, 315, 4038, 433, 690, 1935, 311, 2033, 279, 3392, 315, 3300, 304, 264, 6201, 2759, 430, 64859, 459, 9974, 220, 21, 4, 2802, 4478, 11, 584, 649, 1005, 279, 6037, 315, 220, 5332, 382, 791, 603