Output~2025-04-07 00:29:19.225179: [RequestOutput(request_id=1207, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Make a rule to categorize documents depending on the information they contain. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 7557, 264, 6037, 311, 22824, 553, 9477, 11911, 389, 279, 2038, 814, 6782, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Based on the instruction, I propose the following rule to categorize documents:\n\n**Rule:** Documents will be categorized based on the primary topic or theme they contain. The categories will be determined by the main subject matter, purpose, or focus of the document.\n\n**Categories:**\n\n1. **Business**: Documents related to business operations, finance, marketing, or management.\n2. **Technology**: Documents related to computer programming, software development, hardware, or IT.\n3. **Health**: Documents related to medical research, healthcare, wellness, or medical procedures.\n4. **Education**: Documents related to academic research, educational policies, or teaching methods.\n5. **Entertainment**: Documents related to movies, music, books, or other forms of entertainment.\n6. **Travel**: Documents related to travel guides, itineraries, or travel tips.\n7. **Government**: Documents related to government policies, laws, or regulations.\n8. **Science**: Documents related to scientific research, experiments, or discoveries.\n9. **Art**: Documents related to art history, art criticism, or artistic techniques.\n10. **Miscellaneous**: Documents that do not fit into any of the above categories.\n\n**Categorization Process:**\n\n1. Read the document and identify the primary topic or theme.\n2. Determine which category best fits the document based on its content.\n3. If the document contains multiple topics or themes, categorize it based on the most prominent or dominant topic.\n\nBy following this rule, documents can be efficiently categorized and easily retrieved based on their content, making it easier to manage and search for specific information.', token_ids=[29815, 389, 279, 7754, 11, 358, 30714, 279, 2768, 6037, 311, 22824, 553, 9477, 1473, 334, 11590, 68063, 45890, 690, 387, 71974, 3196, 389, 279, 6156, 8712, 477, 7057, 814, 6782, 13, 578, 11306, 690, 387, 11075, 555, 279, 1925, 3917, 5030, 11, 7580, 11, 477, 5357, 315, 279, 2246, 382, 334, 21645, 25, 57277, 16, 13, 3146, 23562, 96618, 45890, 5552, 311, 2626, 7677, 11, 17452, 11, 8661, 11, 477, 6373, 627, 17, 13, 3146, 63507, 96618, 45890, 5552, 311, 6500, 15840, 11, 3241, 4500, 11, 12035, 11, 477, 8871, 627, 18, 13, 3146, 14884, 96618, 45890, 5552, 311, 6593, 3495, 11, 18985, 11, 39890, 11, 477, 6593, 16346, 627, 19, 13, 3146, 40234, 96618, 45890, 5552, 311, 14584, 3495, 11, 16627, 10396, 11, 477, 12917, 5528, 627, 20, 13, 3146, 2300, 11454, 96618, 45890, 5552, 311, 9698, 11, 4731, 11, 6603, 11, 477, 1023, 7739, 315, 16924, 627, 21, 13, 3146, 41348, 96618, 45890, 5552, 311, 5944, 28292, 11, 433, 10670, 5548, 11, 477, 5944, 10631, 627, 22, 13, 3146, 62569, 96618, 45890, 5552, 311, 3109, 10396, 11, 7016, 11, 477, 14640, 627, 23, 13, 3146, 36500, 96618, 45890, 5552, 311, 12624, 3495, 11, 21896, 11, 477, 54098, 627, 24, 13, 3146, 9470, 96618, 45890, 5552, 311, 1989, 3925, 11, 1989, 19347, 11, 477, 32692, 12823, 627, 605, 13, 3146, 52079, 41242, 96618, 45890, 430, 656, 539, 5052, 1139, 904, 315, 279, 3485, 11306, 382, 334, 34, 7747, 2065, 8773, 25, 57277, 16, 13, 4557, 279, 2246, 323, 10765, 279, 6156, 8712, 477, 7057, 627, 17, 13, 31001