Output~2025-04-07 00:30:31.835984: [RequestOutput(request_id=1235, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Come up with an algorithm for predicting house prices in a given city. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 15936, 709, 449, 459, 12384, 369, 52997, 3838, 7729, 304, 264, 2728, 3363, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here\'s a potential algorithm for predicting house prices in a given city:\n\n**House Price Prediction Algorithm**\n\n**Input:**\n\n* `city`: The city for which we want to predict house prices\n* `features`: A set of features that describe the house, including:\n\t+ `num_bedrooms`: The number of bedrooms in the house\n\t+ `num_bathrooms`: The number of bathrooms in the house\n\t+ `square_footage`: The square footage of the house\n\t+ `age`: The age of the house in years\n\t+ `location`: The neighborhood or zip code of the house\n\t+ `condition`: The condition of the house (e.g. "good", "fair", "poor")\n\t+ `amenities`: A list of amenities the house has, such as a pool, yard, etc.\n* `training_data`: A dataset of historical house sales in the city, including the sale price and the corresponding features for each house\n\n**Algorithm:**\n\n1. **Data Preprocessing**:\n\t* Normalize the features by scaling them to a common range (e.g. 0-1) to prevent features with large ranges from dominating the model.\n\t* Handle missing values by imputing them with the mean or median value for each feature.\n2. **Feature Engineering**:\n\t* Create new features that capture additional information about the house, such as:\n\t\t+ `price_per_sqft`: The price per square foot of the house\n\t\t+ `bedroom_to_bathroom_ratio`: The ratio of bedrooms to bathrooms\n\t\t+ `age_squared`: The square of the age of the house (to capture non-linear relationships)\n\t* Select the most relevant features from the original set and the new features created in this step.\n3. **Model Selection**:\n\t* Choose a suitable machine learning algorithm for regression tasks, such as Linear Regression, Decision Trees, Random Forest, or Neural Networks.\n\t* Split the training data into training and validation sets (e.g. 80% for training and 20% for validation).\n4. **Model Training**:\n\t* Train the chosen model on the training data using the selected features.\n\t* Tune hyperparameters using techniques such as grid search or random search to optimize the model\'s performance on the validation set.\n5. **Model Evaluation**:\n\t* Evaluate the performance of the trained model on the validation set using metrics such as Mean Absolute Error (MAE) or Mean Squared Error (MSE', token_ids=[8586, 596, 264, 4754, 12384, 369, 52997, 3838, 7729, 304, 264, 2728, 3363, 1473, 334, 29707, 8650, 62965, 41425, 57277, 334, 2566, 25, 57277, 9, 1595, 9103, 45722, 578, 3363, 369, 902, 584, 1390, 311, 7168, 3838, 7729, 198, 9, 1595, 20922, 45722, 362, 743, 315, 4519, 430, 7664, 279, 3838, 11, 2737, 512, 197, 10, 1595, 2470, 90179, 9949, 45722, 578, 1396, 315, 28689, 304, 279, 3838, 198, 197, 10, 1595, 2470, 890, 589, 9949, 45722, 578, 1396, 315, 40983, 304, 279, 3838, 198, 197, 10, 1595, 38576, 76859, 425, 45722, 578, 9518, 22609, 315, 279, 3838, 198, 197, 10, 1595, 425, 45722, 578, 4325, 315, 279, 3838, 304, 1667, 198, 197, 10, 1595, 2588, 45722, 578, 12818, 477, 10521, 2082, 315, 279, 3838, 198, 197, 10, 1595, 9233, 45722, 578, 3044, 315, 279, 3838, 320, 68, 1326, 13, 330, 19045, 498, 330, 42000, 498, 330, 5481, 269, 1158, 197, 10, 1595, 25807, 1385, 45722, 362, 11