Output~2025-04-07 00:34:20.771124: [RequestOutput(request_id=1315, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Historians have been debating the answer to this question - did the Wright Brothers really invent the first airplane? ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 22425, 5493, 617, 1027, 71513, 279, 4320, 311, 420, 3488, 482, 1550, 279, 27839, 34179, 2216, 17459, 279, 1176, 44024, 30, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="The Wright brothers, Orville and Wilbur Wright, are widely credited with inventing and building the world's first successful airplane and making the first controlled, powered, and sustained heavier-than-air human flight on December 17, 1903. On that day, they successfully flew their Wright Flyer at Kitty Hawk, North Carolina, with Orville piloting the first flight, which lasted for 12 seconds and covered a distance of 120 feet. Wilbur piloted the fourth and final flight of the day, which lasted for 59 seconds and covered a distance of 852 feet.\n\nHowever, some historians have questioned the Wright brothers' claim to being the first to invent the airplane, citing the work of other inventors and experimenters who were also working on similar projects around the same time. For example, Clément Ader, a French inventor, had built a steam-powered, bat-like aircraft called the Éole in the 1890s, which he claimed to have flown in 1890. Similarly, Otto Lilienthal, a German engineer, had built a series of gliders in the 1890s that were precursors to the modern airplane.\n\nDespite these challenges to their claim, the Wright brothers' achievement is widely recognized as a major milestone in aviation history. They designed, built, and tested the first powered, heavier-than-air aircraft that was capable of sustained flight, and their innovations in areas such as wing design, propulsion, and control systems paved the way for the development of modern air travel.\n\nIn conclusion, while there may be some debate about the extent to which the Wright brothers were the first to invent the airplane, their achievement is widely recognized as a major breakthrough in aviation history, and their innovations continue to influence the design and development of aircraft to this day.", token_ids=[791, 27839, 20820, 11, 2582, 8078, 323, 10785, 11490, 27839, 11, 527, 13882, 41857, 449, 17459, 287, 323, 4857, 279, 1917, 596, 1176, 6992, 44024, 323, 3339, 279, 1176, 14400, 11, 23134, 11, 323, 29759, 44922, 48754, 38635, 3823, 11213, 389, 6790, 220, 1114, 11, 220, 7028, 18, 13, 1952, 430, 1938, 11, 814, 7946, 32122, 872, 27839, 20793, 261, 520, 67281, 56423, 11, 4892, 13030, 11, 449, 2582, 8078, 11715, 11780, 279, 1176, 11213, 11, 902, 36513, 369, 220, 717, 6622, 323, 9960, 264, 6138, 315, 220, 4364, 7693, 13, 10785, 11490, 11715, 9437, 279, 11999, 323, 1620, 11213, 315, 279, 1938, 11, 902, 36513, 369, 220, 2946, 6622, 323, 9960, 264, 6138, 315, 220, 24571, 7693, 382, 11458, 11, 1063, 51801, 617, 29440, 279, 27839, 20820, 6, 3802, 311, 1694, 279, 1176, 311, 17459, 279, 44024, 11, 33264, 279, 990, 315, 1023, 17459, 1105, 323, 9526, 388, 889, 1051, 1101, 3318, 389, 4528, 7224, 2212, 279, 1890, 892, 13, 1789, 3187, 11, 2493, 42625, 362, 1126, 11, 264, 8753, 72001, 11, 1047, 5918, 264, 20930, 41503, 11, 16120, 12970, 14467, 2663, 279, 29124, 1286, 304, 279, 220, 9378, 15, 82, 11, 902, 568, 11922, 311, 617, 53850, 304, 220, 9378, 15, 13, 35339, 11, 66991, 41578, 1188, 12130, 11, 264, 6063, 24490, 11, 1047, 5918, 264, 4101, 315, 2840, 13572, 