different parts of the code.\n\t* Code should be easy to follow, with a clear flow of logic and minimal nesting.\n6. **Variable Declaration**:\n\t* Variables should be declared at the beginning of their scope, with clear and descriptive names.\n\t* Variables should be initialized with a clear and consistent initialization value.\n7. **Code Duplication**:\n\t* Code should be free from unnecessary duplication, with repeated logic or code sections avoided.\n\t* Code should be refactored to eliminate duplication and improve maintainability.\n8. **Error Handling**:\n\t* Error handling should be clear and consistent, with clear and descriptive error messages.\n\t* Error handling should be implemented in a way that is easy to understand and debug.\n9. **Code Style**:\n\t* Code should follow a consistent style guide, with consistent use of syntax, formatting, and naming conventions.\n\t* Code should be easy to read and understand, with a focus on clarity and simplicity.\n10. **Testing**:\n* Code should be thoroughly tested, with clear and descriptive test cases.\n* Code should be tested in a way that is easy to understand and debug.\n\nBy following these criteria, code can be made more readable, maintainable, and efficient, making it easier for developers to understand and work with the codebase.', token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 743, 315, 13186, 369, 2082, 92594, 1473, 334, 2123, 4557, 2968, 14577, 57277, 1271, 6106, 430, 2082, 374, 34898, 11, 433, 1288, 3449, 279, 2768, 13186, 1473, 16, 13, 3146, 15577, 18620, 97575, 1221, 31759, 334, 512, 197, 9, 12689, 5144, 1288, 387, 53944, 323, 1833, 264, 13263, 36048, 21977, 320, 68, 1326, 2637, 50252, 4301, 11, 53209, 45297, 11, 5099, 13, 4390, 197, 9, 5830, 323, 1749, 5144, 1288, 387, 53944, 323, 1833, 264, 13263, 36048, 21977, 627, 17, 13, 3146, 2123, 21021, 334, 512, 197, 9, 6247, 1288, 387, 17057, 1139, 20406, 14491, 477, 13761, 11, 449, 2867, 70552, 323, 6170, 311, 10552, 279, 7580, 315, 1855, 3857, 627, 197, 9, 24460, 323, 5528, 1