Output~2025-04-07 00:51:41.927630: [RequestOutput(request_id=1696, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Write a mystery story setting involving a sandstone quarry. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 9842, 264, 23347, 3446, 6376, 16239, 264, 9462, 11046, 37170, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text="The sun was setting over the vast expanse of the sandstone quarry, casting a golden glow over the rugged terrain. The air was thick with the sweet scent of wet earth and the distant rumble of machinery echoed through the valley. It was a place where time seemed to stand still, where the only sounds were the gentle hum of the wind and the occasional shout of a worker.\n\nBut amidst the tranquility, a sense of unease settled over the quarry like a shroud. It started with small things: a misplaced tool, a faint whisper in the darkness, a feeling of being watched. At first, no one paid much attention, chalking it up to the usual quirks of working in a remote location. But as the days passed, the occurrences grew more frequent and more intense.\n\nIt began with strange noises at night. The sound of footsteps crunching through the gravel, the creaking of rusty gates, the distant rumble of rocks tumbling down the quarry walls. The workers tried to brush it off as the wind or the settling of the earth, but deep down, they knew something was amiss.\n\nThen, the equipment started to malfunction. Machines would shut down for no reason, only to restart on their own. Tools would go missing, only to reappear in strange places. It was as if something was playing a twisted game of hide-and-seek, always staying one step ahead of the quarry's inhabitants.\n\nAs the tension mounted, the workers began to whisper among themselves about the legend of the quarry. A story of a long-forgotten miner who had died in the depths of the quarry, his spirit trapped between worlds, seeking revenge on the living. Some said he was a vengeful spirit, driven mad by the isolation and the darkness. Others claimed he was a guardian, watching over the quarry and its secrets.\n\nOne by one, the workers started to vanish. At first, it was just a rumor, a whispered tale of someone who had gone on a solo hike and never returned. But as the days passed, the disappearances became more frequent, and the quarry's inhabitants realized that something was very wrong.\n\nThe remaining workers banded together, determined to uncover the truth behind the strange occurrences. They scoured the quarry, searching for clues, but every lead ended in a dead end. It was as if the quarry itself was hiding its secrets, waiting for the perfect moment to strike.\n\nAnd then, one fateful night, the workers stumbled upon an ancient symbol etched into the sandstone wall", token_ids=[791, 7160, 574, 6376, 927, 279, 13057, 506, 95519, 315, 279, 9462, 11046, 37170, 11, 25146, 264, 21411, 37066, 927, 279, 55883, 25911, 13, 578, 3805, 574, 12314, 449, 279, 10437, 41466, 315, 14739, 9578, 323, 279, 29827, 14322, 901, 315, 26953, 55212, 1555, 279, 34681, 13, 1102, 574, 264, 2035, 1405, 892, 9508, 311, 2559, 2103, 11, 1405, 279, 1193, 10578, 1051, 279, 22443, 2854, 315, 279, 10160, 323, 279, 28961, 42223, 315, 264, 12128, 382, 4071, 65904, 279, 41664, 1429, 11, 264, 5647, 315, 6316, 521, 23183, 927, 279, 37170, 1093, 264, 559, 43376, 13, 1102, 3940, 449, 2678, 2574, 25, 264, 90660, 5507, 11, 264, 38678, 35955, 304, 279, 27394, 11, 264, 8430, 315, 1694, 15746, 13, 2468, 1176, 11, 912, 832, 7318, 