Output~2025-04-07 00:51:53.873736: [RequestOutput(request_id=1703, prompt="<|begin_of_text|><|start_header_id|>user<|end_header_id|>\n\n{'Below is an instruction that describes a task. Write a response that appropriately completes the request. ### Instruction: Identify two differences between a smartphone and a feature phone. ### Response:'}<|eot_id|><|start_header_id|>assistant<|end_header_id|>\n\n", prompt_token_ids=[128000, 128000, 128006, 882, 128007, 271, 13922, 39314, 374, 459, 7754, 430, 16964, 264, 3465, 13, 9842, 264, 2077, 430, 36001, 45695, 279, 1715, 13, 17010, 30151, 25, 65647, 1403, 12062, 1990, 264, 22234, 323, 264, 4668, 4641, 13, 17010, 6075, 4989, 92, 128009, 128006, 78191, 128007, 271], encoder_prompt=None, encoder_prompt_token_ids=None, prompt_logprobs=None, outputs=[CompletionOutput(index=0, text='Here is a response that completes the request:\n\nA smartphone and a feature phone are two types of mobile phones that differ in several ways. Two key differences between the two are:\n\n1. Operating System: A smartphone runs on a mobile operating system such as Android or iOS, which allows it to run third-party apps, access the internet, and perform various tasks. On the other hand, a feature phone typically runs on a proprietary operating system and is limited to making calls, sending texts, and playing games.\n2. Touchscreen: Smartphones have a touchscreen interface, which allows users to interact with the phone by tapping, swiping, and pinching their fingers on the screen. Feature phones, on the other hand, typically have a physical keypad and a small display screen that is used for displaying text messages, phone numbers, and other basic information.', token_ids=[8586, 374, 264, 2077, 430, 45695, 279, 1715, 1473, 32, 22234, 323, 264, 4668, 4641, 527, 1403, 4595, 315, 6505, 18084, 430, 1782, 304, 3892, 5627, 13, 9220, 1401, 12062, 1990, 279, 1403, 527, 1473, 16, 13, 36233, 744, 25, 362, 22234, 8640, 389, 264, 6505, 10565, 1887, 1778, 439, 8682, 477